The Ministry of Foreign Affairs presents the results of the 12th Meeting of the Ministers of Foreign Affairs of Mekong-Kongke Cooperation (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Dr. Sok Siphana, Senior Advisor to the Royal Government of Cambodia, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and Cooperation International leaders lead a Cambodian delegation to the 12th Mekong-Ganges Cooperation Foreign Ministers' Meeting in Bangkok, Thailand on July 16, 2023.
According to a press release issued by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Fresh News praised the contribution of Mekong-Mekong cooperation in promoting socio-economic development in Mekong member countries. Cambodia, Laos, Myanmar and Vietnam have welcomed India's assistance through the implementation of their soon-to-be-implemented projects and noted that 78 projects have been completed since its inception in 2015.
Dr. Sok Siphana emphasized the importance of the India-Myanmar-Thailand Trilateral Expressway, a major infrastructure project to boost economic and cultural ties between India and the Mekong countries, and praised the commitment of India for expanding eastern connectivity to Cambodia, Laos and Vietnam.
The construction of the expressway is also linked to the 2025 ASEAN Connectivity Master Plan and India's Eastward Policy, both of which aim to improve connectivity. Local. He pointed out that the future direction of Mekong-Mekong cooperation should focus on digital revolution, green revolution and economic, trade and investment cooperation.
The meeting adopted the Joint Statement of the 12th Mekong-Ganges Foreign Ministers' Meeting, attached to two annexes, including: Concepts on Country-Sector Mechanisms and the Mekong-Ganges Cooperation Business Council.
