Cambodian Aquaculture Association asks China to co-invest and provide breeding techniques for aquaculture products for export to China
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Fishermen's Association has requested the Chinese side to invest and provide technical training on aquaculture products for export to China through the "Fish and Rice" corridor agreement, as China is in demand for these products.
He pointed out that the Chinese side has expressed demand for 12 aquaculture products, both freshwater and saltwater products, including freshwater prawns, lobsters, eels, shrimps, snails and other sea fish. And those products must be of standard and quality.
However, Cambodia has not yet been able to supply these priority products that the Chinese side needs, as many Cambodian hydropower companies have not been able to raise these products on a small scale, while breeding techniques are still limited. That requires technical experts to train more.
He said that the Chinese side will discuss the proposal with state-owned companies in China. The Entrepreneurship Development Fund, a state institution that supports the export of these products, will raise the issue with the Fisheries Administration to find out if Cambodia can raise these products, especially in the Special Economic Zone. There are four provinces in the northwest, including Pursat, Battambang, Banteay Meanchey and Pailin.
Please be informed that during the visit of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia to China in February 2023, the Government of Cambodia and China have launched a new cooperation called "Diamond" cooperation. Under the "Diamond" cooperation, Cambodia and China have agreed to develop a cooperation framework focusing on five areas: politics, production, agriculture, energy and security.
