(Phnom Penh): A Singaporean agricultural company that is investing in growing cassava and processing it for export has announced that it is looking for participants to grow cassava on its land in Oral district, Kampong Speu province to meet the demand for cassava production. Its market is growing rapidly.
Ms. Long Taifa, Plant Manager of HLH, said that the company's cassava flour is in high demand after being in business for many years. According to Taipei, despite the global crisis of Kovid 19 or other global problems, cassava flour orders have not declined and are on the rise.
Ms. Long Taifa said that the company currently supplies cassava flour to the Netherlands, the United States, Korea and Japan in the amount of about 3,000 to 5,000 tons per month.
In addition to the supply of cassava flour, HLH also supplies about 5,000 to 7,000 tons of dried cassava to China. At the same time, companies from the country need up to 30,000 to 50,000 tons per month, but the company has not yet been able to supply.
In response to today's high-growth market demand, HLH has launched a new strategy to increase crop production, opening up opportunities for potential investors to invest in cassava cultivation on government-licensed land.
Through this new strategy, the company allows resourceful people to access cassava cultivation on its land, providing the company with planting techniques and varieties, and at harvest time the company is the buyer.
Through this strategy, it is an opportunity for those who want to profit from growing cassava. Ms. Long Taifa confirmed that the cultivation of the company's land is the team provides land, seeds, provide free technical advice, and when the harvest is not worried about no place to sell, the company makes a collection contract. Buy potato tubers at a reasonable market price when planting.
In addition to the guarantees on the market, the cultivation of potatoes on the company's land is a company that helps find machinery to find labor for planting and harvesting, if you go there without machinery or manpower. Labor. But the cost of machinery or labor is paid by the grower.
Currently, there are people coming to cultivate on this land gradually, and there are both Cambodians and foreigners. Mr. Womo, a Cambodian, and Mr. Lasman, a Sri Lankan, are growing cassava on the company's land.
They claimed that the land at the site was good for cassava and that cultivation was much easier.
The story that led Mr. Womo and Mr. Lasman to come and cultivate in the above location because the land provider provides free seed. The best thing is that after the harvest is not worried or difficult to find a market to sell potatoes, but to transport the company's processing plant in that location.
Mr. Womo and Mr. Lasman encouraged the wealthy to invest in growing potatoes on the company's land for profit.
Please note that for the above land location, HLH also announced to welcome lovers in the field of agriculture can participate in planting other crops or raising animals.
