As for the price of clean water, a large number of people may not be aware that the water they are using every day is cheaper than the cost of producing clean water. But this is true, consumers of 0-7 cubic meters, the price of water must be set to sell below the cost so that people can use clean water at a lower price, with the Royal Government as a subsidy (replacement fee).
The price of clean water is not the same, it varies depending on the region or situation of production. In Phnom Penh, the cost of producing clean water per cubic meter is 1,280 riels per cubic meter.
