ASEAN Approaches Japan to Become a Strategic Partner (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Kong Phok, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and ASEAN Senior Minister of Cambodia, said that ASEAN is closer to Japan becoming a Strategic Partner. That is, if nothing changes, the announcement will be made in September 2023.
Kong Phok made the remarks while making a report at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs on the morning of July 17, 2023 on the results of Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon's participation in the 56th ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting. Relevant meeting held in Jakarta, Republic of Indonesia.
"We agreed and announced the establishment of a comprehensive strategic partnership between ASEAN and Japan on the occasion of the 26th ASEAN-Japan Meeting in September," he said.
Since then, significant progress has been made in all areas, including political security, economic, financial and socio-cultural cooperation.
Japan joined the Treaty of Amity and Cooperation in Southeast Asia (TAC) in July 2004 and became a dialogue partner, appointing its ambassador to ASEAN at the ASEAN Secretariat in Jakarta. The Japan Mission to ASEAN was established on May 26, 2011.
The United States and India will become all-round strategic partners of ASEAN in 2022. This was stated by Mr. Kong Phok in a press conference showing the possibility of the 40th and 41st ASEAN Summits and related summits hosted by Cambodia.
Cambodia's Efforts and Progress in the Field of Human Rights highlighted at the Human Rights Council
(Geneva) - The Human Rights Council concluded its 53rd session on July 14, 2023, after convening a total of 38 meetings and approving a total of 30 resolutions on specific topics and countries.
The Cambodian delegation also participated in discussions on strengthening the work of the Office of the High Commissioner for Human Rights and the Human Rights Council, as well as topics on the human rights situation in some countries.
The following is an excerpt from the Cambodian intervention:
* Cambodia's poverty rate has halved to 16 percent today. To strengthen local resilience in the aftermath of the epidemic and the global economic downturn, the Royal Government of Cambodia has so far launched a number of support projects, including cash assistance programs for poor and vulnerable households. Tax exemptions for affected sectors and cash subsidies for suspended workers.
* To protect and promote the rights of migrants, policies, programs and strategic plans have been put in place at both the national and sub-national levels. Cambodia has signed a memorandum of understanding with the host country to ensure that the rights of Cambodian workers abroad are protected and promoted.
Pretending to be independent or affiliated with any political party is not a license to violate the law with impunity. To regard law enforcement as a restriction on the freedom of any group is to undermine the rule of law and equal treatment for all citizens.
* In the absence of two or three politicians or political parties who have violated the law or have been banned from politics for violating the law, Cambodia is committed to holding free, fair and just July elections. Be transparent and fully reflect the will of the people.
* Cooperation is a mutual process. For real results, UN human rights bodies and mechanisms, including the Office of the High Commissioner for Human Rights, need to work fairly and politically, in accordance with the principles of universal, neutral, fair and non-partisan principles, as well as a genuine dialogue. Definitely constructive based on verified sources.
* Technical assistance and effective cooperation programs need to be made at the request, in consultation with and with the full consent of the state, as well as in line with national priorities and recommendations from the Universal Periodic Review (UPR). Take. The primary role of the state as a human rights envoy should be respected in this process.
In a conference room in Beijing on Monday morning, Xi said the two climate envoys could play a role in improving US-China relations. The meeting earlier this week, which continues until Wednesday, is expected to focus on the elimination of methane and other non-carbon emissions and will continue until the global climate talks.
Kerry said it was imperative that China and the United States make concrete progress four months before the COP28 global climate talks to be held in Dubai, United Arab Emirates. Kerry also called on China to partner with the United States to reduce methane emissions and reduce the climate impact of coal power.
Climate talks between the two countries, the world's largest emitters of greenhouse gases, have been suspended following a visit by former US House of Representatives Speaker Nancy Pelosi to Taiwan. It is Kerry's third visit to China as a US envoy and the resumption of the two countries' climate diplomacy.
