Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan donates alms to 20 pagodas in Serei Sophorn
(Banteay Meanchey Province): In the afternoon of July 16, 2023, Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan, Member of National Assembly, Chairman of the National Authority for Combating Drugs and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group visited Banteay Meanchey Province and Mrs. Mao Malay presented gifts to monks. Waiting for the rain at 20 pagodas in Serei Sophorn.
The ceremony was held at Wat Kiri Chum Chamkar Khnor in Sangkat O'Ambel, Serey Sophorn City, Banteay Meanchey Province, with the participation of representatives from all levels.
It should be noted that the Vesa festival is an important festival in Buddhism, an important time for monks and nuns to learn the Dharma and discipline consistently according to the Buddha's teachings.
People who believe in Buddhism often celebrate the festival by bringing rice, drinks and other items to the monks as much as possible.
Monks are required to stay at the pagoda for three months during the rainy season and are not allowed to travel long distances during the day unless they have important duties, such as their parents who are seriously ill or determined to perform dharma. Return within 7 days. This festival starts from the 1st day of the month of Assad to the 15th day of the month of Assoch.
