(Phnom Penh): Cambodian businessmen and economists have suggested that the establishment of a riel and yuan payment system between Cambodia and China via QR Code will make it easier to trade goods and create additional payment options.
Oknha Lim Heng, vice president of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, told Fresh News that the development of multiple payment methods is a good thing for the convenience of citizens as well as business people and investors. Payment will be easier for Cambodia and the import and export of various goods and also attract more foreign investors.
"Traders, investors, traders are happy and supportive if there are ways to pay with multiple currencies, it will be easier as well as provide more options for payment and exchange of goods with other countries," he said. "Obviously, in the ASEAN Summit, which Indonesia has chaired in the past, also mentioned the means of settlement in the ASEAN region in the use of their respective currencies."
She stated that for cross-border electronic payments, this really benefits the promotion of the use of the riel in Cambodia, because this cooperation requires a riel account, which means that Chinese tourists can pay to Cambodian traders can only have a Cambodian riel account.
Dr. Hong Vannak, an economist at the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that QR Code payments are a means or mechanism to facilitate investors and tourists to use QR Code payments, which is more convenient for trading. Investment and spending of tourists without having to go to the bank or exchange office as before.
At the same time, as payments between Cambodia and China are denominated in riel and yuan, the use of the dollar may be reduced, making the dollar less stressful for Cambodian trade and commerce. China and other countries that have an agreement to use the QR Code system.
However, Cambodia may need a large amount of money depending on the size of the transaction for payment with China, because in the past, most of Cambodia used the dollar as the basis of payment with China. In this case, Cambodia may need to throw more money into the economy.
Currently, Cambodia has also successfully cooperated with Thailand, both in Thailand and in Cambodia, Cambodia will continue to cooperate with Laos, China, India and Vietnam.
She stated that this electronic cross-border payment really benefits the promotion of the use of the riel in Cambodia, because this collaboration requires a riel account, which means that Chinese tourists can pay to Cambodian traders can only have a Cambodian riel account.
This cooperation has made it easier for Chinese tourists to come to Cambodia without having to withdraw the yuan into riel or the dollar to spend in Cambodia. In addition, it has made it easier for both Cambodians and Chinese tourists. And to boost the spending of Chinese tourists in Cambodia, because spending in Cambodia is as easy and safe as spending in their own country.
Currently, Cambodia has also successfully cooperated with Thailand, both in Thailand and in Cambodia, and Cambodia will continue to cooperate with Laos, China, India and Vietnam.
