Khmer Civilization Expert: How do people who go to the polls reflect their will?
(Phnom Penh): In a free society, when it comes to multi-party liberal democracy, where every citizen has to go to the polls every five years, it will be closer on July 23, 2023, because the country is peaceful and This progress is really the most important reflection of its will.
How do people go to the polls to reflect their will?
Therefore, the multi-party liberal democracy in Cambodia, in which the people go to the polls to elect their leaders in the future, is no different from the nations of the world, reflecting their will as follows:
First, give a positive signal to the public, we go to the polls, make sense of our good relations with like-minded people, and give a positive public signal of honesty in caring for our neighbors, our region. And our precious society.
Second, to promote the culture of democracy, we go to the polls as a sign that we are citizens of a democratic culture, because it is a powerful opportunity to connect with the people around us to contribute to the support and encouragement of outstanding dignitaries. Ideas to serve the nation, the motherland and the real people.
Thirdly, to value ourselves, we go to the polls to value ourselves, because the exercise of the spirit of the Constitution on the right to freedom of expression is the most valuable right in Cambodian culture from the beginning.
Therefore, for the Cambodian people to go to the polls, it is really important for the nation and for themselves to reflect and value themselves as citizens who want to live in a democratic society, want the country to have peace and development.
