Koh Sdach development attracts tourism
(Koh Kong): Mr. Toun Ooty, Deputy Governor of Kirisakor District, said that the current Koh Sdach commune is prosperous, which makes a commune Koh Sdach has developed tourism, which has the support of national and international tourists who come to visit the resort. In this commune of Koh Sdach.
The Deputy Governor continued that for construction, there are three factors: the first factor is the development of the country, the second factor is the geography of the people living in the district, and the third factor is the flow of tourists to visit a lot. Therefore, investors or citizens can afford to build resorts or renovate homes.
People live on King Island, they have lived since the French era and during the 1980s and are engaged in fishing and trading from the sea.
For compensation on the water, the district authorities and officials are now focusing on monitoring illegal construction sites.
However, it is understandable for people who want to repair their houses to be made of solid concrete to protect their safety, they are afraid of collapsing into the water during a rainstorm, it can be a high risk to their lives, and the authorities have tied In some cases, the Royal Government needs to develop in the future.
He said that the fishing output has decreased significantly, forcing some people to turn to guesthouses or buy boats to transport tourists to visit the islands instead of fishing or buying fish for sale. In the market as before.
Authorities often inspect illegal constructions that affect natural resources, biodiversity, or navigation routes. In particular, people can build only on the old location, living can not be expanded new absolutely.
In the past, Kirisakor district authorities and professional officers also inspected and stopped many unauthorized construction sites when they were found to be in violation of technical standards or serious violations into the sea.
Mr. Meng Phalla emphasized that making water pillars in water is easy to rot and spend a lot of money to repair every year, so buy concrete pipes to make pillars instead of wood, it is strong for many years, this is a necessity almost When living on the water in Koh Sdach commune, it is not a violation of the state's water surface, it is just wanting a strong house that is good for living and earning a living.
He stated that in the future, if the Royal Government plans to develop anything, they are willing to follow the plan if necessary. Because the authorities do not allow the construction of a standard document with seafood as state property.
