Citizens who have disputes and issues related to real estate transactions can file a complaint or request for intervention from the real estate regulator.
The Real Estate and Mortgage Regulator is the only institution that has the role and duty to manage and control all activities related to the real estate development business, receive complaints or applications for intervention to mediate and mediate disputes and investigate, research and prevent all crimes. Involved in any form of real estate development business, with or without a license.
In this regard, the Real Estate and Mortgage Regulators would like to inform the public that in case of any dispute or irregularity related to the sale, purchase or lease of real estate, any party to the contract or any relevant party may file a complaint or request. Intervention to the NCDD Address: Building 168F (7th floor), Street 598, Sangkat Chrang Chamre 1, Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh, or contact by telegram number 011 598 372 and 069 517 186.
