The following is a statement from the Phnom Penh Municipal Administration: Commentary: Crimes committed by the United States in Laos in the past should not be replicated in the Ukraine crisis.
It should be noted that during the Vietnam War from 1964 to 1973, the United States dropped several cluster munitions on southern Vietnam and eastern Laos and Cambodia. Laos is one of the countries most affected by cluster munitions.
On the issue of cluster munitions, the American attitude is different. In 2008, the US government pledged to ensure that US troops no longer use cluster munitions and "shut down and stockpile" all cluster munitions. Currently, the ammunition supplied to Ukraine is a cluster munition made more than 40 years ago and "closed and stockpiled" 15 years ago.
The opposite is true: a year ago, then-White House Press Secretary Jen Psaki said that using cluster munitions would be a war crime. A year later, the United States became the target of its condemnation. In the face of American self-interest, what is the value of virtue and shame?
