International Energy Agency cuts global oil demand outlook for 2023
Global oil consumption will increase by 2.2 million barrels per day, or about 2%, by 2023, Bloomberg reported, citing a report released by the Paris-based IEA on Thursday. That's down from about 220,000 barrels last month. However, demand is still on track for the highest level this year, with significant oil spills in the second half of this year.
"Global oil demand is under pressure from a challenging economic environment, especially due to the tightening of monetary policy," the IEA said. "Demand in OECD member countries, and especially in Europe, is declining at a time of declining industrial activity," the IEA added.
