ASEAN foreign ministers reaffirm the need for a five-point peace plan for the crisis in Myanmar (Video inside) (Jakarta): ASEAN foreign ministers reaffirm their position That the five-point peace plan remains the main principle in resolving the ongoing political crisis in Myanmar. This was released by the AFP news agency on Friday, July 14, 2023.
In a joint statement issued on Thursday night, the ASEAN diplomats also condemned the ongoing violence in Myanmar, including airstrikes, artillery shelling and shelling. Destroy public infrastructure.
"The Foreign Ministers called on all parties concerned to take concrete action to immediately end all forms of violence and to condemn all acts that lead to escalation of violence," the statement said. The ASEAN Foreign Ministers also stressed the need to create a conducive environment for humanitarian assistance and the establishment of a comprehensive national dialogue.
Myanmar, a member of ASEAN, has been embroiled in violence since early 2021, and ASEAN has launched a five-point peace plan, including a call for an immediate end to all hostilities. All forms of violence and constructive dialogue between stakeholders to resolve the current conflict, but to no avail.
