(Pursat): O'Som is a commune in Veal Veng District, Pursat Province. O'Som is located on a high ridge, which is highly conducive for nature tourism and for various crops as well.
In the past, O'Som commune, although located on a ridge and has no access road, has been inhabited by indigenous peoples for a long time. Later, because the land in that area was highly suitable for plantation, people from other areas migrated to live in that area.
The livelihood of the people on the ridge in O'Som commune is very difficult because there are no roads to travel, no water supply, no electricity, no schools, health centers and other living infrastructure.
Mr. Sok Boeun, 74 years old, is a Chuong resident who has been living in Osom since he was born. Mr. Sok Boeun reminded that living in Osom in the past was very difficult because there was no way to travel to other areas.
Ms. Ly Davy is a resident of Kampong Cham Province. After her husband was from Pursat province, she also moved to O'Som commune. Ms. Davy has been living in O'Som commune for more than 10 years. The hardships of Ms. Davy and her family are not different from the families of other people in O'Som commune. The big problem for daily life more than 10 years ago was the lack of roads. Want to go down from the mountain to Veal Veng district town or to Pursat province takes days.
Ms. Nhem Khatna is from Battambang province but has been living in O'Som commune for more than 10 years. She also has difficulty finding a way to travel like other people in O'Som commune. Roads also lead to livelihood problems and hinder the importation of agricultural products to the market.
Road construction is a priority policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Roads not only help integrate people from one area to another, but roads are the lifeblood of the national economy and the economy of the Cambodian family.
Based on this realistic policy, the Royal Government of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) has worked hard to build interconnected roads from the capital to the provinces and from each provincial town to remote rural areas. For Pursat Province, after National Road No. 55 connects National Road No. 5 in Pursat town to the mountainous area of Veal Veng district until the Thai border is completed, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also started construction of National Road No. 10 Another line.
Samdech Techo Prime Minister announced the opening of the construction site of National Road No. 10 at the same time as the inauguration of National Road No. 55, on March 9, 2020.
National Road No. 10 is nearly 200 kilometers long, connecting from Samlot District, Battambang Province, connecting to National Road No. 55 in Pramoy Commune and up to O'Som Commune, then connecting to Koh Kong Province. The road is planned to cost nearly $ 200 million in loans from the Chinese government.
After more than three years of construction, National Road 10 is about 60 percent complete. Although National Road No. 10 is not 100% completed, it is now possible to travel to the beautiful eco-tourism area of O'Som commune without any difficulty.
The Royal Government and the Cambodian people have a slogan: "There is a way, there is hope." National Road 10 is changing the lives of the people of O'Som commune to be beautiful and full of smiles. In particular, solved the difficulties of their journey.
This achievement of National Road No. 10 not only brings fun for the people of O'Som commune to travel. But it also brought hope for their farm. They are no longer worried about transporting agricultural products to the market as before.
O'Som commune is located on a high ridge, which is accompanied by mountain ranges, forests and waterfalls, etc. It is highly favorable for tourists who want to connect life with nature. Natural concessions for relaxation, along with the achievements of National Road 10, have enthused tourists from all over to O'Som and no longer calm O'Som as before.
Attracting tourists and facilitating the finding of markets for agricultural products after National Road 10 also helped to improve the lives of the people in O'Som commune.
O'Som commune is not only prosperous with National Road No. 10, but by making O'Som more beautiful, the authorities have also installed electricity, water supply system and other infrastructure such as concrete road to facilitate Live of the people and provide accommodation to tourists.
