(Jakarta, Indonesia): On Thursday, July 13, 2023, in Jakarta, Republic of Indonesia, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Secretary-General of ASEAN, attended the Foreign Ministers' Meeting with India. The meeting reaffirmed the commitment of ASEAN and India to further strengthen future ties.
Afterwards, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Secretary-General of ASEAN, was invited to attend the ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting with China. The meeting reviewed the progress of ASEAN-China cooperation and discussed future directions, especially to strengthen the ASEAN-China Comprehensive Strategic Partnership through the implementation of the Action Plan and Annex. The meeting also exchanged views on regional and international issues of common interest and concern.
In the afternoon of the same day, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn attended the ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting with the European Union. The meeting called for the effective implementation of the Action Plan for the Implementation of the ASEAN-EU Strategic Partnership 2023-2027 and exchanged views on ways to strengthen cooperation in areas of common interest and discussed regional issues. And international.
Dr. Kao Kim Hourn also attended the ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting with Canada. The meeting welcomed the progress of ASEAN-Canada cooperation and looked forward to upgrading ASEAN-Canada relations to a strategic partnership in September.
On Thursday evening, the ASEAN Secretary-General met with Canadian Foreign Minister Mélanie Joly. On that occasion, both sides look forward to hosting the ASEAN-Canada Summit to launch the ASEAN-Canada Strategic Partnership on the occasion of the 43rd ASEAN Summit and related summits in September.
