According to the president of the Cashew Association, the price of raw cashew nuts sold by farmers in the past was 5,500 riel to 6,500 riel, depending on the quality of the seeds, and he expects that during August and September, the price of raw cashew nuts will increase to 6,800 riel. Riel.
However, he said that the data on cashew exports may exceed the figures recorded by the Ministry of Agriculture, as some exports to neighboring countries are made informally through the corridors to Vietnam and some Thailand without. No request for phytosanitary certificate from the Ministry.
The president of the Cambodian Cashew Association hopes that by 2024, the two state-owned banks will release more capital to producers and processors in Cambodia so that they will be able to collect more raw materials from farmers and process the finished product for export. Value added as a contribution to the cashew industry.
He said that through the signing of a memorandum of understanding between the Cambodian Cashew Association and the SME Bank in early June, the state bank offered a special interest rate of 5.5% for producers and processors in the cashew sector and 5% for entrepreneurs. Women, which is a good level of interest for cashew processing enterprises to encourage them to have enough capital to buy from farmers and be able to compete with neighboring countries.
He added that the signing of the understanding is part of solving the challenges in the cashew production chain, as well as helping to improve the cashew processing industry in Cambodia to another level.
