China was the first superpower to voluntarily sign the SEANWFZ protocol. This was confirmed by Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia in a press release from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.
The Deputy Prime Minister also reaffirmed Cambodia's support for China's willingness to sign the protocol first without a "reserve" and, as requested by the ASEAN chair, the signing of the protocol could Held during the 43rd ASEAN Summit and related summits in September this year.
The treaty is known as the Bangkok Treaty. Through it, ASEAN reaffirms the importance of the Non-Proliferation Treaty (NPT) in preventing nuclear proliferation and Contribute to international peace and security.
