(Phnom Penh): On July 10, 2023, for the third time, nearly 500,000 identified Cambodian families received a subsidy from the Royal Government from the cash subsidy program for vulnerable families during There is inflationary pressure.
The Cash Support Program for Vulnerable Families During Inflation Pressure is another national social protection program to help protect vulnerable households during inflationary pressures after the global economy, including Cambodia, was affected by the spread of Kovid 19, geopolitical issues, and the war between Russia and Ukraine, which pushed up market prices.
This cash support program was announced by the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen on December 3, 2022 in order to alleviate the living burden of the people not to fall into poverty and as part of building Social resilience to another level.
Residing in Sangkat Phsar Thmei II, Khan Daun Penh, who currently lives with four members in charge of Ms. Sun Duong Dara, she received an allowance of 180,000 Riels at a time after she was evaluated by the Sangkat authorities to receive a cash subsidy program. Families are at risk during inflationary pressures to pay for basic necessities such as rice, medicine and grandchildren.
In her old age and in charge of raising a child and two grandchildren, Ms. Duong Dara requested the authorities to inspect and assess her family situation again to obtain an equity or poor card to be able to receive subsidies from the Royal Government and Go to the hospital for free while she is also sick on a regular basis.
The 52-year-old Ly Naisim, who has just returned from a third paycheck from a cash-strapped program for vulnerable families during the inflationary pressures, said the money has partially helped her livelihood. Pay for food and pay for grandchildren.
After the 19 epidemic of Kovid and the economic impact, Sam Sopheap's family of nine was struggling to make ends meet, as daily vegetable sales were less frequent. Fortunately, her family was identified by Phsar Thmei II authorities to receive cash from a cash-strapped program for vulnerable families during inflationary pressures.
With more than one family member at a time, the 62-year-old woman's family received an allowance of 310,000 riels.
The Cash Support Program for Vulnerable Families during Inflation Pressure is supported three times, the first: on December 10, 2022, the second: on April 10, 2023 and The third time: on July 10, 2023.
Dr. John Narith, Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Secretary General of the National Council for Social Protection, said that the Royal Government has spent more than $ 40 million on this subsidy. The third is $ 17 million.
