North Korea on Tuesday condemns US President Joe Biden's decision to send a cluster munition to Ukraine To go to Ukraine as a crime and demanded that Washington cancel the plan immediately. This was released by the AFP news agency on Wednesday, July 12, 2023.
"On behalf of the North Korean government, I strongly condemn the United States' decision to supply this deadly weapon to Ukraine, calling it a crime and demanding that the United States withdraw its sanctions," Cho said. "Make your decision immediately."
Last week, Washington announced it would send cluster munitions to Ukraine as part of a new $ 800 million security aid package. The weapon is controversial because of the serious risks it poses to civilians, even long after the fighting has ended.
Many US allies and partners supporting Russia in Russia's war of aggression are among the 111 countries that are parties to the Convention on the Prohibition of Cluster Munitions. The Convention prohibits the use, stockpiling, production and transfer of all types of cluster munitions and entered into force in 2010. North Korea is not a party to the convention, and Russia, Ukraine and the United States have not yet signed it.
