National Police Continues Fire Drills at Aeon Mall 1 to Increase Awareness of First Aid and Evacuation
(Phnom Penh): The Fire Prevention and Rescue Police Department of the National Police General Commission this morning, July 12, 2023, continued to cooperate with Aeon Mall 1 to launch firefighting and rescue exercises. In addition to the professional police officers of the department, there are also many employees of Aeon Mall 1.
Lt. Gen. Neth Vantha, director of the Fire Prevention and Rescue Police Department, who personally led the exercise, said that the current exercise is to make the staff in Aeon Mall 1 know the basic fire prevention and extinguishing measures. Self and evacuate with guests from the scene as well as connect with the expertise of the authorities.
Exercises on that occasion include:
* First: Emergency evacuation * Second: Rescue of victims * Third: Fire.
Through this exercise, the director of the department saw that the operation of staff and professional officers is carried out equally well and have clear skills, so he expects that in case of an emergency, the staff in this Japanese supermarket can be rescued. Initiate yourself with your guests, and in small cases manageable and widespread.
In addition, Lt. Gen. Neth Vantha suggested to the owners of supermarkets, enterprises, establishments and large buildings, etc., should increase cooperation with law enforcement forces, fire prevention and fighting skills, especially joint exercises to increase awareness. From to its staff about first aid measures, use of firefighting equipment and evacuation from the scene.
Chou Sovannara, General Manager of Aeon Mall, said that in addition to raising awareness among staff working in the market, another goal is to comply with Cambodian law and other legal documents in force to prevent and Prevent potential fires. Another is to increase the confidence of customers who come to Aeon Mall directly.
At the same time, Mr. Chou Sovannara, on behalf of Aeon Mall, expressed his deep gratitude to the National Police General Commission for its regular training and promotion, as well as cooperation with Aeon Mall in conducting important fire drills at this time. . He expects that after the training, the market staff will be more aware of the measures to prevent and extinguish the fire.
In the first half of 2023, there were 516 fires, an increase of 144 compared to the same period in 2022, resulting in 41 deaths, according to Lt. Gen. Neth Vatta. The number increased to 29 and caused many other property damage. The cause of the fire was caused by electric shock, power consumption and other factors.
In addition, Lt. Gen. Neth Vatta outlined the department's various rules for fire prevention and called on residents to know how to put out the fire first when contacting the department at 117 toll free. 24 hours a week. Samdech Techo Hun Sen's call for US and Ukrainian presidents not to use cluster munitions has been widely reported on TikTok in China.
(Phnom Penh): The words of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the head of the Supreme Government of Cambodia, calling on the President of the United States and the President of Ukraine not to use cluster munitions are becoming very popular in China, with many media outlets broadcasting on China's TikTok.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's call was made on July 9, 2023, after reports that the United States would supply cluster munitions to Ukraine to fight the Russian army. At the same time, Samdech Techo's speech was widely disseminated by the Chinese media, more than 20 units, both large and small.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's appeal message reads as follows:
In recent days, there have been widespread reports that the United States will supply cluster munitions to Ukraine to fight Russian troops. If this is true, it could be the greatest danger to the Ukrainian people for decades or even hundreds of years if the cluster munitions were used in Russian-occupied territory.
The tragic experience of Cambodia, which received the US bombing in the early 1970s for more than half a century, has yet to find a way to eradicate it.
I know for sure that Cambodia is small and weak, soundless, but out of compassion for the people of Ukraine, I call on the President of the United States, the donor, and the President of Ukraine, the recipient, to refrain from using cluster munitions in this war, because the real victims are The special population is Ukraine.
According to a Reuters report released on Friday, July 7, 2023, the United States plans to send "cluster munitions" to Ukraine for use in the fight against Russian aggression. Despite opposition from human rights groups, such weapons could add energy to Kiev's offensive operations.
Chinese media report on cluster munitions in Ukraine
