Nine dead after boat capsizes in northern Uganda
Uganda: At least nine people have been killed after their boat capsized in the Nile River in the northern Apac district, police said on Tuesday. Of Uganda. This is according to the release by the Xinhua news agency on Tuesday, July 11, 2023.
An Ugandan police spokesman said the boat capsized at 4 a.m. local time when 13 workers decided to board a small boat to travel from the Congo port to Masindi port after their ferry. Every trip stopped at that time. Of the 13 people, nine died and four were hospitalized.
The catastrophic incident comes just one week after two separate incidents in Lake Victoria killed at least six people. Boat accidents are common in the lakes and rivers of East Africa due to overloading and bad weather.
