At the same time, Colonel Pok Sang, Deputy Commander of the Kandal Provincial Gendarmerie, claimed that donating blood did not harm his health, but only made him physically and mentally healthy. Personally, I have donated blood 13 times and I ask you to donate blood to save lives.
On this occasion, Dr. Sok Po, President of the National Blood Transfusion Center, called for blood donation, while 6 minutes need one block of blood to save lives, and it is necessary to need 160,000 blocks of blood per year to meet this blood demand. Donating blood does not affect health, and blood has only one source: people do not have a pharmaceutical factory, and do not wait until the time when we want to donate blood is too late.
