Below is a video of a former activist of the Anti-Candlelight Party in Kampong Thom Province: ASEAN Secretary-General Dr. Kao Kim Hourn attends six important meetings related to the ASEAN region in Jakarta
On the morning of July 11, 2023, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Secretary-General of ASEAN, attended six important meetings related to the ASEAN region in Jakarta, Indonesia.
In the first meeting, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn attended the meeting of the Commission on the Non-Proliferation of Nuclear Weapons in Southeast Asia.
On that occasion, the ASEAN Secretary-General briefed the Commission on the review of progress in the implementation of the Action Plan to Strengthen the Implementation of the Nuclear Non-Proliferation Treaty of Southeast Asia from 2023 to 2027. The meeting also discussed further directions for accession to the protocol of the Nuclear Non-Proliferation Treaty of the nuclear-armed countries.
Earlier in the day, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn attended a meeting between the ASEAN Foreign Ministers and the ASEAN Intergovernmental Commission on Human Rights (AICHR).
The ASEAN Foreign Ministers reaffirmed their support for the AICHR's efforts to promote and protect human rights in the region. The AICHR also issued a statement and submitted the 2023 Annual Report to the 56th ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting.
Next, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn continued to attend the 56th ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting. The meeting discussed the progress of ASEAN community building, the state of ASEAN external relations, as well as some of the urgent issues facing the region.
On that occasion, the two sides discussed ways to boost ASEAN community building efforts to strengthen the ASEAN Middle East and ASEAN solidarity as regional architecture evolves.
On that occasion, the ASEAN Secretary-General highlighted Brunei's significant contribution to ensuring that ASEAN remains a people-centered and people-centered community, including through initiatives such as the ASEAN Youth Scholarship Program and Bandar Seri Begawan Declaration on Strategic and Comprehensive Initiative to Link ASEAN Disaster Response and Emergency Response (ASEAN SHIELD).
