Malaysian government intends to rehabilitate high-speed rail line (Video inside) (KUALA LUMPUR): Malaysia is seeking proposals from private companies to develop a high-speed rail line between Kuala Lumpur and Singapore that will cost the railway project thousands of dollars. Millions of dollars that were canceled more than two years ago resurrected. According to Reuters.
Malaysia and Singapore in 2021 canceled their plans to build 350 km of railways after the two countries failed to agree on several proposals for modifications to the project.
Companies from China, Japan, South Korea and Europe have expressed interest in construction contracts, operations and financing of the railway and its assets.
MyHSR Corp., a Malaysian government entity responsible for the railway project, has called on the private sector to submit proposals to develop and operate the project through Reuters, Reuters reported on Tuesday. As a public and private partner.
"(This process) is a government initiative to revitalize the project through funding mechanisms and new implementation models in an effort to further improve infrastructure," MyHSR said. "Rail transport and to boost the national economy."
Singapore's Ministry of Transport did not immediately respond to a request for comment from Reuters.
Last year, Singapore said it was open to new proposals from Malaysia on the project.
