On that occasion, the Permanent Secretary of State welcomed and congratulated the 24 winners as civil servants from various ministries and institutions of the Royal Government of Cambodia, including 3 health officials who received scholarships from the Government of Japan. JDS) for a two-year master's degree (2023-2025) at universities in Japan.
The Permanent Secretary of State also shared many experiences related to the study of life and customs, traditions of living abroad, especially Japan, which she had studied for one year.
At the same time, she encouraged the 24 winners to work hard and focus on learning new techniques and skills and good experiences from Japan, a developing country, including new technologies. Modern to contribute to the development of Cambodia to achieve the goal of a high middle income country by 2030 and a high income country by 2050.
