Ministry of Labor announces the implementation of the third master plan on occupational safety and health 2023-2027
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has announced the launch of the third Master Plan on Occupational Safety and Health 2023-2027, which covers the textile, garment, footwear, bag and travel products sectors, as well as system and employment. Outside of other systems, such as employment in agriculture, construction, etc.
This announcement was made on July 11, 2023 at the Phnom Penh Hotel under the chairmanship of Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training.
Mr. Tep Sophorn, General Manager of the Federation of Employers and Business Associations of Cambodia (CAMFEBA), expressed his hope that the Third Master Plan on Occupational Safety and Health 2023-2027 will be a mechanism for addressing policies, priorities and necessary measures. To continue to ensure occupational safety and health for workers.
Mr. Tun Sophoan, National Coordinator of the ILO in Cambodia, assessed that the past implementation of occupational safety and health has reduced workplace accidents, leading to increased productivity in factories. He said that the issue of occupational safety and health is very important to the ILO, with a series of regulations and requires member states to participate.
In order for the third master plan to be successfully implemented, the Minister recommended to all stakeholders to continue to cooperate to prevent work accidents in the workplace as follows:
1. Labor inspectors must strengthen the implementation of the Labor Law through increasing the efficiency of labor inspections and further strengthening the tripartite mechanism of the National Committee for Occupational Health and Safety to improve the working conditions of workers and strengthen the system. Manage occupational health and safety at all levels.
2- Permitting the re-opening of health checks for workers by occupational doctors because it is the only mechanism to implement the master plan on occupational safety and health.
4. For the workers to pay attention to inform the manager about the risks and dangers that may occur in the workplace, find out about the risks and dangers that may occur in the workplace and measures to protect themselves from the manager or officials. Occupational safety, increase awareness of health and safety information posted in the enterprise.
