BEIJING, July 9 (Xinhua) - US Treasury Secretary Yellen wrapped up a four-day visit to China on July 9. During the talks and talks in recent days, both China and the United States have indicated that they will strengthen communication and cooperation. Chinese officials have stressed that generalizing national security is not conducive to normal economic and trade communication.
Yellen is the second senior US government official to visit China in a month. Yellen's visit to China is seen as a practical step to implement the consensus reached by Chinese and US leaders at the Bali summit, as well as boost communication and financial exchanges. Between the two countries.
At present, China is promoting modernization in the Chinese style and is willing to strengthen cooperation with other countries in the world, including the United States, to promote common development. As for the United States, China has a huge market, and cooperation with China is conducive to boosting US employment opportunities and curbing inflation.
At the same time, the United States must make efforts not to turn economic problems into political issues. The United States should soon lift tariffs on China, ease export bans to China, lift sanctions on Chinese enterprises, as well as create conditions for the two countries' enterprises to expand cooperation. Trade and investment operations.
