Authority: Permission to build on a creek in Kang Meas district, aiming for the general public to shelter and prevent landslides
(Kampong Cham): Deputy Governor of Kang Meas District, Mr. Oeun Sothealy, came out to claim that the authorities allowed the owners to build on the forage land because it saw that it was in the public interest, especially the local people, this construction is a kind of school for Ordinary people pass through and can take refuge.
Mr. Oeun Sothealy confirmed this on July 11, 2023 to end the public confusion regarding the construction of a construction site affecting the forage land in Anlong Koki village, Sdao commune, Kang Meas district, Kampong Cham province.
According to the Deputy Governor of Kang Meas District, the owner of the building is Seng Kimsa, a 72-year-old female who lives on the side of the road next to a canal in Anlong Koki village, Sdao commune, Kang Meas district. But every year when the river floods, the creek always collapses almost off the road in front of his house.
Due to the collapse of the access road to the canal, the owner of the construction requested the district authority to build for the common good, that is, for the shelter of the general public, and also to prevent the land at the mouth of the canal from collapsing. Continue off the road.
"This road, in addition to the transit of local people, is connected to Prek Koy commune, Reay Pai commune, or can travel from Chbar Ampov commune in Batheay district to this road as well," he said.
According to Mr. Lay Senghong, Sdao commune chief, the road at the mouth of the canal has been collapsing since 2002. At the same time, the commune authorities used to help fill the mouth of the canal with hundreds of cars, but still could not resist.
"If there is no construction, the road will collapse and traffic will be completely suspended, causing local people and people from other areas to cross," he said.
Separately, Mr. Leh Bull, Director of the Office of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction of Kang Meas District, said that the construction was built on the land of the canal, the office did not issue a construction permit to the owner. However, this building is seen as being built for the public good, not the owner of the building for personal gain.
Mr. Le Bull said that the construction of this point has been built three times, the first time was small and collapsed into the canal, so this time the builder to build strong to prevent the collapse of the road to facilitate the canal. Make people's traffic.
