(Phnom Penh): Mr. Dith Tina, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, ordered the relevant officials of the Ministry of Agriculture to take the strictest action against the criminals who cleared more than 50 hectares of flooded forest land (area 3) in Kampong Leng district. Kampong Chhnang Province.
In relation to the above case, Mr. Pum Sotha, the Royal Government delegate in charge of the Director of Fisheries Administration and Mr. Ouk Vibol, Director of the Department of Fisheries Conservation, said that there was indeed clearing and encroachment on flooded forest land in three areas.
Mr. Ouk Vibol said that the land that was cleared was a fisheries conservation area in Chronok commune, Kampong Leng district.
Mr. Pum Sotha also said that on July 6, 2023, Fisheries Administration officials in Kampong Chhnang province raided and confiscated three motorbikes belonging to the flooded forest clearing.
Regarding the protected land in the provinces around the Tonle Sap Lake, the Royal Government has already allocated the land for the people to enjoy. The Royal Government also banned the clearing of flooded forest land in the other three areas.
Floodplain forest land is an important habitat for spawning fish during the rainy season. If this inundated forest land is lost, it will also affect the biodiversity of the Tonle Sap Lake.
While civil servants were busy with the election, a group of crooks took the opportunity to clear and encroach on the flooded forest land around the Tonle Sap Lake.
According to Mr. Pum Sotha, the encroachment on flooded forest land in three areas in Kampong Chhnang province is the largest. For other provinces, it is on a small scale.
