Police arrest 3 illegal online loan agents, send them to court after they threatened the victims
(Phnom Penh): The Anti-Technology Crime Department of the National Police in collaboration with the Phnom Penh Municipal Police has arrested three suspects as illegal online loan agents after they went to threaten victims at Borey Peng Huoth. Boeung Sno, Sangkat Chbar Ampov, Phnom Penh.
According to the Anti-Technology Crime Department, on July 11, 2023, the three suspects were arrested on July 9, 2023 under the coordination of Mr. Seng Heang, Deputy Prosecutor of Phnom Penh. Sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for legal action today.
In front of the police, the three suspects confessed that they had worked as agents for an online lending company and that they had acted as lobbyists and borrowers from both lenders. That often threatens those who do not pay on time. The department also found that these loan companies were unlicensed and did not seek permission from the National Bank of Cambodia.
According to the Prakas between the General Commissioner of the National Police and the National Bank of Cambodia dated 23 January 2023, it will confirm that it will take strict legal action against illegal lending and dissemination in all forms related to the provision of financial services. No rules allowed.
