(Phnom Penh): Dr. San Vathana, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, stated that until now, digital education has become a concept in learning and teaching, which so far is not. There are students who say they know how to learn on the phone, and there are no teachers who have never taught with the Zoom system.
Dr. San Vathana said this morning, July 11, 2023, on the occasion of presiding over the opening of the seminar on "Campaign to support digital education for students in Phnom Penh High School" with the participation of Mr. Hem Sinareth, Director of the Department of Education, Youth and Sports of Phnom Penh, Mr. and Mrs. Director of Educational Institutions in Phnom Penh, including many teachers.
The campaign aims to improve student achievement and quality in the digital age, which will begin in July 2023. Dr. San Vathana also said that this digital education is an opportunity that allows us to make a difference for the better, for the students of Cambodia as well.
Dr. San Vathana said that the campaign to support digital education for students in Phnom Penh secondary schools will be implemented in 38 public secondary schools in Phnom Penh and more than 40,000 students who are studying at the upper secondary level will receive Training by 367 student-teacher-student volunteers has been conducted directly to nearly 1,000 classrooms.
1: Exploring learning methods Each student can find a learning method that is suitable for each lesson and subject, as well as a learning method that is appropriate to their personality.
2: In-depth learning using multidisciplinary learning resources: Each student can use appropriate learning resources to learn self-study after work in the classroom and collaborative learning to solve classroom problems as well. Additional training or practice with homework
3: Accelerated learning: For students who learn slowly or do not understand the lesson well or miss out by learning with learning resources produced specifically for a detailed understanding of each lesson.
4: Establish a study club for slow learners or subject study club: Students can jointly create a study club with outstanding students to help teach students who are slow to learn or students who are interested in learning by creating a project to study more deeply and In a cooperative manner
5: High School Preparatory Exam Preparation: Students will receive an explanation of the key to exam preparation and guidance on important study resources to improve and enhance their ability.
6: Use of mobile applications - Classrooms: Students can access a full range of learning resources (all lessons, all subjects, all levels) mixed (with a variety of videos, worksheets, textbooks, practice books ...). And rich (learning in brief, learning with questions and answers, learning with video tutorials, self-test).
