(Phnom Penh): At least 45 suspects were arrested in criminal and drug offenses across Cambodia on July 10, 2023 yesterday. This was confirmed by General Khieu Sopheak, spokesman for the Ministry of Interior, to Fresh News on July 11, 2023.
General Khieu Sopheak added that of the 45 suspects, 17 were arrested in 14 criminal cases and 28 were arrested in 11 drug cases.
Duke Kith Meng asks Australian government to set up commercial office in Cambodia as bilateral trade grows to over $ 546 million
(Phnom Penh): Duke Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, has called on the Australian Government to establish an Australian Chamber of Commerce (AusTrade) in Cambodia to strengthen and expand bilateral ties.
The proposal was made on the occasion of the Duke's participation and speech at a meeting between the Cambodian private sector and Australia's Special Envoy for Southeast Asia, Nicolas Moore, at the Australian Ambassador's residence. In Cambodia on the afternoon of July 10, 2023.
The event was also attended by senior Australian officials, members of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, representatives of the International Chamber of Commerce, business associations and more than 80 Cambodian companies.
The gathering was held on the occasion of the Australian Special Envoy's visit to Cambodia to strengthen ties with the Cambodian private sector to promote trade and investment between Cambodia and Australia.
Speaking on the occasion, Duke Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, warmly welcomed the Australian Special Envoy's visit to Cambodia and highlighted the excellent relations between Australia and Cambodia, which have had diplomatic ties since 1952. Australia supported the peace process in Cambodia during the 1980s and 1990s, contributing to the building of Cambodia's current stability.
Duke expresses enthusiasm over the Australian Government's 2040 Southeast Asian Economic Women's Strategy to identify emerging trade and investment opportunities and make ASEAN a place for future business with faster economic growth. In the world with a total population of over 660 million and a gross national product of $ 3.66 trillion. More specifically, Cambodia is in the middle of this region.
He emphasized that trade and investment between Cambodia and Australia continued to grow and benefited from the ASEAN-Australia-New Zealand Free Trade Agreement and the Regional Economic Partnership Agreement. Cambodia is one of the fastest growing economies in the region, with economic growth projected at 5.6% in 2023. Many Australian companies are currently doing business in Cambodia.
The duke supports trade and investment between the two countries in all fields, especially agriculture, health, resources and education. In this regard, the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce will organize a business visit to Australia and welcome the Australian business delegation to visit Cambodia.
(Pursat): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, presented candles and gifts to 18 pagodas in Pursat province.
In the joyful and generous ceremony, Duke Try Pheap and Duke Kien Srey Neang offered candles, incense and flowers to Preah Ratanatray. After that, Ta Achar also led religious ceremonies, including chanting, Preah Ratanatray, Samathan Sil, etc., and offering Preah Vossa candles and offerings to the 18 pagodas.
After handing over the Preah Vossa candles and gifts, the monks also blessed Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, as well as the duke and the owner of the candles, and dedicated all the merits. To relatives who have passed away.
Every year, on the eve of the New Year, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit always present Preah Vossa candles and gifts to all temples throughout the country, especially for Pursat province through Duke Try Pheap. Presented Preah Vossa candles and gifts to pagodas without fail.
The 18 pagodas that were prepared to offer candles and gifts this morning came from Pursat, Bakan, Phnom Kravanh and Veal Veng districts.
During the ceremony, in addition to offering Preah Vossa candles to a pair of pagodas, Duke Try Pheap and Duke Kien Srey Neang also made other generous donations, including: Four suffixes for 18 monks, each 1,760,000 Riel suffix for monk's meal per pagoda 1,000,000 Riel Wash 18 packs Study materials 18 packs Rice per pagoda 100 kg Noodles, condensed milk, canned fish, pork, fish sauce, soy sauce, fruit juice, pure water.
In addition to offering candles and offerings to temples and monks, this morning's ceremony also saw the distribution of alms to 340 grandparents, each of whom received 100,000 Riels and 2 scarves. Well.
In addition, Duke Try Pheap and Duke Kien Srey Neang also prepared lunch for the 18 monks and grandparents who were invited to attend the ceremony.
The Vesa Candle and Gift Offering Ceremony was held in a happy and generous atmosphere. Grandma and Grandpa also expressed their happiness for receiving the gift that comes from the heart, which is pure generosity.
The current support policy for the sector is not attractive and the market expects further stimulus measures to be launched soon.
In November last year, the People's Bank of China issued a statement outlining 16 measures to support the cash-strapped sector, including deferred repayments in a stimulus package to ease the financial crisis that has plagued the sector. Since mid-2020.
The extension of the policy encourages financial institutions and real estate companies to negotiate independently and actively support real estate developers through Revolving (rollover) existing loans and adjusting loan repayment arrangements.
The People's Bank of China added that an additional one year extension for these existing types of loans, which will be due before the end of 2024, is allowed.
The People's Bank of China also said that loans provided to support construction projects not completed before the end of 2024 will not be downgraded to a risk rating during the lending period.
