The generous gift of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit for the family of 3 twins was handed over by Mr. Seng Teang, the personal assistant of Samdech Techo Prime Minister and his wife on Sunday 9th and 10th Monday. This July 2023.
Each family received 5 million riels, 50 kilograms of rice, 2 large boxes of milk, 5 kilograms of sugar, 2 sarongs and 2 scarves.
The families that gave birth to the triplets were the 399th and 400th families. The third family has a father named Thiv Thuch, 36 years old, and a mother named Bin Vorn, 37 years old, living in Kak village, Chob Vary commune, Preah Net Preah district, Banteay Meanchey province. The family gave birth to triplets for the fourth time.
Separately, the 400th family has a father named Moh Tun E, 25 years old, mother named Yean Sophan, 21 years old, gave birth to triplets, two boys and a girl. The family lives in Kam Prohm village, Khun Ream commune, Banteay Srei district, Siem Reap province.
In front of the families of the three twins, Mr. Seng Teang conveyed the deepest condolences from Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to the two families. He said that the two princes always send greetings to people everywhere.
Mr. Seng Teang also said that from 1999 to the present, more than 24 years ago, there were 400 families with three or four twins. They have always received generous donations from Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to support the hardships of daily life, especially raising three twins to be the grandchildren of both Samdech.
Mr. Seng Teang also pointed out that all these donations are not donations from the Royal Government, donations from the Cambodian Red Cross or donations from political parties. On the contrary, all these gifts are the gifts born from the sincere and high-mindedness of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, who have realized the real difficulties for people who give birth to triplets.
