(Phnom Penh): Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen has called on NATO member states and US allies to work together to prevent the use of cluster munitions in the war between Russia and Ukraine.
Regarding the use of cluster munitions in the war between Russia and Ukraine, on July 9, Samdech Techo Hun Sen called on the US President not to use cluster munitions.
He said the use of cluster munitions would be the greatest danger to the people of Ukraine for decades or even hundreds of years if the cluster munitions were used in Russian-occupied territory.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also recalled the painful experience of Cambodia, which received cluster bombing from the United States in the early 1970s. Samdech Techo confirmed that for more than half a century now, there has been no way to destroy all the bombs.
According to a Reuters report released on July 7, 2023, the United States plans to send "cluster munitions" to Ukraine for use in the fight against Russian aggression.
The US plan to use cluster munitions is raising concerns about the catastrophic consequences of the war between Russia and Ukraine. Several countries, including human rights groups, have reacted to US plans to use cluster munitions.
