The girl who Samdech Techo saved her life from a hollow heart disease has returned home
(Phnom Penh): After successfully undergoing heart surgery and resting for about a week, Monty Dana and her mother have now returned home from the hospital with happy faces.
Mang Thidana, 5 years old, in Toul Makak village, Anlong Thnout commune, Krakor district, Pursat province. The girl was born with a heart problem. On June 30, 2023, Ms. Chhay Chanthy, the mother, brought the girl, Thidana, to ask for help from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister, during a meeting with workers in Krakor district, Pursat province.
Receiving a request to save his daughter's life from this poor woman, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also instructed Ms. Youk Sambath, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, to intervene and seek medical treatment for this girl without delay. Not only advising to seek medical treatment for Monty Dana, the Prime Minister also donated some money to mothers to solve difficulties in life.
Monty Dana underwent a closed ventricular fibrillation (VSD) surgery at Kantha Bopha Hospital in Phnom Penh on July 3, 2023. After about 5 hours of highly responsible surgery by a team of doctors, Thidana's heart was successfully reattached.
Dr. Kisanti, director of Kantha Bopha Hospital in Cambodia, said that after a week of post-surgery follow-up, Monty Dana's health had improved and she was allowed to return home. Return home on the morning of July 10, 2023.
Leaving the hospital this morning, both mother and daughter Thidana showed a wide smile on their faces, a sign of great joy. In particular, a smile full of hope to continue the journey of life after receiving the warmth of the rescue of Samdech Techo Prime Minister.
There is no happiness equal to taking a life out of a daughter's chronic illness, and no greater merit than the life-saving merits. With incomparable excitement, Ms. Chhay Chanthy raised her hand from a distance to express her deepest gratitude and appreciation to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen.
Ms. Chhay Chanthy confirmed, "My daughter and I are very excited. Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit are the living gods who helped my son to come back to life. This multiplication is so great, nothing is priceless, nothing can compare. I want to remember this merit for the rest of my life.
