After the riots, the French government banned the sale and possession of fireworks on the National Day 14 July
PARIS (Reuters) - France has banned the sale, possession and transportation of fireworks during the July 14 national holiday following riots sparked by police shooting, the French government said Sunday. Kill a teenager. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Sunday, July 9, 2023.
Fireworks are among the weapons chosen during the riots that erupted in France after a police officer shot and killed a 17-year-old boy on June 27 near Paris.
"To prevent the risk of serious disruption to public order during the July 14 festival, the sale, possession, transportation and use of poisons and fireworks are prohibited until "July 15."
