In many conflicts in the past, cluster munitions have had a high rate of sudden explosions, with thousands of unexploded ordnance scattered throughout the land, which could endanger human and animal lives to this day. The United States used the latest cluster munitions in the Iraq war in 2003.
For more than a year, the United States and its allies have sent large amounts of weapons aid to Ukraine, including millions of millions of 155 mm artillery shells. The 155 mm artillery shell is capable of hitting targets at a range of 24 to 32 km. But at the same time, the Ukrainian military has used so many artillery pieces that almost the United States and NATO have not yet produced.
In a letter sent to the Joe Biden administration in March, several senior US lawmakers from both the House of Representatives and the Senate said the United States had at least 3 million cluster munitions left. Urged the White House to send the bombs to Ukraine to ease the burden of US arms supplies.
* Is the use of cluster munitions a war crime?
The Convention on the Prohibition of the Use of Cluster Munitions has been signed by 123 countries, which have agreed not to use cluster munitions for production, transfer or storage. But the United States, Russia and Ukraine are not signatories to the convention.
