Since the pagoda is far from the provincial town and far from the hometown of his hometown, he also initiated this festival to buy gifts such as chivor, candles, candles and other food items, especially to raise money. To build a pavilion for the monks who live in this temple.
Venerable Viriya Thammo Han Theany said that he had led the construction of this pavilion since 2022, so far it has been 30% completed, at a cost of 7,000 dollars, but lacked funds to continue and suspended construction. For a while.
According to the priest, the head abbot of this pagoda, he is currently on the temporary chan hall without a hut.
