Electricity fire burns a house, causing complete damage and property damage of nearly 20,000 dollars in Chhlong district
(Kratie): A power outage caused a fire in a house built entirely of damaged wood while the owner was not at home to do business in a distant district.
According to the Chhlong district police report, one house measuring 6 meters by 11 meters, made of wood, tile, wall, and board, was completely damaged.
The owner of the house is Te Vong, male, 56 years old, and his wife is Mao Sopheap, 57 years old. The landlord left the business in a distant district and was electrocuted, causing a complete fire and damaging some appliances, totaling about $ 1,600,000.
According to the report, in the case of the fire, the police force used the fire truck of the Chhlong District Police Inspectorate to intervene and put out the fire completely and did not spread the fire to other houses, using 2 vehicles and did not cause any fire. No one was injured in the incident.
However, having a lot of debt is not good, it will affect your financial health as well as your mental health, especially if borrowing too much debt beyond the ability to repay or misuse it will cause. Becoming indebted can lead to business loss, loss of friends, relatives, or even the sale of property to pay off debts.
In order not to fall into deeper debt, Ieng Sotheara, a well-known Buddhist trader and businessman in Cambodia, offers the following five tips:
1. Debt is suffering He explained that in Buddhism explained that happiness because there is no debt, that is, when we have debt will lose happiness or happiness is reduced both physically and mentally. Therefore, if it is possible to avoid borrowing, they should avoid it.
3: Do not take risks
He explained that "taking such a risk is very dangerous because we take this risk will have problems in the future, so do not take any risks, think carefully before borrowing or before lending. And do not take another risk before lending, there must be a contract with an honest lawyer, properly stamped by a lawyer, because when there is a problem, we have to take legal documents or contracts as a solution.
4: If you are very tired, find a good friend
Some individuals become more indebted when they are in deep debt. The first step is to settle down and seek out friends who have experience in this field and can provide strategies to help them deal with this debt.
So, if you have a debt problem that can not be solved, first of all, you need to find a good idea or strategy to help find a solution, and the second step is to go to the rich so as not to sink deeper.
