Thai Securities and Exchange Commission seizes assets of listed company for fraudulent accounting
The Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) of Thailand has seized the assets of Stark Corporation and its largest shareholder, as well as the assets of several former CEOs, accusing them of involvement in accounting fraud. . According to the Bangkok Post.
The move comes in addition to banning them from traveling abroad.
According to the Bangkok Post, the SEC recently charged the 10 parties with financial misconduct by the Special Investigation Department (DSI), accusing them of involvement. Agree with others to produce fake financial statements for Stark and its subsidiaries between 2021 and 2022 to defraud others.
The securities regulator said the asset freeze order was issued because "there are reasonable circumstances to believe that individuals will transfer or sell those assets."
The SEC will also seek a court order to prevent the accused from leaving the country within the next 15 days, the statement said.
