Kampong Chhnang Provincial Court President Donates 3 Million Riels to Peam Khnong Primary School in Kampong Leng District
(Kampong Chhnang): Mr. Kim Rath Narin, President of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Court, on July 8, 2023, donated 3 million Riels to Peam Khnong Primary School in Peam Khnong Village, Plou Touk Commune, Kampong Leng District. For moving and lifting the school building, place the pillars high above the water.
The announcement follows a call from students, teachers at Peam Khnong Primary School, as well as parents, guardians and local authorities to philanthropists and leaders to provide some funding for the rolling fee. A school building is raised on a stone pillar to keep it high above the water to make it easier for younger students to study during the rainy season this year as well as next year.
According to the principal, one school building that will be moved backwards will be raised on the pillars above the water, there are 2 rooms, 1 room for teachers to stay and 1 room for students to study. This room also has two shifts for students to study. In the morning shift, there are 81 first grade students and during the day shift, there are 31 third grade students in this room.
However, since the village authorities and teachers could not afford it, they all decided to seek support through the broadcast on Fresh News, lest there be philanthropists or leaders to support the above request for fear. Maybe the water level will rise a little sooner and it will not be possible, while the younger students will have a hard time getting to school because the water level rises and floods here every year.
