(Phnom Penh): July 8, 2023 is the eighth day of the election campaign for the 7th National Assembly election in 2023. According to the report of the Capital and Provincial Election Commission (CEC), 12 political parties conducted campaign activities, including 7 political parties marched.
In addition to the above seven political parties, five other political parties, including the Local Democrat Party, the Khmer National Unity Party, the Women's Party for Women, the Theosophical Party, and the Peasants' Party, have been campaigning through microphone meetings at the party's headquarters and mobile. The village distributes leaflets in the backyard, closes leaflets and banners in public, performs concerts, performs slide shows and videos at the polling stations where they stand.
Overall, the general situation of the political party election campaign on the eighth day went smoothly, with security, safety, good order and no violence.
5,000 luxury saplings planted at Touk Meas Kangrei Wildlife Sanctuary and Forest with support from Ung Fund Design
(Kampong Chhnang): Touk Meas Kangri Association has organized a campaign to plant 5,000 saplings of luxury trees, including: 1,430 beng trees, 1,450 rose trees, 1,250 koki trees and 870 teal trees in Touk Meas Kangri Animal and Forest Conservation Area in Chamnok and Po communes, Kampong Leng district, Kampong Chhnang province, in order to inspire a common spirit of protecting the environment and saving the planet.
In response to this important task, under the initiative and vision of the long-term and generous of Duke Ung Bunhou, the Ung Fund Design Foundation was established as a non-profit fund, with the duke using his own resources to help. People in need, as well as building schools, hospitals and pagodas, etc.
For the purpose of caring for, protecting and conserving wildlife and forests, a new association has been established under the auspices of the Ung Fund Design, with the approval of the Royal Government, with the Ministry of Environment as the Joint Chiefs of Staff for Wildlife and Forest Conservation in the Phnom Touk Meas area. .
Speaking during the campaign, Mr. Ung Siv Meng called on the people and relevant authorities at all levels to continue to work together to prevent forest crime and wildlife trafficking in the community.
According to the governor of Kampong Leng district, as the authority, he is very happy and willing to participate in wildlife and forest conservation activities in this area, where Duke Ung Bun Hou always spends his time and money to protect and plant more seedlings. And the acceptance of wildlife from the people in this area.
He called on government officials, the armed forces, especially the people, to work together to preserve wildlife and forests in the area.
The Touk Meas Kangri Association was registered with the Ministry of Interior No. 2512, dated April 25, 2023, with its headquarters in Damnak Kak village, Po commune, Kampong Leng district, Kampong Chhnang province.
