A car with a Lao license plate hit a roadblock in Sen Sok district, the police took more than 100 pieces of drugs and stored them.
(Phnom Penh): A Hyundai car with Lao license plate crashed into a barrier dividing the road ahead in Sen Sok district, when the police took the crane and suddenly found more than 100 pieces of drugs.
Brigadier General San Sok Seiha, spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, told Fresh News that local authorities had received information about the incident that hit the road at midnight on July 8, 2023 in Sen Sok district. Leave it alone as the driver escapes.
According to Brigadier General San Sok Seiha, when the police received the information, they went out to inspect and temporarily stored it at the Sen Sok District Police Inspectorate. A search of the car to identify the driver and the occupants revealed more than 100 suspected packages of methamphetamine and ice.
The spokesman stressed that the specialized police force is currently conducting further research to find those involved and take legal action.
