(Washington): Since Russia's war of aggression against Ukraine erupted in February 2022, cooperation between Russia and China has grown in all areas. Moscow has made no secret of the fact that it is relying on China in a global confrontation with the US-led West, seeing Beijing as a "common enemy."
The claim that Russia is or will become a vassal state of China has yet to answer an important question: Why does Beijing want to create unbalanced relations with Moscow? Indeed, it is very difficult to identify issues or areas in which Russia may refuse to cooperate with China on a regular basis. The Russian market is open to Chinese goods, and Russia intends to supply China with the resources that Beijing needs.
