(Phnom Penh): In 2024, the Cambodian economy is projected to achieve a growth rate of around 6.6%. This is according to the circular on the preparation of the strategic budget plan for 2024-2026 and the preparation of the draft law on finance for the management of 2024 of the Royal Government of Cambodia, which was received by Fresh News on July 7, 2023.
The Royal Government of Cambodia has stated that "for the year 2024, the Cambodian economy is projected to achieve a growth rate of around 6.6% due to the expectation of a recovery in external demand." "And investment confidence while domestic economic activity continues to balance."
Cambodia's economy in 2024 is supported by:
1. The agricultural sector is projected to grow at around 1.1%, supported by the growth of the crop and livestock sub-sectors, while the fisheries sub-sector is expected to continue to recover slowly.
2. The industrial sector is projected to grow at a rate of 8.5%, supported by better growth in the garment and non-garment sub-sectors, while the construction sub-sector continues to grow at a slower pace than before the Kovid-19 crisis.
3. The services sector is projected to continue to grow at a rate of 6.9%, with continued activity in the hotel and restaurant sub-sector and other support services, including the wholesale-retail sub-sector and the transport and transportation sub-sector in Cambodia. While the real estate sub-sector is expected to continue to achieve lower-than-normal growth.
The implementation of the "Strategic Framework and Program to Restore and Stimulate Cambodia's Economic Growth in Living with Kovid-19 in the New Normal Path for 2021-2023" in the past, both on the rehabilitation of existing growth sectors as well as A number of new potential areas, including the development of small and medium enterprises and the development of digital and green infrastructure, will contribute significantly to boosting and adding value to the economy.
