NEW DELHI: A Supreme Court in western India on Friday rejected a call by opposition leader Rahul Gandhi to suspend his conviction in a defamation case pending a court ruling. Completed his hopes of returning to parliament and contesting the 2024 national election. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Friday, July 7, 2023.
Gandhi, 52, from India's Congress party, was sentenced to two years in prison, but his sentence was extended and he was released on bail. After rejecting the request for suspension, Gandhi was able to appeal to the Constitutional Court and then to the Supreme Court, his last resort.
