Watch the full video below: A worker in Cheung Kreav commune, Kampong Chhnang province, met with a traffic accident, became disabled, could not afford to pay the bank debt and faced the confiscation of houses and land, asked for the intervention of the management to facilitate (Video inside)
(Kampong Chhnang): The family of a female worker is living in extreme poverty because she became disabled, lost her ability to work and could not work because she was injured in a traffic accident while leaving Returning from work more than three months ago.
She recounted that one day, when her daughter was leaving the factory in the evening, riding a motorcycle alone, halfway through, she was hit by a herd of cows. Her head fell to the paved road, seriously injuring her left side of the skull and injuring several other bodies.
Due to her daughter's condition, she was taken to Kampong Chhnang Provincial Hospital, where she was rushed to a Russian hospital in Phnom Penh, where she regained consciousness two months later. Of doctors, but she is still disabled, having completely lost her ability to work.
She said that in a Russian hospital, doctors tried to save her by performing surgery with little hope, but fortunately her daughter survived, leaving her paralyzed for the rest of her life. During the two months that his daughter was hospitalized in Russia, she was unconscious.
As for the husband, who used to work as a construction worker, he also had to suspend his work because he did not work as consistently as before. One of her daughters, who was in her second year of university, now has to drop out of school to take care of her mother.
