In the first week of July, the Customs Risk Management and Audit Unit cracked down on 11 tax evading trucks and fined 400 million riels while an armed perpetrator was detained
(Phnom Penh): The General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia on July 7, 2023 issued a press release confirming that the General Department of Customs has been actively implementing Regulation No. 01 BOP dated June 7, 2022. Royal Government on measures to increase efficiency in preventing and suppressing tax evasion.
This work is important to increase the atmosphere of fair competition in business, revenue collection in the national budget and social protection (crackdown on smuggling of drugs and substandard goods ...) and so on.
In fact, at the beginning of the first week of July, the Risk Management and Audit Unit of the Customs in collaboration with the Special Intervention Team conducted operations to crack down on smuggled goods at some targets, cracking down on 11 smuggled trucks with a total weight of 69,520. .00 kg and has an estimated amount of taxes and duties, including penalties for violations of the law, more than 400 million riels.
By obstructing the customs authorities and especially the explosion of firearms on the customs authorities are enforcing the law as a serious crime, the customs officials have filed a complaint to the competent authorities of Takeo province, with the support and attention of General Santin Bandit Neth Savoeun, the National Police Commissioner, who caused the explosion, was arrested by the competent authorities and the Takeo Provincial Court and is being processed according to the law.
It should be reminded that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has often instructed the Armed Forces and authorities at all levels to support the customs and tax authorities in performing their roles and responsibilities to raise revenue for the national budget.
