General Chea Dara: The famous temple of Preah Vihear belongs to the Khmer people, representing the "great masterpiece of Khmer architecture" that must be protected together at any cost.
(Phnom Penh): Former Border Commander, General Professor Chea Dara, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Personal Adviser to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia in charge of Rector of the National Defense University on behalf of Rector, Deputy Chief of Staff All of the National Defense University would like to congratulate the 15th anniversary of the Temple of Preah Vihear being inscribed on the World Heritage List on July 7, 2008-July 7, 2023.
General Professor Chea Dara emphasized that the famous temple of Preah Vihear belongs to the Khmer people, representing the "great masterpiece of Khmer architecture" that we, the Cambodian people, must protect together, no matter what the cost.
General Chea Dara stated that the history of registration:
The 32nd meeting of the WHC on July 7, 2008 in Quebec City, Canada, unanimously decided to list the famous temples, representing the "great masterpieces of Khmer architecture".
One week later, on July 14, 2008, a celebration was organized by Phnom Penh Capital Hall in collaboration with the General Department of Bayon Radio and Television in the National Stadium to welcome the arrival of the Cambodian delegation from Quebec City, Canada. . The event further strengthened the overall national unity under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who raised national pride through the accomplishments of the Cambodian delegation.
The next day, July 15, 2008, in complete violation of the UN Charter and the international legal base, Thai troops crossed the Cambodian border into Cambodian territory, heading for the newly inscribed Preah Vihear temple on the World Heritage List. This occupies the "neighborhood near the temple on Cambodian territory", including Wat Keo Sikkha Kirisvara and the area around the pagoda.
The general stressed that war is not uncommon because Cambodians have been through decades of armed conflict. However, Cambodia was shocked and disappointed by how Thailand reacted to the events of the July 7, 2008 decision in Quebec City.
Cambodia must defend its territorial integrity, no matter how sacrificed, but the whole nation has the wisdom to be patient, leaving this order to the Royal Government of Cambodia to resolve under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen as Prime Minister.
