BEIJING: US Treasury Secretary Janet Yellen arrived in Beijing on Thursday to meet with Chinese leaders as part of efforts to restore strained relations between the two countries. Due to security, technology and other issues. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Thursday, July 6, 2023.
During her visit, Yellen plans to focus on stabilizing the global economy and curbing China's support for Russia during its invasion of Ukraine, a treasury official in Washington told reporters ahead of the trip. This visit.
The visit follows Anthony Blinken's recent visit, the highest-level US visit to Beijing in five years. The two countries agreed to stabilize relations but failed to agree on improving relations between the two militaries.
Yellen has previously said the two governments "may and may need to find ways to live together" despite tensions over geopolitics and economic development.
