Four people sent to court in connection with a club fire near the Depot Market, killing eight people
(Phnom Penh): The Tuol Kork District Criminal Police on July 6, 2022, arrested four suspects suspected of being involved in the July 2 fire at a karaoke club and 6969 Keys Hotel, which resulted in their deaths. Eight people went to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court to be handed over to the prosecutor's office to open an investigation and proceed with the charges according to legal procedures.
An additional report from the Tuol Kork Police Inspectorate, obtained by Fresh News on the morning of July 3, 2023, states that in this incident, the police also arrested four people on July 2, 2023. 2023 Yesterday, a decorator repaired the above location and caused a fire.
Based on the confession of the decorator, Khom Sophal, 29, claimed that eight of them were decorators, three were working on the ground floor and five were building the fifth floor ceiling to renovate the rooms. The ceiling suddenly saw smoke coming from the top of the ceiling, black glass, glass on the ceiling, causing flames.
When he saw the wires about the size of a thumb on the metal ceiling, he was lying on the ceiling, so he and the other workers used fire hoses to put out the fire, but it did not go out. But the fire broke out and later, the fire brigade of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police came down to intervene to help put out the fire.
Through the examination of the scene and the bodies, as well as the confirmation of the Phnom Penh forensic doctor, all eight bodies died from suffocation in the fire. The fire consumed a total of 22 water trucks, 88 of which consumed 352 cubic meters of water, of which 8 auxiliary vehicles consumed 24 units of 96 cubic meters of water.
The eight bodies have now been handed over to their families for traditional rites. Mr. Hun Many: One vote for the Cambodian People's Party is equal to one vote for the improvement of one's life and family.
