(Phnom Penh): Cambodia and Australia are working together to promote the establishment of agro-industrial parks in Cambodia as soon as possible to promote the production and processing of agricultural products in Cambodia for export to international markets.
He pointed out that the potential target for the establishment of agro-industrial parks now is at the Fourth Special Economic Zone of Cambodia, located in the northwestern region of Cambodia.
He added: "This agro-industrial park is a requirement of Cambodia, which is the goal of Cambodia's policy set out to increase the processing industry for our agricultural products in the future to avoid more exports. "Raw materials go to gross, as we do not add value to the processing of our agricultural products, which is a strategy for our country."
The Australian Embassy in Cambodia said that the agro-industrial park will be a hub for agricultural processing, research and development, capacity building and is being set up to provide a safe workplace and environment, especially for Women and staff in need.
In April, the Cambodia-Australia Partnership for Sustainable Economic Development (CAPRED) organized a visit for members of the Cambodia Agro-Industrial Parks (AIP) Committee to Melbourne and Perth to review Australia's Agro-Industrial Parks and Learn about Agro-Industrial Ecosystems, including food processing, improving the business environment and government policies in Australia.
According to a recent report by the Australian Embassy in Cambodia, more than 90% of Cambodia's unprocessed agricultural products are sold to neighboring ASEAN countries, and those countries are processed into The products are more valuable than the original agricultural products, such as fruit juices, crisps, baby food, flour and biofuels.
In the first quarter of 2023, Cambodia exported more than 2.5 million tons of agricultural products to international markets worth more than $ 1.3 billion. This is according to the report of the Ministry of Agriculture. Task Force in Talas Commune, Maung Russey District, Battambang Province Campaign for the 7th National Assembly Election in Wat Chas Village
