(Phnom Penh): Mr. Duong Dara, Secretary of State of the Office of the Council of Ministers and a personal aide to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, visited the Cambodian Agricultural Business Center called "Phsar Doeum Kor Thmey Modern 24 Hours" located on Veng Sreng Street. Trapeang Thleung 4, Sangkat Choam Chao I, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh, on the afternoon of July 4, 2023.
This activity has attracted a lot of public interest and erupted in surprise and full support for this great project in the near future and will help the Royal Government to solve the agricultural market for farmers. Well done.
During the visit, Mr. Duong Dara had a chat and had a detailed discussion with Mr. Phan Sopheak, the founder of the Cambodian Agricultural Business Center.
Mr. Phan Sopheak informed Mr. Duong Dara of two important features of the project:
First, at the beginning of the operation of the Agricultural Business Center of Cambodia, called "Phsar Doeum Kor Thmey Modern 24 hours", there is a plan to collect and buy about 500 tons of agricultural products from farmers per day from the agricultural communities and farmers of the target provinces around the capital. Phnom Penh for distribution to traders in various markets in Phnom Penh and some priority provinces.
Second, the current situation of the project of the center has some national and international development partners are focusing on such development programs in the field of digital marketing, especially USAID has been interested in the principles of project implementation, working mechanism of project development and The Center's medium- and long-term direction plans, which the founders, co-founders, and senior executives are currently working with USAID.
As a result, Mr. Duong Dara fully supports the core plan, along with the strategic direction of the founders and development partners of the organization with the idea of making Cambodian farmers have a wider agricultural market. Nearby centers and leaders from ministries, institutions, especially the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries also supported.
