General Meas Virith: Cambodia continues to suffer from threats posed by the production, trafficking and use of illegal drugs in the region and the world.
(Phnom Penh): General Meas Virith, Secretary General of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, said that Cambodia continues to suffer from threats posed by the production, trafficking and use of illegal drugs in the region and the world. This statement was made at the 44th ASEAN Senior Officials' Meeting on Drugs and Related Meetings on 6 July 2023 via the Via Videoconference hosted by Myanmar.
On that occasion, General Meas Virith added that the rapidly evolving and complex drug situation in the region and the world has affected all countries, in which Cambodia has continued to address by implementing a comprehensive, integrated approach, adhering to the principles of equity. Discrimination and respect for human rights in accordance with the ASEAN Work Plan and the ASEAN Cooperation Plan, with a focus on priority areas of cooperation.
In response to these issues, Cambodia has launched a campaign against illegal drugs from 2017 until now, the eighth step focused on:
* First: Preventive education for all stakeholders, both public and private, and organized this international event on June 28, 2023 under the theme International: People First: Stop Discrimination and Stigma, Strengthen Preventive Education.
* Second: Treatment and Rehabilitation Cambodia provides treatment and rehabilitation services at national and temporary centers and community-based treatment at health facilities: hospitals, referral hospitals and health centers.
* Fifth: In promoting dialogue and facilitating the sharing of information on the illegal drug situation in the region, efforts are made through regular ASOD mechanisms, such as the Airport Drug Prevention Team for ASEAN, the Prevention Team. Drugs in seaports for ASEAN ASEAN Center for Drug Prevention Cooperation. (ASEAN-NARCO) and the ASEAN Drug Control Network (ADMN).
