According to the National Bank of Cambodia's report on financial stability in 2022, obtained by Fresh News on July 6, 2023, "the outlook for 2023 is that the Cambodian economy is projected to grow by 5 percent. "5% with a low inflation rate of about 2%, in which the main potential risk comes from external factors due to economic openness, as well as the strong dependence of the Cambodian economy on the external sector."
These risks include: * Prolonged tensions between Russia and Ukraine and the tightening of the international financial situation, which has affected export and investment prospects in Cambodia.
Prolonged problems in China's real estate market that could hinder the growth of real estate investment in Cambodia.
Rising credit interest rates caused by rising international interest rates have led to lower credit growth and higher borrowing costs, which could also reduce domestic investment.
In addition to external risks, potential internal risks also need to be considered and monitored, possibly from the real estate sector about a decade before the Kovid-19 crisis. The global and domestic economic slowdown due to the Kovid crisis and the recovery in uncertain conditions have led to a steady decline in demand in the sector.
The National Bank of Cambodia (NBC) states that this situation requires careful monitoring, especially on lending to the real estate sector, as well as strengthening close cooperation between the relevant authorities to manage potential risks and their impact on the sector. .
In the face of this uncertainty, the National Bank of Cambodia has been implementing crisis relief measures by carefully restructuring its regulatory framework to strengthen the resilience of the banking system while helping the sector. Priorities such as small and medium enterprises, agriculture, education during the economic recovery.
At the same time, maintaining financial stability is an inter-sectoral task that requires the cooperation and coordination of both authorities and stakeholders, as the financial system is closely interconnected, both within the financial sector and with the physical economy. Headquarters $ 43 million officially launched
