(Phnom Penh): For the past five years, wage protests have increased almost daily in the Cambodian media, but now the number of garment workers' protests is less due to the Royal Government focusing on one of the conditions Many of the conditions demanded by the protesters are salary increases.
The reason why the Royal Government deals with the increase in wages is because the low wages make the workers unable to live in an economic situation and affect labor productivity. This issue is also a major direct issue, causing a large number of workers to faint during the daily work, which parties in the garment sector need to pay attention and intervene.
At the same time, some economists in Cambodia have said that in order for workers to have a comfortable life, factory owners need to facilitate food prices in the workplace, facilitate the price of houses or accommodation, or factory owners ensure food. Workers. Doing so will improve the lives of workers and can boost labor productivity, which can boost factory profits.
On the other hand, reducing the burden on workers, such as sending money to support their families, is an important part of enabling workers to save money for living while working. At the same time, the Royal Government and the private sector, civil society and unions must work together to help improve training and technical capacity to suit higher salaries.
Reducing large costs for factories, such as transportation costs and other informal fees, is also an important part for factory owners to afford to transfer those costs to raise workers' salaries.
But now the workers seem to have stopped protesting, but the factory has asked the Royal Government to help, while the Cambodian garment industry has asked the Royal Government to help reduce some administrative and tax costs that can be offset by higher costs to increase Minimum wage and social security system allowance for workers.
* The role of the government and the livelihood of garment workers
According to the plan, the Royal Government of Cambodia plans to increase the minimum wage for factory workers every year in the Strategic Plan 2022 to 2027, which is a good sign to respond to the first: the inflation rate, the second: the increase in the cost of housing, the third. Fourth: Increased factory competitiveness through good work experience and fifth, factory owner profit sharing.
This foundation is an effective mechanism to ensure the sustainable development of the garment sector in Cambodia. The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia has announced that the lives of workers must be taken into account because the number of workers is the guarantor to support the Cambodian economy through exports, help profits for factory owners and partly support the economy through distribution. Share salary to help families in rural areas.
It is estimated that there are approximately 1 million indirect beneficiaries of garment workers in Cambodia, such as families, shopkeepers around factories, tenants, runners, etc.
Currently, there are about 700,000 garment workers in Cambodia, which will export more than 11 billion US dollars to international markets by 2021, of which the garment sector is worth 8 billion dollars, the footwear sector is 1.3 billion dollars. Leather bags and suitcases are worth about $ 2 billion.
