(Phnom Penh): Monty Dana is a twin girl from a poor family in Tuol Makak village, Anlong Thnout commune, Krakor district, Pursat province. When in the womb, Thidana was found to have an abnormal heart.
At birth, Kantha Bopha doctors found that the girl had a hollow heart and needed to be monitored to see if it could grow close. Due to the lack of livelihood, the family did not bring Thidana to monitor the development of the disease, and the disease worsened as she grew older.
The spirit of a mother who loves and cares for her children is immense, incomparable. The desire to save her child from the dead of the disease made Ms. Chhay Chanthea continue to try to help her daughter, even though there is not much hope.
Ms. Chanthea knows that entering Samdech Techo's program is tense and difficult. Even if there is little hope, it can not stop the ambition of the heart to seek to save her daughter's life. Riding a bicycle, Mrs. Chanthea prayed to God, worshiped the deity, accompanied her to meet Samdech Techo to save her daughter.
Ms. Chanthea's great spirit really moved the angels and helped her to meet Samdech Techo as intended. Meeting Samdech Techo is like meeting an angel to help Ms. Chanthea's child have hope to continue to breathe and get rid of hollow heart disease.
After receiving the information about Thidana's illness, Samdech Techo, a leader full of Brahmanism, felt very sorry for her. Samdech Techo also donated some money and instructed Mrs. Youk Sambath, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, who was invited to participate in the program, to arrange for the treatment of girls.
Without delay, Ms. Youk Sambath immediately sent the girl to seek treatment at Kantha Bopha Hospital.
Dr. Pon Ladin, a cardiologist at Kantha Bopha Hospital in Siem Reap, said that Thidana had a 5 mm diameter ventricular cavity. This coronary artery is present from birth.
The doctor, who has worked at Kantha Bopha Hospital for 20 years, said that the hollow heart causes fatigue and high blood pressure in the lungs, which requires timely surgery.
Cardiac surgery is a difficult task and requires a lot of attention to the surgical work. To save Thidana's life, the doctors spent up to 5 hours on the operation with a patient and responsible attitude.
After successfully undergoing surgery on July 3, Thidana's health has now improved. Thidana has difficulty breathing and is not as tired as before.
Helping her daughter get back to normal is an incomparable pleasure for Ms. Chanthea. This life-saving multiplier is also a huge multiplier that cannot be calculated. Ms. Chanthea considered Samdech Techo as an angel who saved her daughter.
Open heart disease or coronary heart disease is also more common in Cambodian children today. According to Dr. Pon Ladin, the symptoms of the disease can be noticed through the child's difficulty breathing or purple body.
According to the doctor's advice, when a child is observed to have any of the above symptoms, the child should be rushed to a hospital for treatment. If treatment is delayed, it can affect the growth and even the life of the child.
Kantha Bopha Hospital is a humanitarian hospital capable of operating on and treating pediatric open heart disease. Many children have successfully had heart surgery and rehabilitation, as well as giving back smiles to children and their families.
However, he emphasized that none of the victims were in danger, and no one had been identified.
