(Siem Reap): On Tuesday morning, July 4, 2023, Dr. Sean Borath, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, High Representative, Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, presided over the graduation ceremony. To 2,141 students of the University of Specialties of Cambodia, Siem Reap Branch (CUS) who have successfully graduated. The ceremony was held at the main conference hall of Sokha Hotel, Siem Reap.
According to the report, the university has already held nine graduation ceremonies. Eight times in Phnom Penh under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit and once under the chairmanship of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, held in Battambang.
The 10th Graduation Ceremony was presided over by Dr. Sean Borath, High Representative of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports.
The University of Specialties of Cambodia, Siem Reap Branch, started training in 2004 and has been active in training and providing knowledge and skills to higher education students to participate in building human resources, which is an important foundation for building the family economy and society. .
Currently, there are a total of 11,747 undergraduate, postgraduate and doctoral students, 5,788 of whom are female, studying at nine locations and branches, including: Phnom Penh, Kampong Cham, Kampong Thom, Siem Reap, Banteay Meanchey, Battambang and Kampot.
Dr. Meas Bora said that currently, the University of Specialties of Cambodia has a board of directors, management, staff, professors, 130 people working in Siem Reap branch, 26 women.
In order to build human resources with quality, value and success for the society, the specialized universities of Cambodia have set the basic principles in the operation of their daily work and promote the implementation of the Ministry of Education's higher education reform strategy. Youth and Sports by correcting the curriculum framework in response to the development of industry, economy, social, digital, innovation and the establishment of talent research centers, namely:
First, students must strive to study, research and learn throughout their lives to expand their knowledge to adapt to the era of globalization, Buddhist society and the digital economy.
Second, professors must strive to research new teaching methods in the 21st century and prepare digital teaching content in line with the evolution of information technology.
Third, academic staff must strive to provide quality services, professional ability and good personality.
Dr. Meas Bora highlighted that the results and achievements of the past 20 years clearly show the ability, ability and experience that colleagues and universities of Cambodia have in its noble mission is "training to know. "Training to have knowledge, training to have a good personality to succeed in work and career."
In the academic year 2022-2023, the University has developed in both size and depth on: the expansion of physical infrastructure, the strengthening of teaching techniques and learning in the new digital context, teaching methods and learning on the new trajectory of the 21st century. , Strengthen management structure, strengthen management through ICT.
In order to strengthen and take advantage of the flow of knowledge and practicality, the University always invites experienced professionals in the field of work to give lectures, conferences, seminars to students on a regular basis and also send students to internships on specific work sites. .
The University has cooperated and signed MoUs with 56 foreign universities and institutions from South Korea, China, Japan, Thailand, the United Kingdom, the Philippines, Bangladesh, Malaysia, India, Indonesia, Germany, Vietnam and Israel.
The University regularly participates in major international forums and conferences in the field of education, including the annual Asia-Pacific Professional Leadership Conference (QS-APPLE), the AUPF Asia University Leadership Forum, and Quality Assurance Workshops. Education of the AUN-QA Southeast Asian University Network.
To help students easily find internships, internships, volunteer work and job search, the Cambodian University of Specialties has signed a memorandum of understanding with 543 local companies and institutions across the country and will continue to push for greater coverage.
Dr. Sean Borath, on behalf of the President of the Presidium, instructed the winning students on some key points:
First, do not just graduate, but continue to study, research and learn more to broaden your knowledge to adapt to the era of globalization, Buddhist society and the digital economy.
Second, to have a good attitude, be disciplined, have high professional ethics everywhere. Be honest with yourself, with your family, with the people around you and with our nation. Think carefully before making any decisions to avoid harming yourself, your family and society.
Third, to use knowledge to cultivate entrepreneurial ideas to contribute to the creation of new businesses, starting from small businesses and continue to strive for continuous development.
