(Phnom Penh): Cambodia and the United States have continued to expand cooperation in the field of labor to increase trade, investment and create more job opportunities.
Mr. Patrick Murphy expressed his satisfaction with Minister Ith Sam Heng's remarks on the progress of the Better Factories Cambodia (BFC) project, which has pushed for more orders from the US market. In addition to the volume of textiles, clothing, footwear, and the export of bags and travel accessories.
Cambodia strives to benefit from Cambodian-US trade, ranking as the fourth largest exporter to the US market and the third largest beneficiary of the Generalized System of Preferences (GSP) from the United States.
During the meeting, the two sides discussed strengthening cooperation to further strengthen Cambodia-US relations in all aspects to increase their investment in Cambodia in many other fields.
Meanwhile, the two sides discussed a number of recommendations, such as cases of child labor, human trafficking, inspections of labor dispatch agencies to ensure the legitimate rights and interests of workers, ensuring the sustainability of the Arbitration Council and the continuation of improvements. Rights, freedoms, professional organizations: and will continue to comply with the international labor standards that Cambodia has ratified.
The United States will provide more cooperation, especially in the field of vocational training: to contribute to the development of human resources in Cambodia. Vote for the Cambodian People's Party
