(Phnom Penh): A drunk Chinese man was walking on the street and did not know what he was upset about. He pulled out a pistol from a backpack and fired several shots into the air, causing an explosion in the middle of the night. To the surprise and fear of the people nearby. The incident happened at 2:00 AM on July 5, 2023 on the concrete road in Kbal Damrey 2 village, Sangkat Kakap II, Khan Por Sen Chey.
After the incident, Colonel Mon Vuthy, Police Inspector of Por Senchey District, led the Khan Police Force and some police stations in cooperation with the Por Senchey District Military Police Force and immediately intervened. After that, they besieged it all night, but could not immediately arrest the perpetrator because the assailant threatened not to approach until dawn, only to seize and confiscate a Maka 54 pistol along with ammunition. More than 20 more.
The suspect, LIU XIANRUI, 42, did not know where he was staying, and police said he had used an unlicensed weapon. On the other hand, due to drunkenness, the shooting was free, but it is not yet known whether the body contained drugs or not, while the police force is preparing to test the urine for drugs and is being detained. He is temporarily at the Police Inspectorate of Po Sen Chey District.
General knowledge: The role of the five gates of Angkor Thom
2. Ghost Gate - East The Ghost Gate, located on the street in front of Bayon Temple, serves as a procession for the bodies of those living inside Angkor Thom to be cremated or dumped in a river on the outskirts of the city. The gate was only opened for the funeral procession, hence the name "Ghost Gate."
4. Takeo Gate - West The west gate was used for execution. When someone commits a serious, unforgivable crime, they are executed outside the gates by digging a pit and covering it with soil or boulders. (Source: Bio Ta Kwan).
5. The North Gate, the North Gate, was used for priests from near and far to march into the city to meet the King in order to ask for a royal pardon for the lesser offenders. Are being held in the city to bring them back to education.
This tradition continues to this day, with the King still having the right to request the Royal Government and the courts to pardon the minor prisoners held in order to receive a series of pardons until they are released. Depending on the type of punishment for each of them.
