SATHAPANA Bank Plc. Came out to comment on its lawsuit against a former employee
The following is the full text of the statement made by the mandate of SATHAPANA Bank Plc.
Article 12: "Pursuant to the principle of universal arbitration, a person who has been acquitted by a court and can no longer be charged with the same acts, even under the name of a new offense. By. Previously, in this case, there was no verdict or final verdict to release the suspect from the charges, only the "decision to drop the charges" in the Closing Order of the Investigating Judge and the Judgment of the Investigative Parliament.
Article 251 states: "After the dismissal order of the investigating judge or the acquittal judgment of the Investigative Assembly becomes final, if a new charge arises, the investigation may be reopened at the initiative of The prosecutor.
Clarification to the public is necessary to prevent confusion from past publications in which the suspect intends to draw the public's attention in order to protect himself from law enforcement. All complaints of SATHAPANA Bank Plc. Are made for the purpose of taking strict action if there is any misconduct or professional misconduct of any employee without exception or discrimination to ensure that the law is respected and enforced.
The public can be misled by the media by news commentators and suspect defenders to rely on social media and the media for protection, thus undermining law enforcement and possibly impunity. "Proper implementation of the law is fundamental to protecting investors, and especially in the financial sector, to ensure that financial institutions are not at risk of loopholes or lack of attention from law enforcement."
