Bank of Thailand aims to resolve household debt crisis
BANGKOK: The Bank of Thailand aims to reduce chronic debt to ease household burdens and help borrowers get out of the debt cycle faster. According to the Bangkok Post.
"The central bank does not want to see the household sector in a long-term debt cycle," she told the Bangkok Post. "Because the debt cycle is too long, customers may incur too much interest on the principal."
"With this scenario, it would be unfair for some retail lenders at a time when household debt is rising," she said. "However, the central bank will determine the long-term debt after the hearing."
According to the Household Debt Settlement Framework, the Bank of Thailand expects to first implement official guidelines for the RL and RBP to monitor responsible lending by financial institutions. However, the Bank of Thailand will spend more time considering the Debt Service Ratio (DSR) guidelines and deciding whether to implement them. According to the Bangkok Post.
