Dr. Kao Thach Campaigns to Explain the Priority Policy of the Cambodian People's Party to Members in 3 Communes of Khsach Kandal District
Dr. explained the 8-point policy and the key points in the 6-point political program to the chairperson of the activity center to explain to the people in the backyard using simple, easy-to-understand explanations. This policy has been implemented and will continue to be implemented in the new mandate, including:
First, the provision of health care services to vulnerable people and poor families.
Second: Short-term technical training for young people, such as electrical skills, air conditioning skills, construction skills, electronics skills, etc. Who can find a job immediately.
Third, the National Social Assistance Program for Poor Families and Vulnerable Families, which will set up a clear institution in charge that will help address the affected people in a timely manner.
Fourth, the new Royal Government led by the Cambodian People's Party will develop the informal economy so that the informal traders can participate in the economy in a system that will prepare the people as traders, tricycle riders and business people. Self-care and health care services, have a medical certificate or equity card for free treatment.
Sixth: Send agricultural technical officers to communes throughout the country to help train agricultural techniques for farmers to produce rice, potatoes, corn, cashews, vegetables, fruits, animal husbandry, aquaculture, etc. Get high yields, sell at a reasonable price and reduce costs, as well as make a profit, improve your life.
In addition to the sixth point, Dr. also shared the experience of modern farming, especially rice production using modern technology of a rice farm, which greatly reduces costs by using only 30 kg of rice seeds. Farmers traditionally produce 250 to 300 kilograms of rice.
