Vietnamese fertilizer prices fall sharply as manufacturers expand export markets
In addition, China no longer has restrictions on the export of 29 fertilizers. The move has significantly increased the supply of fertilizers in the world market, putting pressure on falling prices to boost consumption.
As a result, the prices of all types of fertilizers have dropped by 60-65 percent from the beginning of last year and are likely to remain stable, maintaining the current low.
In addition, demand for fertilizers also declined as it was not the season for large-scale fertilization, which contributed to falling prices.
To meet these challenges, in addition to its traditional markets such as Japan, South Korea, Malaysia, Cambodia and Laos, many local fertilizer companies have tried to expand their exports to other markets such as Taiwan, Brazil, India and other countries. Southeast Asia and Europe. According to Vietnam news.
