The inauguration ceremony of the Cambodian Swiss System was held on July 4, 2023 with the participation of Ms. Chea Serey, Deputy Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia.
Digital payment transactions have grown significantly through the introduction of new payment services and tools by banks, deposit-taking microfinance institutions and payment service providers such as mobile banking, contactless payment cards, virtual payment cards. The growing popularity of mobile payments and QR codes in the market is showing positive signs towards the digital economy revolution in the country and the world.
In addition, allowing payment service providers to join the CSS system will contribute to improving the financial environment, making the use of financial services easier and more comprehensive, in line with the National Strategy on Financial Environment 2019. 2025.
Mr. Sok Voeun, Chairman of the Board of the Microfinance Association of Cambodia, said that the official launch of the Cambodian Securities system is very important to promote the financial sector as a whole by expanding the scope of operations of banking institutions and Finance.
Through its extensive network of ATMs, all members of the Cambodian Swiss system allow people living in rural areas to access a wide range of banking services, actively contributing to government policies to improve the financial environment. Objects and national economic development.
Mr. Char Sopheap, Chairman of the Payment Committee of the Banking Association of Cambodia, said that the launch of the Cambodian Swiss system in response to the financial sector development strategy 2016-2025 will contribute to the promotion of digital payments and debit. Reduce the use of cash as well as increase transparency in the banking and financial sector and to help promote sustainable and inclusive economic growth.
The CSS system also contributes to preventing the occurrence of eventual occurrence, such as access to counterfeit cash, torn and banknotes with many other problems, the CSS system will also help users save time, confidence and security by Customers can make payments from all private financial institutions, including participating member banks and microfinance institutions across the country.
