(Phnom Penh): Cambodia continues to cooperate with partners to continue the progress of the labor sector, promote workers and promote the export of textiles, clothing, footwear, bags and travel equipment abroad, and also ask partners to help promote progress. From decent working conditions in Cambodia to contribute to the growth of orders and exports.
The American Center for International Labor Solidarity (ACILS) has a mission to focus on the decent living of workers, exercise basic labor rights, and select working conditions and public policies that affect employees. ACILS is an independent organization not affiliated with the United States Government.
During the meeting, the two sides discussed the progress of the labor sector, improving the health and safety of workers and promoting the export of textile products to foreign markets, especially the United States and Europe. Both sides noted that Cambodia is one of the countries that has ratified the most of the ILO conventions, and only Cambodia has a Prime Minister who has met with workers in person and has resolved many issues for them.
Seeing this progress, William Conklin intends to request a renewal of the Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) with the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, as the current Memorandum of Understanding will expire on July 28. 2023 is coming.
William Conklin stated that if the new Memorandum of Understanding is renewed, he would like to further expand cooperation, especially on the promotion of occupational health and safety for workers, traffic safety of workers, minimum wages, social security and protection. Maternity, the elimination of violence and sexual harassment in the workplace, climate change, and so on.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng replied that the above points are in line with the objectives and policies of the Royal Government of Cambodia, while many policies in the field of employment, vocational training, social security and problem solving are Is practiced and continues to be practiced consistently.
He said that after the formation of the seventh government, the Ministry of Labor will continue to cooperate with the ACILS and other partners to implement the policies set out above.
In addition, Minister Ith Sam Heng also praised the ACILS Center for helping to promote the progress of the labor sector by promoting workers with decent working conditions in Cambodia, contributing to the promotion of orders for textile products from Cambodia while ordering products to The United States has seen an increase over previous years.
