Ministry of Education Releases Press Release on Supporting Digital Education Campaign for Students at Phnom Penh Secondary School
(Phnom Penh): In order to improve the quality of students' learning outcomes in the digital age, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports will organize a "Digital Education Support Campaign for Students in Phnom Penh Secondary Schools" which will take place Go in July 2023 at all public high schools in Phnom Penh.
In a statement issued by Fresh News on the afternoon of July 4, 2023, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports said that the campaign will be implemented by the Center for Digital Education and Distance Education by In collaboration with the National Institute of Education, Phnom Penh Pedagogical Institute and the Department of Education, Youth and Sports of Phnom Penh.
Through this campaign, the pedagogical students of the National Institute of Education and the pedagogical students of the Phnom Penh Pedagogical Institute will provide students from 10th to 12th grade by providing training in each classroom directly on the following 6 topics:
1: Exploring learning methods Each student can find a learning method that is suitable for each lesson and subject, as well as a learning method that is appropriate to their personality.
6: Use of mobile applications - Classrooms: Students can access a full range of learning resources (all lessons, all subjects, all levels) mixed (with a variety of videos, worksheets, textbooks, practice books ...). And rich (short learning, learning with questions and answers, learning with video tutorials, self-test).
The campaign will be implemented at 38 public secondary schools in Phnom Penh, and more than 40,000 students studying at the upper secondary level will be trained by 367 student teachers and volunteer teachers who will go directly to class. Study nearly 1,000 rooms.
