(Phnom Penh): The Governor of Phnom Penh, Mr. Khuong Sreng, this morning, July 4, 2023, led the specialized departments and authorities of Tuol Kork district to clean and spray water on Mao Tse Toung Street in Tuol Kork district after suffering Extreme levels of flood danger were announced last night.
Mr. Khuong Sreng instructed the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh and Khan authorities to clean and spray water along some of the roads that were flooded last night, such as Mao Tse Toung Road, Kampuchea Krom Road, 2004 Road and some other roads. It is also important to clean up today to keep Phnom Penh clean and the environment as normal again.
Mr. Sam Piseth confirmed that this morning, July 4, with the guidance and direct inspection along Mao Tse Toung Road, Mr. Khuong Sreng urged the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh to use all workers with the use of vehicles. Spray 18 units of water to clean along Mao Sotong Road, as well as Kampuchea Krom Road and some other roads with mud and rubbish on the road.
He claimed that with heavy rainfall up to 153 mm, the pumping station was able to pump three times as much water as before, pumping water overnight, causing some areas to recede. In that, Kampuchea Krom road was completed at 12 o'clock at night, 2004 road was closed at 1 o'clock at night and Mao Tse Tung road was closed at about 3 o'clock in the morning.
In the morning of the same day, some areas in Boeung Tumpun were still inundated because the area was the lowest. However, under the efforts and attention of the authorities at 11 or 12 today, the water will be able to drain from those areas.
