Listen to the following remarks from people living in Europe: Investment contributes to the development of Cambodia's agricultural sector and the expansion of overseas markets.
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government has considered agriculture as a priority sector that promotes national economic growth and is also a potential sector for attracting investment.
Investment projects in the agricultural sector have been steadily increasing every year, contributing to the development of Cambodia's agricultural sector and expanding exports to foreign markets.
In fact, THACO AGRI is a large-scale agricultural company that is investing in some provinces in Cambodia, and through its investment, it has contributed to the development of the agricultural sector and the expansion of the market for Cambodian products abroad.
Invest in large-scale agricultural production based on organic, industrial management, use of biotechnology and digital mechanisms in appropriate stages. THACO AGRI is establishing two production areas in Kratie and Ratanakkiri provinces.
Aiming to contribute to the development of Cambodia's agricultural industry, THACO AGRI has been investing heavily in infrastructure such as solar energy, roads, irrigation systems, banana packaging plants, etc.
Dr. Ky Sereyvath, President of the Chinese Studies Institute of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that the Cambodian agricultural sector, if we consider the efficiency and quality of the soil, see that Cambodia has great potential, but the challenges in the current agricultural sector are technical factors and support in this field, such as fertilizer. Pesticides and so on.
Dr. continued that the transformation of the Cambodian agricultural market also has some challenges, and for the investment of large companies from abroad will help create some jobs for Cambodians and can absorb agricultural technology and techniques from abroad and benefit. From land lease as well.
Currently, THACO AGRI not only participates in the development of the agricultural sector in Cambodia, but also works with local authorities to promote social activities to improve the lives and services of the company's workers, such as: water supply, electricity, road development, schools, shopping malls. Free primary care, clean water ....
According to the development strategy, THACO AGRI will continue to invest more in agriculture in the Northeast. Currently, the company is developing banana production for cattle to export to international markets, thus providing employment opportunities for Cambodians with a decent salary and many social benefits.
