According to the report of the Capital and Provincial Election Commission (CEC), on the third day, the political parties conducted the election campaign, which was mostly a microphone broadcast at the party headquarters and mobile mobilization in the distribution of leaflets. In the backyard, leaflets in public places and meetings, most of which were conducted by the CPP. At the same time, four political parties marched in the election campaign.
The Cambodian Nationality Party marched in Phnom Penh, the FUNCINPEC party marched in Tbong Khmum, the Khmer Anti-Poverty Party marched in Kampong Speu and the Khmer United National Party marched in Pailin, Kampong Thom and Preah Vihear Province.
Overall, the general situation of the political parties' election campaign on the third day went smoothly, with security, safety, good order and no violence.
