On the morning of June 29, 2023, the Cambodian Senate fully approved the draft amendment to the election law, while the amendment was approved by the National Assembly on June 23, 2023. In essence, the new draft election law will amend eight articles, ranging from sub-national to national elections.
Amendments to the Election Law There are four major articles that the new draft election law is currently amending, ranging from amendments to the National Assembly election, Commune / Sangkat Council elections, Senate elections and elections. Election of Capital, Province, Municipality, District and Khan Council.
Amendments to the Senate Election The draft amendment to 13 new articles, including 23 new articles and related articles of the National Assembly Election Law, shall be applied for the election of senators.
The fourth amendment to the Capital-Provincial Council Election Law stipulates a new Article 15, which requires citizens to participate in the last general election if they wish to stand as a candidate for the council election.
