JERUSALEM (Reuters) - Israel has just approved the purchase of a third US F-35 fighter jet in a deal worth up to $ 3 billion, the Israeli Defense Ministry announced on Sunday. This was released by the AFP news agency on Sunday, July 2, 2023.
The Israeli Defense Ministry said that under the agreement, 25 F-35s would be purchased, which would bring the Israeli Air Force to a total of 75 advanced stealth fighter jets, and that the deal would be finalized. Pay the budget through the defense assistance package that Israel receives from the United States.
Israel is the first country other than the United States to receive F-35 fighter jets. In May 2018, the Israeli air force chief claimed that Israel was the first country to use the aircraft in actual combat.
