Today, as the global economy slows and the Ukraine crisis worsens, the United States really needs to engage with China in many areas. After Blinken's visit to China, the United States announced that US Treasury Secretary Yellen may visit China in early July to restore ties with China.
Whether China-US relations can ease tensions China has made its position clear and, more importantly, depends on what Washington will do. As the Chinese Foreign Ministry said, "Communication must address the concerns of both sides, must be effective and resolve non-communicative issues, but also to the detriment of the interests of the two sides. "
Comment: China enacts "Foreign Relations Law" to show the world that China adheres to peace, development, cooperation and win-win
As the world enters a period of turmoil and change, the positive energy emitted by this law will make the world better aware of China, know China and trust China.
