Samdech Techo Hun Sen said: "In the sixth legislature of the National Assembly, the Royal Government led by the Cambodian People's Party, with me, His Majesty the Prime Minister, has strongly defended the peace, stability, security and social order that "Ensure the peaceful living of the people, socio-economic development and the strengthening of democracy."
At the same time, the President of the Cambodian People's Party stated that the rights and freedoms of the people are respected, protected and promoted, and the economic, social, cultural, educational, health, employment and other sectors are more developed, and the living standards of the people are better. Ascending.
Maintaining political stability throughout the country under the umbrella of peace, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that many new achievements include: roads, bridges, irrigation systems, water supply, water wells, electricity, information systems, factories, farms, small and large construction, business centers. Schools, hospitals, pagodas, etc. Built and expanded in both urban and rural areas and border areas. No base is remote, inaccessible and undeveloped.
In addition, Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that in the face of the epidemic of Kovid 19, the Royal Government has successfully led the fight against this deadly disease, saved the lives of the people, and maintained the livelihood and economic balance. And enable the national economy to recover rapidly after the 19-Kovid crisis and return to the path of potential growth.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued that the Royal Government has also introduced and effectively implemented various policy measures to promote production, increase employment and employment of the people, strengthen the expansion of public services, strengthen justice, equity and social harmony, as well as promote protection. Society for all people, especially the poor and vulnerable in spirit, does not abandon any Cambodian citizen.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that in this sense, the upcoming 7th National Assembly election on July 23, 2023 is a historical political event that is extremely important to our nation. The political decision of the people in this election to choose which party to continue to lead the country is limited to the future destiny of our nation and our people.
(Kratie): Mr. Prum Sokha, Chairman of Kratie Provincial Assistance Team and Mr. Vathon, President of Kratie Provincial CPP, Kratie Provincial CPP leaders this morning, July 1, 2023, led CPP members. 29,100 Cambodians are campaigning for the 7th National Assembly election, the first day of the election campaign.
Leaders of all members gathered to listen to the voice message of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party before the march, while in other districts also organized the event with a large number of participants. .
