The first day of the campaign! Khoy Rida Launches Large-Scale Election Campaign in Pursat City with More Than 5,000 Members
(Pursat): In the first day of the campaign! Mr. Khoy Rida, Governor of the Provincial Board of Governors, Chairman of the Provincial Party Committee and Chairman of the Pursat Municipal Assistance Team, this morning, July 1, 2021, led more than 5,000 CPP members in the seven Sangkats in Pursat City. To launch the election campaign for the 7th legislative election.
During this morning's election campaign, Khoy Rida told the people that voting for the Cambodian People's Party is to ensure local development, improve livelihoods, have adequate infrastructure, bridges, roads, people have access to fast and quality public services. Access to quality schools, hospitals and medical services ensures local security, safety and order.
At the same time, Mr. Khoy Rida called on all registered voters to go to the polls to vote for the 18th Cambodian People's Party, which has the symbol of the angel throwing flowers as a symbol on July 23. The coming year 2023.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's speech was made during the opening ceremony of the 7th National Assembly election campaign and commemorating the 72nd anniversary of the founding of the Cambodian People's Party on the morning of July 1, 2023.
At the same time, to ensure the protection and promotion of the interests of the people, Samdech Techo Hun Sen will promote the effective implementation of the following priority policies:
1: Provide public services to the people in a transparent, easy and reliable manner, continue to implement free of charge on birth registration, marriage registration, death list, provision of residence book, family book and identity card of Khmer nationality.
2: Continue to avoid taxing family farmland, help farmers to expand production and find markets to sell agricultural products at reasonable prices, allocate land and provide land ownership to poor landless families who have complied with social land concessions, prevent Illegally occupy all types of state land and continue to provide land to people living and enjoying the location of state land in accordance with the principles set by the state.
4: Promote the implementation of the policy of safe villages, communes and sangkats, continue to develop all communes / sangkats to have better communication roads by regularly repairing and maintaining new roads, building new roads and improving roads from dirt roads to Paved or concrete roads, adequate electricity and water supply, better irrigation and quality telecommunication services.
6: Promote the provision of quality, safe, effective and equitable health care services to the people. Expand primary schools to all villages, expand secondary schools to all communes and increase high schools in districts, provide young people with opportunities for vocational training and employment.
7: At the same time, Samdech will set out six priority policy programs in the political program of the Royal Government of the 7th legislature of the National Assembly, including:
* Program 2: Vocational and technical training for more than 1.5 million young people from poor and vulnerable families across the country at state vocational training institutions at the degree level. Technical and Vocational Level 1 Free tuition and monthly stipend.
Program 6: Deployment of technical officers to provide agricultural services to all rural communes throughout the country to promote agricultural productivity and assist farmers' families in promoting their agricultural products.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia, the 7th legislature, will also organize farmers' associations in rural areas to maintain the strength of farmers in production as well as the sale of agricultural products with buyers.
(Kampong Speu): On the morning of July 1, 2023, the Chairman of the Central Working Group for Kampong Speu Province of the Cambodian People's Party, Mr. Chhay Thorn, Mr. Hun Many, Member of Parliament for Kampong Speu and Mr. Vy Samnang, Chairman of the Provincial People's Party. Announcing the opening of the election campaign for the 7th National Assembly election in 2023, with more than 5,000 members gathered at the Independence Monument, Samdech Sangka Chuon Nath Park, Chbar Morn City.
