Mr. Eang Sophalleth considers veterans as an important driving force in contributing to the implementation of Samdech Techo's win-win policy to make Cambodia peaceful
(Tbong Khmum): Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Chairman of the Working Group of the Local Party in Oreang Ov District, Tbong Khmum Province, considered the uncle, aunt, brother, veteran brother as an important driving force in contributing to the implementation of the win-win policy of Samdech Techo brings peace, development and prestige to Cambodia throughout the country and on the international stage.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth made this remark during a meeting and awarding medals to more than 200 veterans across Ou Raing Ov district, Tbong Khmum province on Friday, June 30, 2023.
The event was attended by Mr. Lam Chhorn, Member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Deputy Chairman of the District Working Group, Ms. San Arun, Member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Deputy Chairman of the District Working Group, Mr. Chairman, Vice-Chairman, Member of Party Working Group, Oreang Ov District, Tbong Khmum Province.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth asked Uncle Ming to help promote and fill our shortcomings as recipients of the peace from the sacrifice of fresh meat, fresh blood, uncle, aunt, former siblings Warriors who have gone through all the flavors of war because "young children walk fast, old men know the way."
He said that in return for the merits of all veterans, we, the Ou Raing Ov team, are committed to maintaining peace, contributing to development and continuing to build achievements for the next generation.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth also wished uncles, aunts, brothers and sisters, all veterans good health and long life to see the continued prosperity of our motherland. General knowledge: Who created the first world map and how did the world map evolve?
(Phnom Penh): Before the creation of the full world map, people were only able to draw maps for their country or the landscape around them, such as the sky, stars, forests, mountains, rivers, seas and cities, but later people also developed the ability Able to map the whole world and easy to use up to date.
Later, many Greek scholars continued to refine the world map in the shape of a round earth as they highlighted Greece in the center of the map, surrounded by the sea like Greece. They are at the center of the universe, too.
On the world map, the Greeks identified only two continents, Europe and Asia. What is special about the previous maps is that they added longitudinal and transverse lines as well as the North Pole (looking directly at the earth) on their map. Compared to the world map of Anarchimander, the map of the next generation is easier to see than just the division of the continent is not yet accurate.
By the time of the exploration of new lands, especially during the European colonial period, the maritime navigation sector had grown so much that they were able to define the world map more clearly, and they had worked hard to develop the ability to process this world map even more. Clearer and easier to use.
Later, the world also reached the modern age, people can build air balloons, can fly airplanes, can even build satellites, thus making the world map even more accurate. This achievement clears the skepticism of humankind in setting the world map after more than ten thousand years of continuous creation and processing.
