Mr. Kao Muy Thong, Deputy Secretary General of the Council for Agricultural and Rural Development, made the remarks at the opening of the workshop on Food System and Food Rights on June 30, 2023, co-organized by the International Institute. Rural Rehabilitation of Cambodia (IIRR-Cambodia) and development partners.
Mr. Kao Muy Thong said that for all of us, there is a lot of understanding about the "food system", which covers all activities, processes and actors involved in food production, that is, it has been involved since the production of food from Production and processing up to distribution, use and management of waste.
"The food system is interconnected with components and stages that contribute to the overall functioning of the food supply chain," said Kao Muy Thong.
He added that understanding of the food system is important to address challenges related to food security, sustainability, nutrition and equity. It involves evaluating and improving efficiency, resilience and fairness to ensure an adequate, safe, nutritious and culturally appropriate food supply for all of us.
This course will focus on the basic concepts of the food system, the right to food through the United Nations Declaration on the Rights of Farmers and Other People Living in Rural Areas, and the Voluntary Guidelines for the Food System. And nutrition. The training workshop will also examine and discuss in depth the specific context of the food system in Cambodia.
