National Bank of Cambodia plans to expand cross-border payment system to 5 more countries
(Phnom Penh): The National Bank of Cambodia (NBC) has been working to expand the development of cross-border payment systems with five more countries, including Vietnam, Laos, Myanmar, China and India, to promote the use of local currency instead of the dollar in trade. Karma and investment between trading partners.
Please be informed that the National Bank of Cambodia has recently successfully launched the Cambodia-Thailand cross-border payment system.
This is according to Dr. Chea Serey, Deputy Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, in the dissemination workshop on "Riel, Financial Knowledge and Bakong System" held on June 30, 2023 in Santuk District, Kampong Thom Province.
Dr. Chea Serey said that Cambodia is connected to Thailand and Malaysia, as Cambodians can scan payments in Thailand from their riel accounts in Cambodia, and Thais can also scan payments in riel in Cambodia. Well.
"This mechanism requires Cambodian buyers and sellers to have riel accounts. This is also a factor in promoting the use of the riel in Cambodia," she said.
Dr. Chea Serey added that the National Bank of Cambodia has also been cooperating with many other countries in Asia, including Africa, Latin America and Europe, to increase the scope of secure, low-cost and cash payment systems. Urgently aim to support and promote tourism, investment, trade and remittances of the Cambodian people, especially workers working abroad.
She stated that the demand for the riel has increased steadily, reflecting the increase in the riel in circulation with an average annual growth rate of 16.6% from about 356 billion riel in 1998 to 14.1 trillion riel in 2022. .
