"Although we all have a duty to protect, we must not forget to rush to the polls to fulfill our duty as good citizens in society." Experts show the procedure for applying for a free health check card for staff at Karaoke, Beer Garden, Bar and Massage (Video inside)
(Phnom Penh): Individuals working in the informal economy tourism services, especially women working in bars, discos, karaoke, beer gardens, massage parlors and spas, are receiving consideration and attention. From the Royal Government of Cambodia to be like those who work in the economy in the system as workers.
Considering the same with workers, the Royal Government has now decided to provide health care through the Health Equity Fund system by providing free health check-ups. This card is valid for individuals working in the informal economy tourism services, valid for one year, and after expiration, if they do not change jobs, it can be renewed.
For the procedure to obtain a Health Equity Fund (MSF) card, the employer or business owner of an institution in the field of informal economy tourism must prepare a list of persons working in the field of informal economy tourism in the enterprise. The institution shall be sent to the Capital-Province or Municipality, District or Khan for verification before submitting to the National Social Security Fund for registration.
Individuals who do not work under an employment contract (those who do not receive a salary from the site owner, ie receive a fee from guests directly) in the field of tourism services of the informal economy have the right to apply for a health equity fund card directly to the Capital Administration. Provinces or municipalities, districts, and Khans for verification before submitting to the National Social Security Fund for registration.
The state is responsible for the costs of providing individual health care services in bars, discos, karaoke, beer gardens, massage parlors and spas. This consideration is made in order to ensure income security, reduce economic and financial vulnerabilities, aim to reduce and prevent the decline of poverty to the maximum for all people.
