Cambodia hopes China to increase rice purchases by 500,000 tonnes
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Lon Yeng, Secretary General of the Cambodian Rice Federation, told Cambodia-China Friendship Radio on June 29, 2023 that so far, Cambodia and China have signed a Memorandum of Understanding on the export of Cambodian rice to the market. China has already met six times and is preparing to sign a seventh Memorandum of Understanding (MOU), which also plans to increase rice exports.
This statement was made at the same time as the Minister of Commerce of Cambodia, HE Pan Sosak, just said at the end of June that the Ministry of Commerce has been negotiating the procedure for the signing of the 7th Memorandum of Understanding to increase imports. 500,000 tons of rice for 2023-2024, which is scheduled to be signed in the near future. HE Pan Sosak added that he hopes that this proposal will help increase Cambodia's rice exports even more.
However, Lon Yeng, secretary-general of the Cambodian Rice Federation, confirmed that the exact timing of the signing of the 500,000-tonne memorandum of understanding was still up to the Chinese side to decide. Trade has made such a request to the Chinese side through the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and through the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia, pending further response.
