Prakas on the capital, regulations of depository banks and financial institutions, aims to strengthen the capital and resilience of depository banks and financial institutions to withstand various risks, especially credit risk, operational risk and market risk, to protect depositors Deposit investors and stabilize the business of the institution as well as the entire banking system.
At the same time, the Prakas on Credit Risk for the Capital Sufficiency Ratio of Deposit-Taking Banks and Financial Institutions has also been prepared with the aim of establishing a comprehensive range of credit risk balancing measures. The type of loan and the borrower or counterparty will reflect the level of risk that the institution may actually face in order to strengthen the effectiveness of risk management.
There is special attention to:
1: Support and encourage lending to small and medium enterprises with proper registration and appropriate financial statements by weighing only 75% so that they can get credit at the rate Appropriate interest from banking and financial institutions will also contribute to strengthening the implementation of the General Department of Taxation's tax collection measures for those enterprises through a mechanism to encourage informal enterprises to enter the formal system.
2. Support for credit guarantee mechanisms established by the Royal Government of Cambodia, such as the Cambodian Credit Guarantee Corporation (CGCC), with a zero-percentage risk rating on secured credit portfolios to facilitate access to more capital for small and medium enterprises. Before.
3. Support for agriculture, education and people's well-being through mitigation of risk at 85% for loans of reasonable size, which provides physical support for the purchase of housing for the purpose of accommodation through mitigation.
4. Implement a strict loan-to-value ratio (LTV) for loans to the real estate sector, aiming to improve the implementation of international standards, maintain financial stability and encourage property developers to register as legal entities. Contribute to strengthen the implementation of tax collection measures of the General Department of Taxation.
5. Credit risk assessment Supporting and encouraging green financing by easing the risk balance by only 80% during the ongoing project and encouraging investment in information technology of banking and financial institutions.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen: The Amendment to the Election Law is Not a Restriction of the Rights of the People, but to Protect the Peace and the Implementation of the Rights of the Citizens (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia That the preparation of the amendment to the election law now is not to deprive the rights of the people, but to protect the peace and the exercise of the rights of the people.
The remarks came after a small number of political parties and civil society organizations criticized the preparation of amendments to the election law regarding the definition of obligations for those who wish to stand for election.
During a meeting with nearly 7,000 workers from 10 factories in Pursat province this morning, June 30, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said: “You see in the law that the Senate voted yesterday. "(Approve) In addition to strengthening the responsibilities of your candidates, check the penalties, there are still restrictions on your political right not to vote, maybe even for life."
The draft amendment to the election law was prepared by the Royal Government of Cambodia and was fully approved by the National Assembly on June 19, 2023 and fully supported by the Senate on June 29 yesterday.
The amendment comes after extremist opposition groups led by Sam Rainsy and his cronies launched a new campaign urging registered Cambodians not to go to the polls or cast their ballots for Sunday's election. This coming July 23.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen added, "Because you have been exploring, legal measures have been taken not to deprive citizens of their rights, but to protect the safety of the people, the process of exercising their rights." Look at the law, go out, you are disappointed.
