Pentagon: Chinese spy balloon does not collect data while flying in US airspace (Video inside) (Washington): The Pentagon on Thursday said that a Chinese balloon that was shot down by US warplanes. In the airspace over the Atlantic Ocean in February, no data or intelligence was collected while flying over the United States. This was released by the AFP news agency on Friday, June 30, 2023.
On Feb. 4, the U.S. military shot down a Chinese balloon that the Pentagon called a spy balloon off the coast of South Carolina and retrieved it from the Atlantic Ocean for study. Then come. China has strongly condemned the United States for shooting down its balloon, which Beijing claims is just a civilian balloon.
