This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen met with workers in Pursat province before taking a break during the election campaign.
(Pursat): On the morning of Friday, June 30, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, met with a total of 6,868 workers. From 10 factories in Pursat province.
Today's meeting is the 19th meeting since May 22, 2023 and also the last meeting before Samdech Techo took a break in the election campaign. Samdech Techo announced that he will continue to meet with workers after the election.
During the mission to meet the workers in the first round, Samdech Techo Prime Minister had already met with the workers in Pursat province once in 2019.
According to Dr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, the 10 factories that allow workers to join the conversation with Samdech Techo are located in Pursat City, Krakor District and Bakan District.
These 10 factories have 3 garment factories, 5 electronics factories, 1 car assembly and 1 agricultural product.
Efforts to find jobs for the people are an essential policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia. In addition to providing jobs for the people, the Royal Government is also thinking about how to reduce the difficulties of people who go to work far from home?
Starting from this reason, in 1999, Samdech Techo Hun Sen set out a policy to deploy factories in the provinces to provide jobs near people's homes.
In the first round of the meeting, Samdech Techo Prime Minister recommended 10 tips to facilitate the investment environment, provide a lot of promotion of rights, benefits and social protection to the workers that the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has been Cooperate with ministries and institutions to implement successfully.
After missing out on years for the 19-year epidemic of Kovid. Samdech Techo Hun Sen also launched a program to meet workers in the second round, starting on May 22, 2023.
For the second round of 19 meetings, Samdech Techo met with a total of nearly 340,000 workers.
In the second meeting with workers on May 22, 2023, Samdech Techo announced the implementation of the old program, new activities and expand the scope for pregnant workers and children under 2 years old.
The garment industry is an important part of boosting the national economy and providing jobs for the people. Under the potential policy of the Royal Government, the garment industry has been growing steadily.
According to a report by the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, in 1997 there were only 64 garment factories in Cambodia, employing about 80,000 workers and exporting about 227 million US dollars.
By 2023, the number of garment factories will increase to 1,326, with an estimated 840,000 workers (660,000 women). Exports reached 13 billion US dollars. Through employment in the garment sector, people are guaranteed a monthly income and a better life.
