(Prey Veng): General Dr. Neth Savoeun, General Commissioner of the National Police and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group visited Kanhchriech and Svay Antor districts in Prey Veng province on the afternoon of June 29, 2023, presided over the inauguration of six school buildings. 4 rooms and bathrooms in Hun Sen Svay Antor High School, located in Svay Antor District, Prey Veng Province.
To begin with, General Dr. Neth Savoeun received a courtesy call from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior, and Chairman of the Prey Veng Provincial Working Group. Best wishes to all the people.
General Neth Savoeun also mentioned Cambodia's success in hosting the ASEAN Summit and related summits, especially the hosting of the recently concluded SEA Games and ASEAN Para Games. Recently, with national pride under the roof of peace and development of the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The General Commissioner of the National Police confirmed that the inaugurated educational institution is now a breeding ground for important human resources that are most needed for the development of the country, along with other areas such as economic infrastructure. All are important and necessary for our country to move forward and compete with developed countries in the international arena.
General Neth Savoeun also mentioned the important contribution of teachers, comparing them to the heart of the restoration, development and backbone of the education sector. The general continued that teachers have worked hard to train and develop human resources with ethics, as well as educate children and youth to have moral discipline in society to become a potential bamboo vine.
At the same time, on behalf of the General Commissioner of the National Police, General Dr. Neth Savoeun reminded and instructed the parents to cooperate well with the authorities, competent forces, teachers by educating, explaining and instructing students about the effects of drugs. Addicts understand the tricks of inciting criminals to avoid falling into the trap of drugs, and young people must say no to drugs, do not want to know, do not want to try and do not get involved at all.
Regarding traffic, General Neth Savoeun did not forget to advise all students and citizens to respect all traffic laws by driving on the right, riding a motorcycle, wearing a helmet and driving a car with a seat belt and not driving. Exceeding the speed limit. For parents to help educate their children before leaving home or school must be reminded to respect traffic laws.
General Dr. Neth Savoeun urged and issued orders for all levels of authorities, competent forces and people to continue to work together to implement the Royal Government's policy of safe villages, communes and sangkats more effectively. Aims to maintain security, order, eliminate gangsters and prevent crimes. On the other hand, when it is time for students to leave school, they need to facilitate traffic in schools.
In addition, General Dr. Neth Savoeun also called on all people whose names are on the voter list to go to the polls for the 7th National Assembly election to be held on July 23, 2023. Everyone, too, to elect a leader who can maintain peace and continue to develop. In addition, we must work together to maintain the peace that Cambodia has today in order to continue its development.
On that occasion, General Neth Savoeun, Head of the Royal Government Working Group in Svay Antor District, also announced the donation of a 6-room school building to Thlao Primary School at a cost of about $ 100,000 through Mr. Ros Neng, a businessman from Svay Antor District. National Anti-Corruption Council Holds 24th Meeting of the Third Mandate
