Social Security Regulator Increases Dissemination of Social Security System Development to Promote Social Welfare
(Phnom Penh): The Social Security Regulator has organized an outreach forum on "Development of the social security system and its impact on social and economic welfare" in order to promote the development of the social security system in Cambodia from its inception to the present and to understand the impact on Social and economic well-being to the public and stakeholders more widely.
The forum also brings together experts from the University of Finland, Professor of Social Policy, and Professor of Social Security and Labor Law, University of Vilnius, Lithuania to share their valuable experiences at the forum.
Dr. John Narith said that the development of the social security system is very important to improve social welfare by ensuring access to health services, maintaining security, safety and appropriate levels of income, reducing Economic and financial vulnerabilities of the people, as well as contribute to economic activity by mobilizing financial resources (savings) for domestic investment.
Mr. Leng Soklong, Representative of the Social Security Regulator, stated that the key reforms introduced by the Royal Government are in accordance with the guidelines of the National Social Protection Policy Framework 2016-2025, which are related to the strengthening of the social security system in the past. Includes:
Establishment of the Health Equity Fund in 2017 for the health expenditures of poor households (approximately three million) and individuals working in the informal economy (approximately 100,000)
Establishment of a health expenditure certification agency in 2017, covering the cost of health services using the Health Equity Fund
* Establishment of social security system for occupational risk for public officials and health care for public officials, ex-civil servants and veterans in 2017
* Restructuring of the new functions, duties and structure of the National Social Security Fund into a public administrative institution in 2019
* Establishment of the Social Security Regulator in 2021
* Implementation of the social security pension system for the private sector by 2022
Establishment of the National Social Assistance Fund, which is partly organized by merging the functions of the National Social Security Fund for Civil Servants and the National Veterans Fund in 2022.
