The Royal Academy of Cambodia holds a lecture on "Responsibility and Irresponsibility in Criminal Matters"
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Academy of Cambodia on the morning of June 29, 2023, organized a lecture on "Responsibility and Irresponsibility in Criminal Matters" to share lessons learned at the Tonle Sap Hall, Khmer Vito Building of the Royal Academy of Cambodia.
The event was presided over by Dr. Ek Chheng Huot, a member of the Reserve Academy and the Royal Prosecutor of Takeo Provincial Court, Dr. Chhit Bunthong, the facilitator, as well as many officers and students.
On this occasion, Dr. Ek Chheng Huot, the criminal liability is as follows:
* First, non-criminal liability due to juvenile causes (Articles 39 to 81/161 to 166) refers to minors aged 14 to under 18 years old: * Principle: Substitution of criminal measures by Follow-up Measures, Education Measures, Protective Measures and Support Measures * Special Cases (Circumstances of Offenses or Personalities of Minors): Courts may declare criminal penalties for minors * Penalties for Minors: Articles 160 to 166.
* Second: Individuals with dementia (Article 31) Complete loss of responsibility: Complete loss of the ability to understand and judge the legal consequences of their actions is not criminally liable.
* Third: State (Public Legal Entity) Article 42: In principle, in cases specified in the law and other legal norms, legal entities may be declared criminally liable for crimes committed by the organization or Its representatives for the benefit of that legal entity.
* Any person who commits an act prescribed or permitted by law, that person does not commit an offense.
* Any person who commits an act on the orders of a legitimate authority, that person does not commit an offense, unless this act is clearly illegal.
* Preliminary: In the case of genocide, crimes against humanity or war crimes, the above acts of justice cannot be exempted from its criminal liability.
* Fifth: Legal protection (Article 33 and Article 34) Conditions of legal protection: * There is an illegal or illegal invasion * Protection must be necessary, this necessity must be in a state * None Asymmetry between the means of defense used and the weight of the aggression.
Seventh: Legal Protection (Articles 33 and 34) Effect of legal protection: Any person who commits an offense in a state of legal protection is not criminally liable, meaning that the person is not liable. Be any criminal.
Eighth: Necessary situation (Article 35) Necessary condition: * Existence of danger that is happening or will occur. * Necessary to protect oneself, protect others or protect property against danger. * There is no disproportion between Ways to prevent the weight of the accident.
9th: The power of force or coercion (Hatra 36) Conditions of force or coercion include: Force or coercion must result from unintentional events, force or coercion must be unpredictable, force Or coercion must be irresistible or unavoidable. Activists of the Candle Light Party, Ampil Commune, Kampong Siem District, Decided to Drop the Party Label in Front of the House
