Minister of Commerce: Draft National Intellectual Property Policy will be a driving force for economic development, trade, industry, culture, tourism and agriculture
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce and Chairman of the National Committee for Intellectual Property Management, stated that in 2023, the National Committee for the Management of Intellectual Property, with the Department of Intellectual Property as the Secretariat, has completed the draft of the National Intellectual Property Policy. 2023-2028 and ready to submit to the upcoming plenary session of the Council of Ministers.
He said that the draft national policy on intellectual property has a vision to develop the intellectual property system in Cambodia to become a driving force on economic development, trade, industry, culture, tourism and agriculture through the promotion of intellectual property protection. Brand names and products of the Kingdom of Cambodia, the creation of cultural works, inventions, genetic resources, traditional knowledge and cultural norms.
The draft National Intellectual Property Policy also promotes the use of intellectual property to promote research and development in product development, technology, innovation, innovation and the cultural industry in response to the digital economy and society, as well as the Industrial Revolution. Fourth, to contribute to the achievement of the vision of the Kingdom of Cambodia 2050.
This statement was made by the Minister on the morning of Thursday, June 29, 2023, during the meeting to review the results of intellectual property work in 2022 and work direction 2023 of the National Committee for Intellectual Property Management (CCI). To respect, report to Samdech Techo Prime Minister and review the draft sub-decree on administrative measures for the implementation of intellectual property rights.
The meeting was attended by members of the National Committee for the Management of Intellectual Property, members of the Secretariat of the National Committee for the Management of Intellectual Property, leaders and officials of the Ministry of Commerce.
On this occasion, the Minister thanked and appreciated the members of the National Committee for Intellectual Property Management and the members of the Secretariat of the National Committee for Intellectual Property Management for their hard work and pride to achieve results. Achieved many important achievements, including:
He said the agreements would be a potential new impetus and new opportunity in Asia and the Middle East, which would be a testament to the country's comprehensive recognition of the country's development. Cambodia is prosperous and peaceful in the digital age.
At the same time, in order to achieve more important achievements to further develop the Cambodian intellectual property sector to be more prosperous and efficient, the Minister requested all members of the National Committee for Intellectual Property Management to continue to implement the following important work directions:
Promote the registration of geographical trademarks of Koh Kong, Prahok, Koh Kong, Prahok, Siem Reap and complete the registration of trademarks of Pursat Orange, Silver, Copper, Kandal Province and Cambodian Ear Spit. * Promote the broadcast on radio, television and other media through national and international programs of registered geographical and collective brands to become tourism and cultural destinations.
* Continue to amend laws and prepare laws and regulations in accordance with the agreements of which Cambodia is a member and in line with the actual development of society, as well as strengthen the implementation of intellectual property laws more effectively.
* Promote education, training and public awareness of intellectual property, especially examining the possibility of integrating intellectual property curricula in vocational education and training institutions.
