Samdech Techo Association for the Development of Small and Medium Enterprises in Cambodia Requests Those Who Have the Title of Duke Oknha to Wear Official Uniforms in Legal Places
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Association for the Development of Small and Medium Enterprises in Cambodia, headed by Duke Te Tang Po, paid a courtesy call on Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, to present the progress of the work of the Samdech Foundation Association. Techo for the development of small and medium enterprises in Cambodia achieved on the afternoon of June 28, 2023.
In this courtesy call, Tycoon Te Tang Po mentioned the Royal Government's sub-decree to authorize the Samdech Techo Foundation Association for the Development of Small and Medium Enterprises in Cambodia to cut uniforms, medals and necklaces for the recipients. Honored all the tycoons and tycoons in Cambodia for use during national festivals, national traditions and other official ceremonies.
According to a sub-decree signed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on November 15, 2021, the official uniforms, badges, badges and necklaces worn on the uniforms of the Duke and Duke were inspected. Prepared and provided in accordance with the guidelines set by the Samdech Techo Association for the Development of Small and Medium Enterprises in Cambodia.
Tycoon Te Tang Po said that the uniforms of the Duke and Duke were designed by experts of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts and approved by the Ministry of Interior and with the approval of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. Issued as a sub-decree on November 15, 2021.
He added that after receiving the right from the Royal Government to cut the uniforms, the Samdech Techo Association for the Development of Small and Medium Enterprises in Cambodia has cut the uniforms to 350 tycoons and tycoons in Cambodia.
He stated that the cutting of the dress was done only for the duke and the duke who had a royal decree from the King, because this is a national representative uniform.
He added that although the Royal Government had issued a sub-decree authorizing associations to cut uniforms for all tycoons in Cambodia, there were still some individuals who had forged uniforms.
He urged those who cut the uniforms of the fake duke to stop this activity so as not to damage the honor of the duke given by the king.
It should also be informed that according to the sub-decree of Samdech Techo, it is stated that anyone who uses or falsifies the official uniform, badge, medal, necklace for wearing on the uniform of the Duke and Duke will be punished according to the law in force.
