Ministry of National Defense holds a meeting to review the results of the first half of the year and raise the direction for the second half of 2023
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of June 29, 2023, the Ministry of National Defense held a meeting to review the results of the first half and raise the direction for the second half of 2023.
The meeting was held at the Ministry of National Defense under the chairmanship of General Neang Phat, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of National Defense, with the participation of the leadership of the Ministry of National Defense, the Commander-in-Chief and subordinate units. Also.
At the meeting, General Neang Phat emphasized the recent political events, including the implementation of the election law, which aims to strengthen and enhance the responsibility of politicians to stand for election. In a democratic society that does not affect the people's right to vote.
Regarding the issue of drones flying over the Cambodian border in Ratanakkiri province, the General considered that it was a serious violation of Cambodian sovereignty, which the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces must respond to. Absolutely not tolerant.
The appeal of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia because these days there are a series of abuses by drones that do not know where to launch into Cambodian territory.
Speaking during a visit to nearly 20,000 workers in Ang Snoul district on the morning of June 29, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also publicly announced that there were no drones flying into Cambodia last night.
According to Samdech Techo, sometimes launching a drone is an act of terrorism that ASEAN must work together in case there is terrorism in any ASEAN member country, because drones can now kill people. Samdech Techo reminded that an Iranian army chief was killed by the United States by a drone of Donald Trump.
Please be informed that the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation on June 28, 2023 issued a statement stating that "the entry of drones into Cambodian airspace is a gross violation and can not be tolerated. "Bow down to the sovereignty and territorial integrity of Cambodia."
The Ministry said that in the spirit of adhering to the sovereignty and principles of not allowing any enemy force to use its territory against friendly neighbors, Cambodia has been cooperating closely with the Vietnamese authorities and armed forces in Preventing such crimes from happening again.
The statement added that after the violence, Cambodia also received information from the authorities and law enforcement forces along the provinces bordering Vietnam, namely Ratanakiri and Mondulkiri provinces that there are drones. drones) fly into Cambodian airspace frequently from June 27, 2023.
The actions of this unidentified group are a grave and intolerable violation of Cambodia's sovereignty and territorial integrity. The Royal Government of Cambodia has exercised its right to self-defense and to take strict and appropriate military action to prevent the drone re-entry into Cambodian airspace. This is according to the additional confirmation of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.
According to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, in case of finding the real source of the drones, the Royal Government of Cambodia will take further legal and diplomatic measures to protest this invasion of Cambodia's sovereignty and territorial integrity.
