Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khi praises the progress of the private security sector, which contributes to maintaining security and social order
(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. E Sok Khi, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, highly appreciated and praised the progress of the private security sector in Cambodia, especially under the attention, support and capacity building of private security agencies from the Department of Management. Private Security of the General Commission of the National Police.
The remarks of Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khi were made on the evening of June 28, 2023, on the occasion of the visit of the representative of General Santeth Dr. Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner General, to close the 50th Private Security Agency Training Course of the Department. Manage private security with 129 participants (4 females), including 5 deputy police chiefs of the department.
The Deputy National Police Commissioner considered that the training of private security agencies is necessary as well as a priority work of the Department of Private Security Management to strengthen the capacity and quality of private security agencies to participate in maintaining law and order. Society, while private security agencies are the main support force of the authorities.
Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khi also claimed that in the past, the General Commission of the National Police, which has the Department of Private Security Management as its staff, has been taking care to ensure that all private security agencies have the capacity, professional knowledge and ethics to raise Elevation to this sector for continuous growth.
At the same time, he also introduced some important work as follows:
* First: Request private security agents to have the appropriate attitude to participate in the work by adhering to what is right after training to respect the qualifications of private security agents to be disciplined, ethical, use private security uniforms And adequate equipment.
* Second: To establish cooperation with the authorities and local authorities: good citizens and good people, an important support force to the competent authorities, good cooperation, timely response. (When you see or suspect any illegal activity, whether in your standing position or where to report immediately to the competent authorities or the department directly by phone or to jointly prevent and Crack down on crime in time).
* Third: Participate in the implementation of the policy of the Royal Government, especially the policy of safe villages, communes and sangkats.
* Fourth: Directors of private security companies and institutions (continue to support the training) by sending private security agents to attend the training.
* Fifth: All participants must apply the knowledge gained from this study and continue to expand their knowledge, intelligence, creativity and high responsibility in fulfilling their roles.
He also called on all private security agencies on the voter list to prepare sufficient documents and go to the 7th National Assembly election to be held on July 23, 2023. Face to everyone as well.
On that occasion, Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey, Director of the Private Security Management Department of the General Commission of the National Police, said that at present, there are 50 training courses for private security agents with 8,709 private security trainee trainees (202 females). 198) National Police trainees (12 females).
He said that the training is aimed at meeting the needs of capacity building to become a qualified and qualified private security agent for participation in the maintenance and protection of stability, security, safety, order and age. People's lives as well as improve the policy of safe villages, communes and sangkats.
