(Phnom Penh): On Thursday, June 29, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, paid a courtesy call on a total of 18,255 workers. From 11 factories in Ang Snoul district, Kandal province.
The following are the main remarks of Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of visiting nearly 20,000 workers in Ang Snoul district, Kandal province:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that social protection policies have been put in place in response to the well-being of the people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen continues to call for joint security at factories to prevent drug trafficking and HIV transmission.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls for joint peacekeeping to ensure sustainable development.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the war had destroyed Cambodia, but the Cambodian people worked together to put out the flames of war.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen encourages people to work together to eradicate poverty.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen told the workers that if the factory closes, the workers will be the first to suffer because they are unemployed.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls on workers to go to the polls on July 23 and ban alcohol.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that women who are civil servants and contracted receive financial support from the time of pregnancy until the child is 2 years old.
