The business environment remains challenging and many companies are struggling to access foreign exchange, trade licenses, import raw materials and services, Bloomberg reported, citing a WB report for Myanmar released on Tuesday. Adapt to logical constraints.
The assessment is a sign of dissatisfaction with Myanmar, which the WB said showed the country showed "temporary signs of stability" in the first half of 2023. Among the positives for Myanmar that the ADB has seen include a broadly stable exchange rate, a slowdown in inflation and an uptrend in various economic indicators.
However, the WB said exporters were facing problems ranging from declining external demand, overpriced official exchange rates and tighter currency requirements.
