(Kampong Thom): On the afternoon of June 28, 2023, the Kampong Thom Military Operations Area Command held a repatriation ceremony for the remains of Vietnamese volunteer soldiers who died during the Cambodian war and were excavated in Kampong Thom. Step 2, Phase 22 of the dry season 2022-2023 on the geography of Kampong Thom province to return home.
Colonel Nguyen Ngoc Anh, head of the Vietnamese K72 Volunteer Corps excavation technical team in Binh Phuoc province, reports that the excavations took place in Kampong Thom province during the rainy season. In the past 2022-2023, 5 relics were repatriated.
He said that in the past 20 years, from 2003 to 2023, the K70 and K72 technical teams have excavated 1,152 remains, while the remaining remains are being excavated. Raise and repatriate in the future.
Lt. Gen. Som Sun, Commander of Kampong Thom Military Operations Area and Permanent Deputy Chairman of the Vietnam Volunteer Army Excavation Expert Committee in Kampong Thom Province, thanked the Vietnamese Volunteer Army for their heroic sacrifices. On Cambodian soil in the cause of cooperation with the army of the United Front for National Salvation of Cambodia to overthrow the genocidal regime of Pol Pot in 1979.
"Today is the 22nd time that Kampong Thom province has celebrated the repatriation of 1,152 remains of Vietnamese volunteer soldiers excavated in Kampong Thom province for repatriation," he said. "Return to the homeland in humanitarian activities under an agreement between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam."
On that occasion, Major General Som Sun wished the 22nd repatriation of the remains of the Vietnamese Volunteer Army 2022-2023, which was carried out in Kampong Thom province, a successful return to the motherland and Security.
