(Phnom Penh): People in Sangkat Phsar Kandal I, Khan Daun Penh, Phnom Penh, as well as people in other provinces, they have benefited from cash support programs for poor and vulnerable families during the fight against Kovid - 19 For three years.
Chea Srey Mom, 51, who also has a chronic illness, said that her family pays 570,000 riel a month, which has greatly helped her livelihood, especially during When epidemic 19 spread, he could not go out to work.
While on her way to pay for a cash aid program for poor and vulnerable families during the fight against Kovid-19 at the Wing counter in Central Market, Mira told Fresh News that she had received the equity card. Since 2017, after local authorities assessed her family situation in poverty.
About 10 family members a month, Mira pays 650,000 riel, which has greatly helped her family buy food, water and electricity for her children.
Ouch Sarom, chief of Phsar Kandal I commune, said that so far, 59 families in Phsar Kandal I commune have received equity cards and allowances while they were affected by Kovid 19.
He said that the authorities always go to the backs of people's houses to assess their livelihoods and provide accurate or poor certificates without discriminating on political grounds.
He added that please stop misunderstanding that the budget that they always open this month is the budget of foreigners or any other organization, in fact, this budget is the budget of the Royal Government to help people in difficult times. It is the highest consideration of Samdech Akka Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
