BEIJING, June 27 (Xinhua) - The annual meeting of the new leaders of the World Economic Forum opened in Tianjin, China on June 27. About 1,500 dignitaries from politics, business, civil society, international organizations and academia attended the meeting. The forum was held under the theme "Entrepreneurship: the driving force of the world economy."
Li Qiang stressed that in the face of the global crisis, no country can be happy on its own, and no country can solve all problems on its own. "Solidarity is the only way out." During this meeting, the meeting will discuss how to drive innovation and career creation to drive growth and create a more realistic, sustainable and resilient global economy.
The main goal of this meeting is to revitalize the vitality of innovation and entrepreneurial spirit in various regions around the world. The meeting will discuss the latest global issues such as global debt, financial stability and climate change, which will have systemic implications for Asia and other parts of the world.
The announcement comes as the Lithuanian president travels to Kiev to discuss the NATO summit in Vilnius next month. About Ukraine's EU membership with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky.
