Sweden has set its sights on a NATO summit scheduled for July 11-12, amid strong support from other members, including the United States, but Turkey and Hungary so far. Still refuses to ratify.
Swedish and Turkish officials met on June 14, with Swedish negotiators calling the talks "good" and planning another summit in Brussels hosted by NATO chiefs. Jane Stoltenberg before the summit.
The Ministry of Commerce, in collaboration with the World Intellectual Property Organization, organized a training course on raising awareness of the use of intellectual property for women entrepreneurs, branding and product development.
(Siem Reap): On June 28, 2023, the Department of Intellectual Property of the Ministry of Commerce in collaboration with the World Intellectual Property Organization (WIPO) organized a training course on "Promoting Knowledge of Intellectual Property Use for Women Entrepreneurs: "Branding, product development and marketing."
