(Phnom Penh): Mr. HUN Many, President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, during a meeting with members of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia at Phnom Penh International University this morning, June 28, 2023, shared some ideas and opinions to respond. To the questioning of members.
Through Facebook, Mr. HUN Many clarified what is the answer related to the process of building and developing the nation, with the participation of the youth must be oriented in both perspective and implementation, and the youth force must be a common force that becomes the solution to the problem. Challenges in society.
"One of the great potential of Cambodia is our people," he said. I have confidence in the future of Cambodia, which has a young population full of ability, critical thinking, creative thinking and high will. But I personally have a connection to the question of how the abilities and strengths of all those young people are being used in any direction.
For example, from the actual history of Cambodia, if we look at the past, the Lon Nol coup d'etat would not have been successful without the participation of the youth forces. In that, the Front 2 December 1978, without the strength of the participation of young men and women who have the courage to sacrifice, can not be successful.
What we can learn is that in the first case, the strength of the youth led Cambodia into a dark page of history, but in the second case, through the strength of the youth who joined the December 2 Front, we liberated the nation from the genocidal regime. And bring complete peace in the country.
In this sense, while we have a strong youth force, we need to use that force in the direction of both vision and practice, and the youth force must be a joint force that becomes a solution to the challenges in society to unite our country. Better.
Delegation of the Ministry of Education attends the 1st Extraordinary Meeting of the Education Cooperation Organization in Ethiopia
The OEC is an international organization that focuses on contributing to equitable social development, justice and prosperity by promoting a balanced and inclusive education to achieve fundamental rights including freedom, justice, dignity, sustainability and cohesion. Society and security, material and intangible for all the peoples of the world.
He also told the ceremony that international organizations such as the OEC should not be the only ones to formulate their own policies, but to take into account the needs of member countries in building their policies. A policy that can be translated into executive action serves the interests of individual member states instead of formulating joint policies that are generally difficult to implement for member countries.
Mr. Nos Sles expressed his appreciation to the founding fathers, including Cambodia, for participating in the establishment of this international organization to balance education and provide opportunities for all. Quality education. Preah Sihanouk Provincial Governor: Informal Economic Work Provides Potential Resources and Promotes Socio-Economic Growth
(Preah Sihanouk): Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, said that working in the informal economy in the field of tourism services has provided resources and potential to contribute to the work sector, get a salary to help improve the livelihood of the family. Has greatly boosted the socio-economic growth of the nation.
This statement was made when the Provincial Governor on the evening of June 27, 2023 met with the staff of Informal Economy of Adult Tourism Service at Leng Try Restaurant in Veal Renh Commune, Prey Nob District, Preah Sihanouk Province. Participation from MPs, Deputy Provincial Governors, Prey Nup District Governor and relevant department heads.
According to Prey Nup District Governor E Thearin in March 2023, there are 39 adult tourism businesses in Prey Nup district, with a total of 371 people working in 15 communes. Of Prey Nob district.
The provincial governor added that in order to address the social security policy on pensions, because obtaining a social security card is useful for health and occupational accident insurance, and asked all employers and site owners to work. Register and collaborate with the Department of Labor to ensure that our staff receive the same ID card and pension as the Armed Forces civil servants.
From 2023, the Royal Government, led by Samdech Techo, has introduced social security policies for factory workers, enterprises and employees in the system and outside the system to receive pensions to receive both health and pension benefits when we 60-year-olds receive a pension according to the level of work we have done to take advantage of the social security system according to their seniority.
On that occasion, the provincial governor also brought the budget of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to support the informal economic staff in the field of adult tourism services in Prey Nup district, each of whom received 50,000 Riels. The case of Lay Samnang, a former official of the Ministry of Social Affairs, who was arrested by the ACU in the case of embezzling more than $ 380,000 from the state budget, was announced by the court on July 5
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sam Bithy Veasna, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, concluded the decision to uphold the charges against Mr. Lay Samnang, Deputy Director of the Department of Finance and Supply of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Former Youth and Youth Fitness for "exploitation "Illegal and money laundering."
Following the indictment of the prosecution, Ms. Ly Sok Vouch, the trial judge, decided to take up the case and announce the verdict on 5 July 2023.
It should be noted that Deputy Director of the Department of Finance and Supply of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Former Youth and Youth Fitness and an agent of the Ministry to pay money from the bank, Mr. Lay Samnang was arrested by the Anti-Corruption Unit on the morning of January 11, 2023 Involved in the embezzlement of more than 1,500 million riels (more than 380,000 dollars).
In addition to embezzling more than $ 380,000 from the state budget, the suspect was also involved in embezzling state policy money from nearly 4,000 poor people in the community and was also suspected of money laundering. It is sent to court for legal action. President of the Cambodian Women's Association for Peace and Development in Kampong Thom Province: Every woman must have good solidarity to participate in the development of the country and strive to increase their capacity
(Kampong Thom): Ms. Hong Phany Nguon Rattanak, Honorary Chairman of the Branch Committee of the Cambodian Women's Association for Peace and Development in Kampong Thom Province, and Ms. Khuon Khundy, Senator and Honorary Vice President of the Kampong Thom Branch of the Cambodian Women's Association for Peace and Development Meet with about 200 representatives of teachers, doctors and branch leaders of Kampong Thom Women's Association on June 28, 2023 at Kampong Thom Provincial Hall.
Ms. Khuon Khun Dy sent a message of greetings and greetings from Samdech Kittisangkhab Dr. Men Sam An, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Special Inspection, Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, Honorary President of the Cambodian Women's Association for Peace and Development. All members who participated in today's program.
She praised the hard work, dedication and responsibility of the women's movement in the past with remarkable success.
"To commemorate the struggle of women, the demand for democratic rights and equal rights between men and women, especially the values of peace, the promotion of a culture of non-violence that the government has been promoting, encourages participation," she said. "From all institutions, including men and women, for social progress towards promoting the rights, living conditions, status, role of women as well as social welfare by preventing and reducing violence."
She encourages women civil servants who are working to develop capacity building in institutions as well as units to become leaders and good mothers to achieve peace and happiness in society, family and society.
Ms. Hong Phany Nguon Rattanak stated that in the past, the Cambodian Women's Association for Peace and District Development has carried out many activities in connection with the provincial administration and cooperated well with the provincial women's association to visit and bring funds to promote Women at the grassroots level have been actively involved in tackling all forms of domestic violence.
Finally, Ms. Hong Phany Nguon Rattanak instructed all women to be united as a container to participate in the development of the country, strive to increase their capacity, educate their children to respect traffic laws and stay away from drugs.
