One Worker Killed and More Than 40 Injured in Traffic Accident in Kampong Tralach District, Kampong Chhnang Province
(Kampong Chhnang): A factory worker was killed while 42 others were seriously and lightly injured in a traffic accident caused by a truck carrying factory workers and a motorbike along National Road 5 between the 65-66 km marker in the village Kbal Thnal, Sep Commune, Kampong Tralach District, Kampong Chhnang Province. This is according to the report of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Road Traffic Police, which was provided by Fresh News Agency in Kampong Chhnang Province.
After the incident, the families of the injured were sent to Kampong Tralach District Referral Hospital and some were sent to Kampong Chhnang Provincial Referral Hospital. For cars and motorcycles, including Tai Kong, cars and motorcyclists are being questioned and researched according to the procedures of the competent authorities.
According to the report of the Cambodian Red Cross, Kampong Chhnang branch confirmed that after the incident and sent the victim to the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Referral Hospital immediately, the leaders in many provinces led by the provincial governor and chairman. The Provincial Branch of the Cambodian Red Cross visited and brought money to the injured workers at the Provincial Referral Hospital and at the Kampong Tralach District Referral Hospital.
On that occasion, the provincial governor, together with officials of the Cambodian Red Cross branch, also donated 200,000 Riels to the workers who suffered in the above incident. Separately, among the victims, three pregnant workers received a subsidy from the Red Cross, 300,000 Riels each, and the caregiver received 50,000 Riels.
Mr. Prak Von, Director of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Health Department, confirmed to Fresh News by telephone on the morning of June 28, 2023 that this morning, Mr. Kuy Sophal, Senior Minister and Secretary of State of the Ministry of the Royal Palace, also led the team. Greetings from Samdech Chao Faraing Kong Sam Ol and Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia to all workers who have suffered with the utmost sympathy.
In that, the Senior Minister brought the money to the workers who were injured and are being treated in the hospital, both Kampong Chhnang Provincial Referral Hospital and Kampong Tralach District Referral Hospital, as well as private hospitals, each received 200,000 Riels. And the caregiver received 100,000 Riels, in which the Senior Minister also donated 2 million Riels to the doctors who work hard to care for and treat patients in Kampong Chhnang Provincial Referral Hospital.
The director of the Department of Health confirmed that of all the victims, three were pregnant and three were female workers were sent to the hospital in Phnom Penh. Senior CPP officials call on party members to prepare enough documents and guide everyone to vote for the CPP on July 23
