He sent a message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, who both miss the people all over the country, as well as all the people in Chantrea district, especially the people who have a shortage, both Samdech always Have the team visit and bring gifts.
In addition, Mr. Moeung Kompheak also urged the authorities and the Armed Forces to continue to participate in providing better public services to the people, both services, requests and needs, and requests that are necessary at the local level. Must be resolved in a timely manner and must implement the policy of 7 villages, communes, safety to be highly effective to ensure that people live in peace.
On this occasion, he also raised some important points such as schools, canals, waterways, roads, etc. The local people make requests to the authorities as well as relevant institutions to help resolve, and all the necessary requests, the working group also urged the relevant authorities and departments to try to find a solution as soon as possible to the people.
It should be noted that the gift of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, which Mr. Moeung Kumpheak brought to give to the needy people in Samrong commune, each family received 50 kg of rice, 1 fish, 1 mama. 1 case of pure water, 1 case of orange juice, 1 case of krama, 1 box of cakes, 1 box of Tai Lao cakes, 1 package and a budget of 40,000 riels. Kampong Thom Provincial Authority opens construction site for 1,200 meters of red gravel road in Stong district
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Prem Ratha, Deputy Governor of Kampong Thom Province, inaugurated the construction site of the 1,200-meter-long red gravel road of the Ministry of Rural Development by the Provincial Department of Rural Development in Leuk and Prasat villages, Preah Damrey commune, Stong Na district. In the morning of June 28, 2023.
Mr. Tan Veasna, Acting Director of the Provincial Department of Rural Development, confirmed that the urgent repair and construction of the red gravel road at this time is in response to the actual needs of the people, especially to facilitate local traffic in Preah Damrey commune to be better. Up more than before.
Mr. Prem Ratha advised the construction company, Tan Meng Hong Construction Company, to repair this road properly according to the technical standards of the contract to ensure the quality and longevity for the people to travel. Easier to transport agricultural products safely.
He called on local people to take care of the road, not to encroach on the road or pour soil higher than the road, which leads to congestion or water on the road, which is the main cause of damage. Road ahead of schedule.
He advised local authorities to advise their citizens to take care of the local environment as well as improve the health of the people in the commune.
Mr. Prem Ratha instructed the Department of Rural Development as well as the administration of Preah Damrey commune to monitor all the construction activities of the above company to ensure that the construction is in accordance with technical standards, contracts and on time.
Three farming communities in Kampong Chhnang province signed an agreement with CACC on the production and supply of organic rice worth more than 435 million riels
(Kampong Chhnang): Three agricultural communities in Kampong Chhnang province, through the provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, have signed agricultural contracts with the Cambodian Agricultural Community Corporation (CACC) on agricultural production on the production and supply of organic rice, Rumduol flowers, water prices. About 435 million riels that were exchanged for good pure seed in Kampong Chhnang province.
He added that the agricultural contract is an important mechanism to achieve the planned agricultural production contract, in addition to the support, which is a key player in promoting and facilitating agricultural contracts. With the farming community and increase rice exports to the world market.
Mr. Ngin Hun said that the current contract is very important for the farming community in Kampong Chhnang to prepare production plans to meet market demand by ensuring efficiency, quality and safety.
The director of the department added that for other agricultural communities that have not yet signed the contract, the department will cooperate with partner organizations to explain to all communities to be ready to participate together for the sustainable development of the community. Get equitable benefits between partners, companies and communities.
It should be noted that in Kampong Chhnang province, there are 62 farming communities recognized by the Department of Agriculture. The contract benefits farmers without having to look for markets to sell agricultural products, but also maintain good market prices for the community.
The Thai Embassy in collaboration with the Royal University of Phnom Penh organized the "Poet Sunthon Phu" Day 2023
More than 150 students from the Department of Thai Language participated in the above program, with Thai language competitions in various categories, such as Thai speeches, Thai calligraphy, Thai poetry composition and singing. .
In addition, there will be exhibitions of biographies of the poet Sunthorn Phu, short scenes in Thai fairy tales and performances by talented Thai language students, demonstrations of how to make Thai cakes by the wives of embassy officials.
In addition, the Ambassador, civil servants of the Thai Embassy and private representatives presented certificates and prizes to the winners of the competition.
The Thai Embassy encourages and encourages Thai Language Department students from all universities in Cambodia to participate in programs that promote and develop Thai language and culture skills, and also support student initiatives in organizing programs to continue and develop Opportunities for education and other careers in the future.
The Royal Government of Thailand, with the Department of International Relations as its staff, has supported and supported the Thai Language Department of the Royal University of Phnom Penh through the development of curricula, teaching methods and learning materials, and the deployment of "Thai Friends Volunteers" to serve as teachers. Thai language every year.
Minister of Commerce: DPM Laboratories Play Important Role in Food Security and Public Welfare
(Kratie): The Minister of Commerce, Mr. Pan Sosak, stated that the laboratory of the General Department of Consumer Protection, Competition and Anti-Fraud (CPC) has played an important role and contributed to food security and promotion. The level of well-being of the people. Seeing the importance of this, the Ministry of Commerce has made efforts to expand this laboratory to the provinces after Phnom Penh.
The Minister emphasized this during the inauguration ceremony of the administrative building and small laboratory of the Branch of Consumer Protection, Competition and Anti-Fraud (KPR) in Kratie province on Wednesday morning, the 28th. This June 2023.
During the ceremony, the Minister congratulated the KPR branch. Kratie Province and praised and appreciated the relevant leaders and construction team who worked hard to plan and process the construction until the beautiful building as seen now.
The Minister recalled the recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, who considered the food issue as the first of the 12 imbalances that need to be addressed. In response to this recommendation, the Ministry of Commerce has put in place a number of key strategic plans to improve food safety, protect consumers and ensure fair and reliable trade competition.
In fact, the Ministry of Commerce has made efforts to establish legal systems and regulations for implementation, as well as to build a special structure, especially a laboratory to support the implementation of those laws and regulations.
South Korea passed a law to abolish the old age method and fully adopt international age standards in December 2022, as it officially took effect on Wednesday. According to a government survey in September 2022, 86 percent of South Koreans claim that they will apply the international age-counting principle in their daily lives when it comes into force.
South Korea, meanwhile, has another age-limiting system for conscription, enrollment and legal age calculation for alcohol consumption and smoking, with an individual's age ranging from zero. At birth, however, one year is added every January 1st rather than on birthdays. According to South Korean officials, the age limit will remain the same.
Mr. Preap Kol Meets Singapore Investors to Present the Investment Environment and Opportunities in Cambodia
In this cordial conversation, Mr. Jonathan Po informed about the investment projects that will help small and medium enterprises in Cambodia to get foreign investment funds and to be able to list on the stock market at home and abroad.
He added that through this investment, there is also a charity project to improve education and vocational training.
In response to the above request, Mr. Preap Kol promised to support the evaluation mechanism and strengthen the capacity of Cambodian enterprises to meet the conditions and needs of foreign investment partners.
The delegation of Capital Investment Co., Ltd. thanked Mr. Preap Kol for allowing the delegation to pay a courtesy call, share information and discuss work related to investment and trade in Cambodia, a gesture of interest. The attention and efforts of the Royal Government of Cambodia to promote good relations with foreign investors.
Mr. Preap Kol informed all delegates that all investment and trade in Cambodia must be organized in accordance with proper procedures, namely through the Council for the Development of Cambodia (CDC), the Ministry of Commerce, the Ministry of Economy and Finance and institutions. Other relevant to ensure that those investment and trade activities are legally protected.
The investor delegation is committed to working with the Royal Government and is happy to work with Preap Kol and other relevant institutions to promote Cambodia to potential investors in Singapore and around the world.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng notes 6 issues related to the drug situation in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, noted six issues related to the current situation of the drug situation in Cambodia, which should continue to be addressed.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng made this remark on the morning of June 28, 2023, on the occasion of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, celebrating the International Day Against Drug Abuse on June 26, 2023. .
For 2023, the International Day Against Drug Abuse is being held under the theme "People First: Stop Discrimination and Discrimination of Drug Addicts, Strengthen Preventive Education" with a focus on greater awareness. Depth by giving priority to the people or considering the people as the basis in formulating policies, strategic plans, action plans and other measures related to the fight against drugs.
Some of the issues related to the current drug situation in Cambodia by Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng include:
* Second, drug imports from the Golden Triangle into Cambodia through the northeastern provinces of the country continue to increase.
* Third: Criminals are still trying to smuggle synthetic drugs into Cambodia by diverting imported chemicals for legal use into illegal drugs.
* Fourth: The crime of trafficking in traffic, processing of large products was effectively and timely suppressed by the competent authorities.
* Fifth: Minor distribution, trafficking and drug use in the community continue to occur significantly, causing annoyance and concern from the people that we do not seem to have fully and effectively addressed. Reliability yet.
* Sixth: Drug use is an increasing problem (increasing number of treatment facilities) and affects individuals, families, communities and society in general. It is a complex issue that requires the joint efforts of individuals, families, communities, NGOs and other stakeholders to address. Kampot Provincial Governor Meets and Visits More Than 10,000 People in Kampong Trach District
(Kampot): Kampot Provincial Governor Mr. Mao Thunin advised the authorities at all levels to consider all people as one family and to take care to serve them well.
This statement was made during a meeting and visit of more than 10,000 people on the morning of June 27, 2023 in the area of Wat Damnak Kantuot South, Damnak Kantuot South Commune, Kampong Trach District.
Mr. Mao Thunin highlighted that "the whole country as well as at the local level throughout Kampot province has developed to this day due to the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, who sacrificed "Physical and mental strength to exchange his life and family with the liberation of the motherland, save the people from the war to find peace and development in almost all areas."
At the same time, the provincial governor also called on all people of voting age and whose names are on the voter list to go to the polls on July 23, 2023 and vote for the 18th Cambodian People's Party on Vote to join Samdech Techo in safeguarding peace and continuing the development of the country.
During the meeting, some people expressed their gratitude for the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, saying that they survived, had a comfortable life and their children were educated, peaceful and had everything like Today, because of Samdech Techo, if we forget something, we can forget, but we can not forget this great merit.
