General Pen Vibol instructs newly trained police officers to use their knowledge and skills to serve their units in a targeted and efficient manner.
(Kampong Speu): General Pen Vibol, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police and Director of the Personnel Department, instructed the police trainees who have just completed the training to use the knowledge and skills they gained from this study to serve the unit in a targeted and effective manner. High for the cause of the nation and the motherland.
The introduction of General Pen Vibol was made this morning, June 28, 2023, on the occasion of being the representative of General Dr. Neth Savoeun, General Commissioner of the National Police, to close the training course on technical skills, cryptography and basic vocational training of police in Cambodia-Vietnam Friendship National Police School.
General Pen Vibol emphasized that from one stage to another, the situation in society is constantly changing, so as National Police officers must receive additional training to strengthen their capacity to keep up with the situation. Today's society.
"Society is constantly evolving, requiring us to strengthen our capacity to provide training," he said. I think the study of skills is very important, so take the knowledge and skills gained from this study to serve their respective units effectively.
General Pen Vibol also praised the dedication of all police trainees from the Capital-Provincial Commissioners and Departments under the General Commission of the National Police to study at the Cambodia-Vietnam Friendship Police Academy for the past four months. . The general also thanked the teachers, police and school leaders for their attention.
He added that the current basic vocational training of police has a total of 187 participants (41 females) from the National Committee Against Torture (NEC), General Secretariat, General Department of Immigration, General Department of Identification, General Department. Logistics and finance, including units under the Ministry of Interior and the Capital-Provincial Police Commission and 25 Departments under the National Police.
Lt. Gen. Oum On added that in each course, the school requires a final exam and a final exam for each lesson, both theory and practice on the field, teachers need to test to assess the ability of trainees and give scores. Each participant, along with discipline, ethics, solidarity, labor, hygiene, living, is the basis for providing a certificate of completion at the end of the course.
While celebrating the brilliant results that all of you trainees have achieved now, Lt. Gen. Oum On hopes that when you return to the unit, all of you will take the knowledge gained from the school. To fulfill the duties of serving the unit with high efficiency. Tang Kork District Governor and Chief Inspector of Kuhonkor Pagoda inaugurated the construction site of a concrete road with a length of nearly 1 km, local people are more happy with this new achievement
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Hak Mong Huot, Governor of Taing Kork District and Preah Monisil Vongton Pisey, Chief Inspector of Wat Kuhon Nokor, on June 28, 2023, opened the construction site of a concrete road 922 meters long and 6 meters wide in the village. Pong, Pong commune, Tang Kork district, as this road is an important road to facilitate travel, boost the economy and transport people more easily.
Mr. Hak Mong Huot said that one road is an important road to stimulate the local economy, connecting National Road No. 6 to the resort of Prasat Kuhonkor, a road for people to travel to farm and transport agricultural products to the market. And other occupations and also the path that students need to travel to school.
Originally, this road was a red gravel road, but after Rev. Ton Pisey initiated the idea to improve it into a concrete road, there were Buddhists and philanthropists near and far to contribute money and reached the groundbreaking ceremony today.
The improvement of this road is the southern part, so in the past, the Pong commune administration and the chief priest of Wat Kuho Nokor have already built a concrete road on the northern part.
The district governor also said that the fact that the team had the opportunity to repair and build roads for people to travel, transport and do business with ease and peace, because the country is completely peaceful, the development that comes from Win-win politics of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. Samdech Techo, President of the Cambodian People's Party and the Royal Government, always consider the lives of the people as necessary.
The Minister explained the political path of the Cambodian People's Party, which is committed to peace and called on the people to participate in maintaining peace and achievements that the Royal Government as well as the CPP have worked hard to build in the past, present and Contribute to future construction so that the base has a rich supportive achievement.
Mr. Hak Mong Huot did not forget to call on the people to get ready to go to the polls on Sunday, July 23, 2023 and vote for the 18th Cambodian People's Party to support the democratic process. Liberal multi-party in Cambodia, especially to participate in maintaining peace, because peace is an important factor leading the nation to development.
The local people in Pong commune expressed their happiness with this new achievement and decided to cooperate in facilitating the construction of this road, while some also volunteered to donate fences, houses, crops and other items to facilitate the group. Road construction work with transparency. Many drugs weighing up to 5 tons were burned, Prince Sar Kheng: Drugs continue to increase, which requires authorities and forces to continue to crack down
(Phnom Penh): Many types of drugs weighing up to 5 tons were burned after being cracked down and confiscated in Phnom Penh recently.
The ceremony was held this morning, June 28, 2023, in celebration of the International Day Against Drug Abuse, June 26, 2023 under the theme "Everything for the people, first stop discrimination and stigmatize addicts. Drugs Strengthen Education and Prevention ”under the chairmanship of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, and with the participation of authorities, forces, people and more than 3,000 people at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng stated that in the first five months of 2023, our competent forces cracked down on 3,143 drug cases and arrested 7,480 suspects with 838 kilograms of drugs seized. 72.6 grams.
In relation to this drug, only in Phnom Penh, our competent forces cracked down on more than 5 and a half tons, which we have to burn now. But this number does not take into account the various chemicals that we need to neutralize and dissolve later.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also stated that the number of drug cases is still increasing, which requires all the authorities and the competent forces to be willing to crack down because it is a serious danger for our people, especially Youth, the nation's bamboo successor.
