(Phnom Penh): To support the environmental protection services and the implementation of the solid waste management policy 2020-2030 and the policy of safe villages, communes and communes towards the effective and effective management of urban solid waste. The environment provided 12 garbage trucks and 10 garbage tricycles donated by the Embassy of Japan in Cambodia (KUSANUNE project and civil aviation fee).
The handover ceremony was presided over by Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment and Mr. UENO ATSUSHI, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia to 14 Capital-Provincial Environment Departments on the morning of July 27, 2023 at the Ministry of Environment. The event was also attended by leaders of government officials, the Ministry of Environment and representatives of the provincial environment departments and municipal administrative units of the 14 provinces.
On that occasion, 12 garbage trucks and 10 garbage tricycles were distributed to the Department of Environment and the district administration to provide cleaning services, collection and transportation of solid waste in 22 districts of 14 provinces. These include: Banteay Meanchey, Battambang, Kampong Chhnang, Kampong Thom, Kampot, Kratie, Pursat, Siem Reap, Stung Treng, Takeo, Kampong Cham, Kandal, Mondulkiri and Preah Vihear provinces.
