Koh Kong Provincial Administration Holds a Meeting on Security Work for the 7th National Assembly Election
(Koh Kong): Koh Kong Provincial Administration held a meeting on security, safety and public order for the 7th National Assembly Election 2023 on June 27, 2023, chaired by Mr. Hak Leng, Deputy Governor of Koh Kong Province and relevant officials. Many more.
Mr. Hak Leng said that this meeting is very important in organizing security, safety and public order for the 7th National Assembly Election 2023, which will be held on July 23, 2023. Therefore, public security must be maintained for all political parties that stand for election and are ready to campaign for each party's election, so the Provincial Unity Command, which has organized security for all political parties.
He added that the provincial administration has reorganized the Security Secretariat of the Standing Committee for the 2022 to 2024 elections, where he was the chairman of the Standing Committee and staffed the provincial Permanent Security Secretariat to monitor and collect information in districts and For reporting to the national level.
Mr. Hak Leng added that to protect security, safety and public order, the security team must be strengthened from each political party campaign until the end of the census.
