Oknha Chan Sokheang stated that the progress of the rice sector is the result of the correct leadership policy and clear vision of the Royal Government, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on promoting production and exports. Rice has left Cambodia's rice production at a surplus of nearly 6 million tonnes, enabling Cambodia to grind, process and export rice to neighboring countries.
In the first five months of 2023, Cambodia exported 278,184 tons of rice, valued at more than 191 million US dollars, and exported 2,142,483 tons of rice to neighboring countries. About 1.37 million tons of rice), valued at more than 545 million US dollars. Overall, the export of rice and millet is worth more than 736 million US dollars into the Cambodian economy.
