(Kandal): On June 27, 2023, Mr. Nuth Puth Dara, Deputy Governor of Kandal Province, led a team from Provincial Department of Rural Development, District and Commune Authorities, Water Aid Organization and the construction company to inspect the construction process of floating toilets. And does not affect the environment for the people in Prasat commune, Saang district, Kandal province.
Mr. Nuth Puth Dara, during the inspection of the construction of the floating toilets, said that in the past, the people living in the floating houses have defecated into the canal, which has seriously affected the health, living, hygiene and environment in the area.
Seeing this problem, Kandal Provincial Administration, in collaboration with the Provincial Department of Rural Development and Water Aid, has organized the construction of floating toilets for the general public to use to make life easier, hygienic and healthy, especially to reduce the impact. To the environment.
It should be noted that Prasat commune is next to Prek Prasat, where people live in 6 months of land and 6 months of flooding, most of them are engaged in fishing and some people live in floating houses, so the construction of toilets to use is a problem. Challenges and difficulties for local people.
The people who benefited from this construction project congratulated and thanked the leaders at all levels who consider the hardships and well-being of the local people.
