It should be informed that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, on June 27, 2023, issued an urgent order for the Cambodian military to shoot down unmanned drones flying into Cambodian airspace in Ratanakkiri province.
Through an audio message received by Fresh News, Samdech Techo Hun Sen ordered Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, and General Hing Bun Heang, Deputy Commander-in-Chief and As the commander of the bodyguards to launch weapons for firing into the area where the drone flew into.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen raised the issue of terrorist attacks in Vietnamese territory about two weeks ago, in which Cambodia cooperated well with Vietnam in preventing terrorist groups from fleeing into Cambodian territory.
"The problem is that there are a lot of drones flying into Cambodia in a row in Ratanakkiri province, we asked the Vietnamese side, the Vietnamese side denied that" it is not their drone, "he said. "Continuing to this day, I estimate that a large number of drones are the enemy's drones that have attacked Vietnam, and there are now signs that some are fleeing into Cambodia."
"We have to use our modern weapons to shoot down any drones that fly into Cambodian territory," he said.
