He said that the Royal Government under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia has always paid attention and given priority to education, economy and infrastructure such as roads, bridges, schools and so on. So far, the education sector has grown both in quantity and quality, with schools in all villages across the country, as well as the development of teachers, curricula, infrastructure and good learning materials.
Mr. Ung Sam Ath said, however, that geographical gaps and inadequate primary schools remain barriers to children's access to education, especially age-appropriate enrollment. The academic achievement of over-age students is lower than that of age-appropriate students. We see that some children in remote areas of poor families drop out of post-primary or secondary school, which is a challenge that we all need to address together.
(Kampong Thom): The Provincial Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs held a ceremony to declare a judicial area for land identification, land classification, state land map and registration as state private land for local social land concessions, land allocation projects for social affairs and development. Economy Phase III (LASED III).
Mr. TOUCH Sokha, Deputy Governor of Kampong Thom Province, thanked the Royal Government, Ministries and Institutions for issuing a sub-decree to clear 793 hectares of land in Phan Nhem Commune for the purpose of Social Land Concession Project (LASED III) for the poor. Use to build housing, grow crops, cultivate agriculture, reduce poverty.
Mr. Theng Chansangvar stated that LASED III, a project of the Royal Government of Cambodia, aims to provide selected land security, agricultural and social services and selected infrastructure to communities and smallholder farmers in their target areas, implemented by a number of national working groups. The two are the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction as the executive agency and the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries as the implementation agency.
Mr. Theng Chansangvar urges the people who have received the land title to use the land properly for cultivation and as a legacy for future generations. If a criminal comes to work illegally, the local authority must be notified to take legal action.
