(Phnom Penh): The Embassy of the Republic of Korea in Cambodia held a gathering of alumni in Korea in 2023 to strengthen the friendly relations and cooperation between Korea and Cambodia, as well as the future socio-economic development of Cambodia based on the accumulated experience In Korea.
The event was attended by about 150 Cambodian alumni who repatriated after studying at a university in Korea through programs such as the Korean Government Scholarship Program for Foreign Students (GKS) and the KOICA Scholarship Program. Etc. And working in all fields, including government, corporations, universities and NGOs.
In his welcoming speech, Korean Ambassador PARK Jung-Wook called on all alumni studying in Korea to contribute to strengthening friendly relations and cooperation between Korea and Cambodia, as well as Cambodia's future socio-economic development. Based on experience gathered in Korea.
The Korea Alumni Association of Cambodia (KAAC) said that since its establishment in 2021, it has had about 400 members and is participating in various activities such as charity programs, seminars. About studying in Korea, sharing knowledge and exchanging with alumni associations studying in other countries.
