National Bank of Cambodia Holds a Meeting of the Financial Sector Development Steering Committee Meeting to Review the Draft Financial Sector Development Strategy
(Phnom Penh): The National Bank of Cambodia (NBC) has organized a meeting of the Steering Committee for Financial Sector Development to review the draft Financial Sector Development Strategy 2021-2030, which is an update from the Financial Sector Development Strategy Document 2015- 2025.
This is the fourth update since the preparation of the Financial Sector Development Strategy Document in 2001 to provide the basis for the development of a comprehensive, consistent and expected financial sector in Cambodia. Yes.
Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia and Chairman of the Steering Committee for Financial Sector Development, said during the meeting, "Through this important document, the Cambodian financial sector has achieved many achievements that support and promote "Sustainable and sustainable economic development contributes to poverty reduction and regional and international integration."
He said that long-term strategic documents are generally updated every five years, in the middle of the implementation period of the strategy to keep up with new developments and challenges, as well as to strengthen the implementation of policies in the development action plan. Highly efficient financial sector.
In the past, the technical working groups of financial authorities, both bank and non-bank, have met several times with online experts and provided input to help improve the content of the draft financial sector development strategy. According to the achievements, challenges and directions of development in each sector.
Mr. Chea Chanto requested that representatives of the financial authorities, banks and non-banks and other stakeholders cooperate to provide input to strengthen the ownership of this strategic document and implement it effectively. Cambodia is working to accelerate the export plan of 1 million tons of rice by 2025
(Phnom Penh): Oknha Chan Sokheang, President of the Cambodian Rice Federation, said that the goal of exporting 1 million tons of rice will be achieved by 2025, while the federation as well as stakeholders are currently preparing various strategies to boost imports. Exit.
In fact, this morning, June 26, 2023, the Ministry of Commerce of Cambodia officially inaugurated the export of more than 2,500 tons of Cambodian rice to the Republic of the Philippines, the first export to the Philippines in a short time. In the future, another 2,500 tons of rice will continue to be exported to this ASEAN member country.
Mr. Oknha Chan Sokheang said that Cambodia is also presenting its presence in the international market so that all buyers around the world know and recognize Cambodia as a country with great potential for rice.
Mr. Oknha Chan Sokheang said, "The plan to achieve the export of 1 million tons of rice in my goal, I want to achieve in 2025 with this desire, the Rice Federation has been preparing a strategy. "To boost exports as well."
Mr. Oknha Chan Sokheang stated that in order to promote the export and promotion of the rice market, the Rice Federation has organized an exhibition in Dubai to introduce Africa and other regions to Cambodian rice. Rice did not do so due to lack of information and some funding, but now the federation has been working and planning to work since the fair in many other countries.
Recently, the Rice Federation recently participated in a food fair in Thailand, and in October is scheduled to be an exhibition in Cologne, Germany, and these are the top food exhibition events in the world.
Minister of Commerce Pan Sosak also unveiled plans to boost rice exports to 1 million tonnes. He said the Ministry of Commerce, which has worked hard to draft a market opening regulation by signing a free trade agreement with China, a free trade agreement with Korea and a free trade agreement with the United Arab Emirates recently. .
The Minister noted that the agreement with the United Arab Emirates is very important to boost Cambodia's rice exports, as the country is a hub for rice distribution to Africa, most people living in Africa eat. Similar to Cambodia, these factors clearly show that when there is a market, exports will perform well.
Minister Pan Sosak confirmed that "the plan to export 1 million tons of rice will be achieved in the next mandate, now we together, the Royal Government and the people have worked hard to push the Cambodian ship to move faster and better."
Please be informed that in 2022, Cambodia exported nearly 640,000 tons of rice to international markets and exported more than 3 million tons of rice, valued at more than 1,255 million dollars.
In the first five months of 2023, Cambodia achieved the export of nearly 280,000 tons of rice and more than 2 million tons of rice with a budget of 736.90 million dollars.
