General knowledge: Why do so many African countries have straight borders?
(Phnom Penh): When we look at the world map, we are likely to notice that the borders of many countries on the African continent are straight lines, especially in the north and south.
Why do so many African countries have such straightforward borders?
Most of the European powers' colonies in Africa gained independence in the 20th century, and their straight borders have been maintained to this day.
Remarkably, the demarcation of the European border was done regardless of the borders of the predominant tribes in Africa. For example, some people live in the same tribal village but have to live in different countries.
