More than 2,500 tons of Cambodian rice has been exported for the first time to the Philippines, and in the near future another 2,500 tons of rice will continue to be exported to this ASEAN member country.
Minister of Commerce Pan Sosak pointed out that Cambodia will export another 2,500 tonnes of rice to the Philippines, a new market, after successfully exporting more than 2,500 tonnes in the first round in May.
He said that the unprecedented export of rice to the Philippine market is the starting point and that Cambodia will expand its market further, hoping that by 2024 it can capture 1%. Of the rice import market to the Philippines and stepped up in the following years to achieve this.
"Through these efforts, guidance has been provided to the leadership of the Ministry of Commerce and the Cambodian Rice Federation to further their efforts, while the Philippines' rice import policy has been reformed, leading to a start-up," he said. "Rice exports from Cambodia now and we believe that will continue to grow, which can stand in the Philippine market stronger and longer."
He urged the Cambodian Rice Federation, together with Green Trade and all exporters, to continue regular cooperation with Philippine importers on jointly promoting Cambodian rice in the Philippine market to boost demand and increase customer behavior. Get more Cambodian rice.
At the same time, he asked the Philippine Ambassador to encourage investors as well as rice importers in the Philippines to invest and receive more Cambodian rice imports because Cambodian rice has a delicious taste as winning rice. Five World Cups and hopefully this year there is another chance that the event will be held in Cebu, Philippines in November.
Cambodia exported 2,575 tonnes of rice for the first time to the Philippines, produced by Duke Kim Savuth's Khmer Food Company.
The Minister of Commerce has encouraged other companies, such as Khmer Food, to reach out as soon as possible to further boost rice exports, as well as to let the world know the taste and quality of Cambodia's rice, which has been ranked as the best in Cambodia. World 5 times.
Oknha Kim Savuth, president of Khmer Food, said the Philippines has been a major rice importer for many years, while Cambodia has been producing more than a million tonnes of rice for decades.
"Due to the efforts and attention of our Cambodian delegation, combined with the strong interest from rice importers in the Philippines, Khmer Food was able to export Cambodian rice in large quantities for the first time to the Philippines," he said. .
He added that among the rice exported to the Philippines, about 75 tons of red jasmine rice and about 2,500 tons of soft rice.
Oknha Chan Sokheang, president of the Cambodian Rice Federation, said that Cambodia had exported rice to the Philippines only twice, the first time in 2020 300 tons and the second time 100 tons in 2021.
He said the Philippines is the world's largest producer and importer of rice, ranking fourth in the world and second only to China in Asia, importing more rice. 3 million tons, and most of the ASEAN countries bordering Cambodia.
