(Kampong Cham): Sub-National Democratic Development, also known as Commune / Sangkat Fund Project, is funded by the Royal Government at the sub-national level to develop local infrastructure such as red gravel roads, canal rehabilitation and road construction. Concrete, etc. in order to improve the lives of people.
In relation to the above local development plan, Mr. Ngor Chuot, Chief of Trop Commune, Batheay District, said on the evening of June 25, 2023, that the 365-meter-long Ame 1 concrete road project has an estimated cost of over 268 million Riels. By IM N at a cost of more than 58 million riels.
The commune chief confirmed that the 365-meter-long concrete road is divided into two lanes, one in Trop village and one in Thmey village. But the construction of access roads in both villages. It took a short time before he used the rest of the money from the bidding for this project to hold a meeting with the community and the meeting with all the commune council procurement committees to decide to continue this road project for a longer time.
Mr. Trop commune chief also stated that in the competitive bidding, the MN company implemented at a price of 32,000 Riels per square meter, built and lost. However, in the follow-up project, after checking that the construction company was in accordance with the technical standards, the Procurement Committee as well as the community agreed to allow the company to continue construction at a cost of 100,000 Riels per square meter.
