The following is the message of Samdech Techo HUN SEN: Mr. HUN Many inaugurated the synagogue and achievements at Wat Preah Puth Andet called Wat Kdei Lvea, a gift from Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit
(Kampong Speu): Mr. HUN Many, Member of Parliament for Kampong Speu Constituency, this morning, June 26, 2023, attended the inauguration ceremony of the Assembly Hall and achievements at Wat Preah Puth Andet, also known as Wat Kdei Lvea, a precious gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen are located in Thlok Village, Trapeang Kong Commune, Samrong Tong District, Kampong Speu Province.
The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Vy Samnang, Governor of Kampong Speu, Mr. Dy Pov, Deputy Chief of Cabinet of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, Dr. Seang Bunleang and Ms. Hun Bunthoeun, Duke, Senator, National Assembly Member, Mr. Yim Sokhon, Chairman of Kampong Speu Provincial Council. As well as government officials, the armed forces and many citizens.
On behalf of the Kampong Speu Constituency MP and a Buddhist, Mr. HUN Many would like to congratulate and approve with Venerable Theranut Thera and all Buddhists near and far, especially the people in Trapeang Kong commune who have received many new achievements. More to serve the needs in the pagoda.
At the same time, Mr. HUN Many expressed his deep appreciation and gratitude to Bhikkhu Anando Ban Sophorn, Preah Chao Athikar of Wat Preah Puth Andet and all the monks and all the committee of Acharya Wat who worked hard to gather. Gather suffixes from philanthropists and Buddhists everywhere to build these achievements to appear.
Mr. HUN Many would also like to thank the generosity and generosity of Lt. Gen. Dy Pov, Deputy Chief of Staff of the Prime Minister and his family, Dr. Seang Bunleang and Ms. HUN Bunthoeun, as well as the generous people who donated their physical, mental and material resources. Participate in building a series of achievements in this floating Buddha pagoda.
At the same time, Mr. HUN Many called on the people to go to the polls on July 23, 2023 and vote for any party that makes peace and development in Cambodia.
Mr. Vy Samnang said that all the above results are absolutely indispensable on the 7th of January and starting from the win-win policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen has made progress in both Buddhism and the kingdom that Samdech Has made our motherland peaceful to the present, as well as a steady and continuous development.
Mr. Vy Samnang said that the slogan "Thank you for peace, thank you for winning politics" has resonated throughout the country and has become the spirit of a strong and vibrant society in the process of building and defending the motherland. If we do not keep the peace, we will not be able to achieve everything we have today.
According to the governor of Kampong Speu, Wat Preah Puth Andet (also known as Wat Kdei Lvea) was founded in 1951 AD, which is more than 522 years old and is one of the 295 pagodas in Kampong Speu province.
Wat Preah Puth Andet (called Wat Kdei Lvea) is located in Thlok Village, Trapeang Kong Commune, Samrong Tong District, Kampong Speu Province. Along National Road 4 and enter the pagoda about 1,000 meters, which currently has a teacher named Ban Sophorn as the pagoda's chief priest.
The synagogue was built with a length of 27 meters, a width of 18 meters, a height of 16.80 meters, lighting system in the synagogue, painting in the synagogue and doors, construction of a large bronze Buddha statue. He and his two little ones.
In addition to the new synagogue donated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, there are also a number of physical infrastructure built in Wat Preah Puth Andet (called Wat Kdei Lvea). The total construction cost is $ 534,168.
