(Kampong Cham): The President of the Boeung Krol Reservoir Community, Mr. Siem Sophal, said that the farmers living in the Boeung Krol Reservoir area are happy that the Batheay District Authority has prepared a law to restore the Boeung Krol Reservoir to store water. Let them water the crops in the coming dry season.
The community leader confirmed this on June 25, 2023 at the Boeung Krol water reservoir in Batheay village, Batheay commune, Batheay district, Kampong Cham province.
Mr. Siem Sophal said that for many years in the catchment area, the bottom of the basin was shallow and could not store much water, which caused farmers in the area to lack water to irrigate crops in the dry season. Therefore, recently, the people agreed through the community to ask the local authority and Batheay district authority to help restore the reservoir of Boeung Krol to store water to irrigate crops during the dry season.
The commune chief confirmed that after the proper permission, the owner of the machine agreed with the people to restore the lost pool and build more dams to make way for the national road, which made the people in this area enthusiastic. Strong for coordination from Batheay district authorities as well as Kampong Cham provincial leaders.
Meanwhile, the owner of the machine, Mr. Him Chanmakara, also said that the restoration of the bottom of the Boeung Kraol Reservoir, he received the right permission and started from May 14, 2023 until now with 40 results. % And is scheduled to be completed in early August 2023.
Regarding the law, the director of the Department of Mines and Energy, Mr. Ly Chanthy, said that the rehabilitation of the main area of Boeung Krol, the owner of the machine has a permit from the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology of Kampong Cham province at the request of the people, village authorities, commune and administration. Batheay district and have a permit as a mining handicraft from the Batheay district administration.
For the restoration of the main river, which is more than one hectare in length, the Batheay district authorities have arranged for three joint owners to have a mining license to restore in time during the rainy season. In addition, Lt. Gen. Di Vichea met with senior officials of the Chinese Ministry of Public Security to strengthen cooperation, especially in the fight against crime.
