Samdech Techo Hun Sen Asks to Pay Attention to Five Important Points to Improve the Quality of Trial and Justice (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): To Improve the Quality of Trial In accordance with the law, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister, on behalf of the Royal Government, requested to pay high attention to five important points.
Such a request by Samdech Techo Hun Sen was made on the occasion of the official inauguration of the "School of Justice" on the morning of June 26, 2023.
Suggestions for high attention on the five key points include:
1. Disputes must be resolved as soon as possible, reduce congestion in court, and help resolve differences between the parties to enhance national unity, harmony and better social order.
2. Encourage the role of judges to be more active in resolving disputes, mediation, conciliation and settlement of disputes between the parties as soon as possible without leaving a long-standing trial file.
3. The Ministry of Justice needs to establish a clear legal framework for the management of mediation and dispute resolution, which is a new priority in the framework of dispute resolution reform in Cambodia.
However, the Prime Minister also encouraged the authorities, judicial officials, as well as the courts at all levels to use mediation mechanisms to resolve disputes as much as possible in a win-win manner in civil cases.
This promotion was made on the occasion of Samdech Techo presiding over the inauguration of the "School of Justice" on the morning of June 26, 2023.
At the end of 2022, the Ministry of Justice expects the Commercial Court to be established in 2023.
Mr. Chiv Songhak, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Justice and Chairman of the Commercial Court Organizing Committee, stated that the establishment of this specialized court is also to increase the trust of investors by improving the quality of services in handling cases in a professional manner. Each participant reduces the congestion of court cases through faster procedures.
He added that the launch of the Commercial Court is the first step in Phnom Penh, and that both the Court of Appeal and the Court of Appeal are together. The next step may be to set up in Sihanoukville, and especially in areas where there is a lot of trade.
Please be reminded that Mr. Keut Rith, Minister of Justice, decided to set up a committee to organize the proceedings of the Commercial Court through the letter No. 03 KYSor / 21 dated 21 January 2021.
The commission, chaired by Mr. Chiv Songhak, is responsible for including the preparation of legal documents related to the establishment of commercial courts in the lower courts and the Chamber of Commerce of the High Courts, and Setting up locations for commercial courts, setting up regulations on commercial procedures and determining the types of commercial disputes.
