Key remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of the inauguration of the "School of Justice"
The "Court of Justice Building" is the office of the Phnom Penh Court of Appeal and the Attorney General of the Phnom Penh Court of Appeal and the Phnom Penh Municipal Court and the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
The following are the main contents of Samdech Techo Hun Sen: The opportunity to inaugurate the "Judicial School Building":
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded that the Royal Government has helped the court to expedite the congestion of the case by helping to close the hotel to hold a hearing.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised and highly appreciated the efforts in the performance of work with a high sense of responsibility, especially the achievements that the Trial Chamber and the Prosecutor's Office at all levels have achieved so far. This.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen encourages judges to use mediation mechanisms to the best of their ability in cases.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in order to ensure peace and political stability, the management of criminal politics is a policy that must be taken into account.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructs judges to try to mediate disputes between spouses, not to encourage divorce.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that legal and judicial reform is a priority in the agenda and political program of the Royal Government to promote "good governance" and "rule of law" for governing and leading the state in accordance with the principles. Of the Constitution, the supreme law of the nation.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in a society governed by the rule of law, the judiciary has played an important role in strengthening the effectiveness of law enforcement, protecting against social injustice, ensuring security, public order and social stability. Sustainable national development.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen advises to resolve disputes as soon as possible, reduce congestion in court cases, help reconcile differences between the parties to increase national unity, harmony with better social order.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen encourages the role of judges to be more active in resolving disputes, facilitating conciliation, ending disputes between the parties as soon as possible without leaving a long-standing trial file.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructs the Ministry of Justice to quickly establish a legal framework for the management of mediation and dispute resolution, which is a new priority in the framework of dispute resolution reform in Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces the opening of the first meeting of the National Assembly on August 28 and the swearing-in of the Prime Minister on August 29.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen advised to study the establishment of a commercial court in the next mandate.
