Mr. Preap Bona, Deputy Director of the Department of Administration and General Affairs of the General Department of Taxation, stated that the tax on house and land rent is determined from the wages from the rent of the house and land to be collected from the owner or the rights of the rights worker (you On behalf of the owner) and this tax is collected for the benefit of the sub-national budget.
He added that taxpayers must pay tax on house and land rent every month and must declare within 15 days from the date of signing the lease or from the date of the lease change to the provincial tax branch. The district in which the leased property is located shall be attached a copy of the lease agreement. At the same time, when the lease is terminated within 15 days, a written declaration must be made to the provincial tax branch where the leased property is located.
If the taxpayer's property is being destroyed or the taxpayer is in a life-threatening situation, the tax payment may be delayed or the tax amount may be reduced or the taxpayer may be exempt from the tax.
