This Morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Meets More Than 20,000 Workers in Bavet City
Samdech Techo Prime Minister has met with workers in Bavet City three times already. The first time in 2005, the second time and the third time in 2018.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, said that the 24 factories that allow workers to participate in this event include 7 garment factories, 3 shoe factories, 1 processing of rubber and plastic products, assembly and Install 1 bicycle, 3 electronics and 9 other factories. These factory products are exported to international markets such as the European Union, the United States, China and Australia.
Starting from this reason, in 1999, Samdech Techo Hun Sen set out a policy to deploy factories in the provinces to provide jobs near people's homes. Svay Rieng has become one of the target destinations for investment in factories and enterprises and has benefited from the policy of deploying factories.
According to Mr. Ith Sam Heng, in 2023, Svay Rieng province has 264 factories with about 90,000 workers, 5,000 people, with an average wage of about 284 million US dollars per year. There are 41 garment factories with about 40,000 workers with an average wage of 124 million US dollars per year. Svay Rieng is the sixth province with the development of many garment factories.
Today's meeting is the 15th meeting for the second round. The 15 meetings were attended by a total of 278,000 workers. Samdech Techo is scheduled to meet four more times, which will meet with a total of 58,000 more workers.
