Samdech Techo Hun Sen: Peace policy between Cambodia and Vietnam for good trade cooperation (Video inside) (Svay Rieng): Speaking from the border area between Cambodia and Vietnam in a meeting with workers on the morning of June 25 In 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, affirmed that the peace policy between Cambodia and Vietnam has led to good trade cooperation between the two countries.
Contrary to the policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia, the policy of going to war with neighboring countries, which incites discrimination just for the sake of the vote, is not a policy that should be supported, and extremist politics creates such hostility. Is dangerous politics for the country. This is what Samdech Techo Hun Sen highlighted.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "If other people who only think about Vietnam every day, curse Vietnam constantly, ask if there is a factory here today?" Extremist politics deceives by inciting civilization with neighboring countries, it is the most dangerous policy for the country. Uncle (Samdech Techo) as the leader who brought an end to the war, Uncle set two goals after the war ended.
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, as the leader who brought about the end of the rescue, he set out two policies: first: to turn the former battlefield area into a developed and marketable one; and secondly. Transform the border area with all neighboring countries into a border of peace, friendship, cooperation and development. Starting from these two policies, the Cambodia-Vietnam border area has achieved success through the increasing number of factories and industrial zones.
In line with what is happening now, Samdech Techo Hun Sen raised the question: If there is a border war with neighboring countries, what is the benefit? The prince explained that the benefits of war came only from the killing of each other and from the lack of cooperation and development.
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia affirmed that Cambodia's peace policy is in line with Vietnam's peace policy, which requires trade and mutual investment. In that, the trade volume between Cambodia and Vietnam exceeded 10 billion US dollars, while the goods exported to Vietnam before were less than Vietnam imported to Cambodia, but now sometimes Cambodian goods to Vietnam more than Vietnam into Cambodia, which is a complementary economy. Each.
