* The first point is to incite anger with the Royal Government, the authorities and the courts. The more angry the people, the more opportunities the opposition has. But in the end, those who are imprisoned are the ones who are crazy and live in the country. * The second point is to inspire people to hate the government. The opposition party has done everything to make the Royal Government of Cambodia hate and take advantage of politics.
Please be informed that Dr. Sonaro returned to the district after leaving for 11 years and before returning to the district, he always acted against the Royal Government from the sea.
Mr. Sonaro was appointed by His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, on May 11, 2023 as the Deputy Prime Minister.
Following the appointment, Dr. Sonaro announced his political affiliation with the CPP. He highlighted the great achievements and achievements of the Cambodian People's Party, which bring prosperity to the nation and improve the lives of the people. Other great achievements, such as organizing regional and international events such as the SEA Games, have brought national fame and pride for the nation and its people.
In the statement, Sonaro also attacked the weak leadership and politics of the opposition, led by traitor Sam Rainsy.
Recently, many key opposition activists have declared their secession and joined the CPP. What sectors of the Cambodian economy have created jobs for young people?
(Phnom Penh): Job creation involves many factors that need to be implemented together. Some countries are doing well and others are not doing well because of the pace of labor force entering the labor market too much and the economy is unable to create jobs on time. As a result, a country has a high unemployment rate.
Cambodia claims an estimated 10,000 unemployed people a year, while an additional 160,000 new workers enter the market each year. This means that Cambodia has a good economic policy on creating jobs on time.
What is Cambodia doing to create jobs for its people?
In general, when it comes to job creation, the most important things to do are investing in infrastructure, entrepreneurship incentives, attracting foreign investment, supporting small and medium enterprises, training, education and technical skills. In addition, more research on job creation is needed, especially as the government works closely with the private sector to tailor the workforce to the desired market.
On the other hand, a government must encourage businesses to invest in investments such as tax incentives or subsidies. At the same time, reducing barriers to doing business and supporting free competition mechanisms are further incentives for investment and business expansion on job creation as Cambodia's human resources grow.
In theory, human resources, especially youth, are the most important factor in contributing to all development in each country in the world. In particular, young people in Cambodia account for up to 70% of the total population of Cambodia. Creating a policy for Cambodian youth to be active in the process of economic development in Cambodia is a priority for the Cambodian government.
In terms of total job creation, the Cambodian economy currently creates about 10 million jobs across the country from agriculture, industry and services, with agriculture accounting for up to 50% of total employment. And foreign companies have also created about 1 million jobs in Cambodia. All this evidence is why the Cambodian government considers economic mechanisms to support investment as an important factor in creating jobs for Cambodians.
According to the Ministry of Economy and Finance, Cambodia's economic growth in 2023 will be 5.6%, up from last year's 5.2%. The figures are similarly projected by international research institutions, including the World Bank, the Asian Development Bank and the International Monetary Fund.
Through Cambodia's economic growth in the past, Cambodia has created jobs in three major sectors, such as the first: the garment sector, about 1 million people, the second: the tourism sector, creating about 800,000 direct jobs and contributing more than 11% of the national economy. Third, the construction sector creates at least 200,000 jobs, of which the construction and real estate sectors contribute about 10% annual economic growth.
In short, population growth or human resource growth is a source of economic growth because population growth will create more economic activity. Conversely, if an economy grows and people are unable to provide them with employment, it will lead to development problems because population growth reflects the growing demand for food, shelter, and government responsibility. Social security and so on.
As a result, the Cambodian government strives to implement policies to attract foreign investment and encourage local enterprises to create jobs. All over Cambodia.
Minister Thong Khon and Governor of Kampong Thom Province Open a Groundbreaking Ceremony for a 22-Kilometer Road in Tang Kork District
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group visited Kampong Thom Province and Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Governor of Kampong Thom Province, on June 24, 2023, opened the construction site of a 22-kilometer paved road. To the people in Taing Kork district, Kampong Thom province.
Mr. Hak Mong Huot, Governor of Taing Kork District, said that the project to build a 22-kilometer paved road starts from the base of the bridge in Neak Veang village, Sralao commune, Tam Kork district, Kampong Thom province, to Roth village, Batheay district, Kampong Cham province, which is an administrative project. Kampong Thom Province and built by a private company.
The governor of Taing Kork district confirmed that this road will facilitate the movement of people and the transportation of agricultural products to farmers more easily, especially in the rainy season, while in the rainy season, the old road is flooded. Flooding of the river made it impossible to travel.
Minister Thong Khon said that this is a new historical achievement in Tang Kork district, Kampong Thom province, especially for people who have to travel between National Road 6 to Veal Kram to the fields and for the villagers of Kork Trabek, which will There are solid paved roads to facilitate travel.
He said that these achievements come from the efforts of the Royal Government led by the People's Party, and our Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen always pays close attention to the well-being of the people.
The Minister also instructed the construction companies to properly implement their contracts and ensure the technical specifications, standards and quality of paved roads to ensure the quality of roads and long-term use.
He called on the people to take care of and protect this road for a long time when the road is completed and put into use, especially for drivers of heavy trucks, trucks do not overweight and drive safely.
The Minister expressed his hope that the rehabilitation of the paved road would be important and beneficial to the trade, transportation and business connection between the people of Taing Kork, Kampong Thom and Batheay districts of Kampong Cham province and contribute. To reduce poverty and improve people's living standards.
On that occasion, Mr. Nguon Rattanak said that the provincial administration built the road for the people is because the country is peaceful and developed by the Royal Government, which has the Cambodian People's Party as the winning party.
He said that this is a solution mechanism of the provincial administration for the people to implement in accordance with the policy of the Royal Government, especially the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4, which is trying to build human resources, develop water, electricity and infrastructure, roads, bridges, schools. And so on.
