Two companies continue to sign contracts to buy 43,770 tons of organic rice and cassava from communities in Preah Vihear province in 2023
(Preah Vihear): Amru Rice and the Cambodian Agricultural Community Corporation have renewed their contract with the agricultural community in Preah Vihear province to purchase 43,770 tons of rice and organic cassava in 2023, compared to 28,000 tons in 2022.
The signing ceremony of the contract for the production and supply of organic rice and cassava was held in the presence of Mr. Kim Rithy, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, with the participation of provincial leaders, directors of the Provincial Department of Agriculture, representatives of the two companies and many other farming communities.
Mr. Kim Rithy said that he was very pleased to attend the signing ceremony of the agricultural production contract under the contract for the production and supply of organic cassava rice between the agricultural community production group in Preah Vihear province with Amru Rice and the Cambodian Agricultural Community Corporation. Exports are among the leading exporters of rice and cassava in Cambodia.
The provincial governor also thanked the Department of Agriculture, Department of Commerce and the Preah Vihear Meanchey Agricultural Community Union for organizing the signing ceremony with the aim of demonstrating the market for organic rice and cassava of farmers in Preah Vihear province in 2023. This.
According to the plan, in 2023, the agricultural production contract for organic crops totaled 43,770 tons, including 18,760 tons of organic rice, 25,000 tons of organic cassava and 10 tons of organic peanuts. Compared to 2022, the farming community in Preah Vihear province supplied more than 28,000 tons to exporters.
Separately, Mr. Peng Trida, Director of Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, said that currently Preah Vihear Province has a total of 43 agricultural communities with a total of about 10,000 families, with the coordination of the Office of Agricultural Community Development and is registered. Recognized as a legitimate agricultural community by the Provincial Department of Agriculture.
According to the director of the department, Amru Rice will continue to sign agricultural production contracts with 21 farmers with more than 3,000 producers on a total of 16,000 tons of organic rice. The Cambodian Agricultural Community Corporation (CACC) will continue to sign agricultural production contracts with 10 farming communities with more than 1,400 producers on 25,000 tons of organic cassava.
