US to hold nuclear weapons meeting with China, Russia, France and UK in June
The United States in June convened a meeting with experts from China, Russia, France and the United Kingdom to discuss the issue of nuclear weapons, including the United States, the State Department said on Friday. There are also ways to mitigate strategic risks. This was released by the AFP news agency on Saturday, June 24, 2023.
White House National Security Council spokesman John Kirby said the talks were part of a regular dialogue. According to the US State Department, Washington hosted the meeting on June 13-14 in Cairo, Egypt, between the five nuclear-armed states and described it as a consultation under the context of NPT Non-Proliferation Treaty.
The NPT, which entered into force in 1970, aims to stop the proliferation of nuclear weapons capabilities and guarantee member states' right to develop nuclear power for peaceful purposes. The treaty allows the United States, China, Russia, France and Britain, permanent members of the UN Security Council, to retain their nuclear weapons.
According to a State Department spokesman, experts from the five countries' foreign and defense ministries also met in Dubai, United Arab Emirates, in February this year. As part of the dialogue under the framework of the NPT treaty, which is currently chaired by the United States.
