Mr. Lao Tip Seiha said that related to the construction of high-rise buildings from 5 floors up, there are 2,586 buildings, including 1,711 buildings in Phnom Penh, 690 buildings in Sihanoukville, 142 buildings in Banteay Meanchey and 142 buildings. Other 43 buildings.
Separately, there are 547 Borey housing projects and housing units. There are 40,917 apartment buildings.
According to Lao Tip Seiha, according to the 2008 census, Cambodia will have a population of more than 18 million, by 2030 there will be a need for more than 1.1 million new homes. For Phnom Penh, cities and towns need about 800,000 houses, on average there is a need for more than 50,000 houses per year.
