Dr. Prohm Vichet Akhra holds a meeting to review the publication of social textbooks that incorporate some of the basic provisions of the Constitution
(Phnom Penh): On Friday morning, June 23, 2023, Dr. Prohm Vichet Akhara, Chairman of the Working Group on the Work of the General Secretariat of the Constitutional Council, chaired a meeting to review the progress of the work of publishing social textbooks of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports. Amend some basic provisions of the Constitution into the curriculum at all three levels.
Ms. Tun Saim, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, said that the social curriculum textbook is planned to be published in accordance with the technical conditions of the Ministry for three consecutive years, grades 1, 4, 7 and 10 to be published in 2023.
In the future, the content of integrating some of the basic provisions of the Constitution into the social textbooks for grades 1, 4, 7 and 10 will be published by the end of 2023, if nothing changes.
Please be informed that under the Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) in 2019 between the Constitutional Council and the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, both sides officially announced the implementation of the Constitution into the curriculum on March 16, 2023. 40 articles of the Constitution are included in the curriculum at all three levels, from grade 1 to grade 12.
The MoU came after the Constitutional Council met with the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports to discuss in detail the procedures for incorporating key constitutional provisions into the education program on the afternoon of June 10, 2019.
Through this agreement, the Constitutional Council provides technical assistance in preparing the main content and lessons related to the basic provisions of the Constitution to be included in the three levels of curriculum, while the Ministry of Education prepares and publishes the basic content and contents. Related lessons.
To ensure the effectiveness of training related to the provisions of the Constitution, the Constitutional Council also runs training courses on the provisions of the Constitution to trainers across the country.
