Minister of Women's Affairs: The Royal Government considers women as the backbone of the economy, "Neary Rattanak" strategic plan is implementing the transformation of women into precious gems
(Phnom Penh): The Honorary Minister of Women's Affairs, Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi, on June 22, 2023, stated that the Royal Government has considered women as the backbone of the economy and society and the strategic plan "Neary Rattanak" is implementing the transformation. Becoming a woman is a precious gem and a potential resource in society.
This statement was made on the occasion of the opening of a workshop on the dissemination and formal operation of the Regional Project on Gender Mainstreaming in Climate Action: Strengthening the Adaptation and Resilience of Poor Women in Rural areas by improving livelihoods and access to clean water.
The workshop on the dissemination and formalization of the above regional project was held on June 22, 2023 with the support of the Special Fund Framework of Mekong-Lanchang Cooperation.
"In the framework of Cambodia's national policies and programs, the Royal Government considers women as the backbone of the national economy and society, and the Rattanak Neary Strategic Plan is implementing the transformation of women into gems," she said. "Valuable and a potential resource in society."
She said that within the framework of the National Policy and Strategic Plan in response to climate change in Cambodia 2014-2023 recognized that among the rural poor, most of whom are women, the most vulnerable to the impact of Climate change because they are so dependent on agriculture and natural resources.
Among them, women and other vulnerable groups are vulnerable to diseases due to resources and activities adapted to the effects of climate change, as well as their preparedness to deal with climate risks and catastrophic targets. . This is the additional confirmation of Mrs. Kittibandit Ung Kantha Phavi.
Responding to the commitment of the Royal Government of Cambodia and its alignment with the "Mekong-Lanchang" Regional Cooperation Framework as well as the Global Framework for Sustainable Development, Ministry of Women's Affairs Mekong-Lanchang Cooperation has designed and planned to implement this project.
This project will contribute to strengthening the capacity and resilience and resilience of poor women in rural areas through the introduction of rules and means to increase economic resilience and improve the quality of water and sanitation to improve the lives of women. And their families, in the Mekong-Lanchang region, sustainably, environmentally, and interconnected in the region.
The project will begin with a capacity development program tailored to the specific situation of each country in response to gender in climate action and strengthening the adaptation and resilience of rural women.
The capacity building program will be conducted by experts from China, Laos, Thailand and Cambodia, and for policy makers and programmers from Cambodia and Laos to identify pilot projects for their countries and communities. Body.
