ARDB Director General Continues to Disseminate the Royal Government's Credit Policy to Support Cashew Nuts and Other Agricultural Products
A meeting with cashew farmers in Kampong Chhnang province on the afternoon of June 22, 2023 was held in order to find out the various consequences that farmers are facing in farming and allow them to make suggestions to the bank. ARDB.
Dr. Kao Thach encourages you in case any farmer or producer wants to get a loan to expand the cultivation or expand the cashew production chain, you can apply for a loan from ARDB at a reasonable interest rate to buy quality fertilizer. Buy medicines that can be used without affecting their health and those who consume them last and for the construction of warehouses and cashew peeling machines.
Dr. advised the farmers to change their mindset from farming to raising rice to entrepreneurship, that is, to be able to supply the market in addition to the family supply. This encourages you to study more, especially in this modern context, which can be learned through YouTube to get new knowledge.
Dr. Kao Thach added that farmers should know how to monitor the price of agricultural products in the market and must know how to monitor the weather forecast, as well as know how to choose seasonal crops and markets.
At the same time, he also advised people to know how to change crops and change the soil so that the cultivation can get high yields and do not leave the land vacant, should find what kind of crops can be grown for a short time, but there is a market and demand and Change the habit of growing only one crop to raise more animals to earn more income.
Dr. Kao Thach encouraged the formation of agricultural communities or production units and to prepare planting plans, breeding plans, harvesting plans to be able to supply and sell in the market. This is very important, if you can do it, you will really get a lot of profit and have a family income.
At the same time, he called on all farmers and agricultural communities who have the right to vote to go to the polls on July 23.
