(Phnom Penh): In the morning of June 22, 2023, the Constitutional Council organized a presentation on "Examining the Constitution of the Law and Resolving Complaints After the General Election of the National Assembly" to students of the University of Cambodia. 60 people.
The event was held at the Secretariat of the Constitutional Council, chaired by Mr. Taing Ratana, Secretary General of the Constitutional Council, while the University of Cambodia was chaired by Ms. Prom Kalyan, Professor of Law, University of Cambodia.
According to Taing Ratana, for Cambodia, the 1947 Constitution has not yet established a Constitutional Council. He cited some points from the Constitution that the Constitutional Council was established by the 1993 Constitution of Cambodia, with the authority to ensure respect for the Constitution, interpret the Constitution and the laws passed by the National Assembly and the Senate.
At the same time, the Constitutional Council has the right to review and decide on disputes related to the National Assembly election and the Senate election.
The King, the Prime Minister, the President of the National Assembly, one-tenth of the members of the National Assembly, the President of the Senate or a quarter of the senators may submit a law passed by the National Assembly to the Constitutional Council for review before it is promulgated.
After a law is promulgated, the King, the President of the Senate, the President of the National Assembly, the Prime Minister, a quarter of the senators, one-tenth of the members of the National Assembly, or the court may ask the Constitutional Council to review the constitutionality of that law.
The people have the right to complain about the constitutionality of the law through the National Assembly or the President of the National Assembly or the members of the Senate or the President of the Senate as stated in the above paragraph.
