Ministry of Environment, provincial authorities, conservationists, citizens and nearly 300 students march to open and close the second zero trap campaign in Battambang and Pailin
(Battambang): Officials from the Ministry of Environment, Battambang and Pailin provincial authorities, conservation organizations, relevant departments and nearly 300 students this morning, June 22, 2023, marched to open and close the second zero trap campaign in the province. Battambang and Pailin Province.
The Opening Ceremony of the Second Zero Trap Campaign in Battambang Province was led by Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment and Chairman of the Zero Trap Campaign, as well as Battambang and Pailin provincial leaders at all levels.
The second phase of the Zero Trap Campaign will run for five months from March 3 to July 2023 and will be implemented in five provinces: Kampong Speu, Pursat, Koh Kong, Battambang, Pailin and Siem Reap.
The second Trap Zero Campaign in Battambang Province aims to reduce and prevent the number of traps in protected areas in Battambang Province as well as in other protected areas in Cambodia and to cultivate a greater love for wildlife in Among the public.
The second zero trap campaign, which came to Koh Kong province after the successful results of the first phase zero trap campaign, was held in Stung Treng, Preah Vihear, Kratie, Mondulkiri, Kampong Thom and Ratanakkiri provinces in 2022. Conservation partner organizations and relevant provincial administrations.
It should also be noted that the trap crisis is not unique to Cambodia. According to the WWF 2020 report, an estimated 12 million traps are present in the protected areas of several other countries in Southeast Asia, such as Laos, Vietnam, Malaysia and Indonesia. According to the same report, these traps are the main source of loss of some rare animals such as: big tigers, leopards, tigers, clouds, wild dogs, bears and so on.
