Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment and Chairman of the Zero Trap Campaign and partner organizations, announced that he would not hesitate to continue the Zero Trap campaign even after the second Zero Trap campaign ended. The announcement was made at a press conference at the Battambang Provincial Department of Environment on the afternoon of June 21, 2023.
Mr. Net Pheaktra stated: "The second Trap Zero campaign will end on June 22, 2023 in Battambang province, but the campaign to fight trapping and eating wild animals continues without hesitation. "
"In Cambodia, we are the first to address the trap crisis, while other countries in the world are eager to learn how we work between civil society organizations and state institutions to campaign for zero traps," he said. "After the completion of the second Zero Trap campaign, civil society working with the government will hold in-depth discussions for the third Zero Trap campaign."
Please be informed that the trapping zero campaign for almost 2 years has been very successful, with people being more aware as the number of traps in the forest and protected areas is decreasing. Both zero trapping campaigns have been carried out in 12 provinces in northwestern Cambodia, covering more than 70 percent of the more than 7.3 million hectares of protected areas managed by the Ministry of Environment.
