Meeting with Samdech Men Sam An, Chairman of the Lao State Inspection Authority, expressed high interest in the field of inspection in Cambodia
His Excellency Dr. Men Sam An welcomed the visit of the Lao delegation to Cambodia, emphasizing that the current visit is very important to exchange experiences in the field of inspection of the two countries and contribute to the promotion of relations and Cooperation between neighboring countries to be deeper, more comprehensive and more strategic.
Dr. Kham Phanh Phommathat expressed his appreciation for Cambodia's rapid progress under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, especially the success in hosting the recent ASEAN Summit and the SEA Games and Para Games. He thanked the Royal Government of Cambodia for always helping Laos at almost every stage, especially in the 19 land clearing phase.
Afterwards, he was interested and asked Samdech Kittisangkhab Dr. Men Sam An to share his experiences related to the field of inspection in Cambodia. In response, Samdech Kittisanghabandit also mentioned the roles and responsibilities of the Ministry, including:
* First: Inspection in all areas throughout the country, including: Inspection on administration, public financial management, management of state assets, monitoring the implementation of laws and regulations to contribute to the prevention of corruption and promote efficiency. Government work
* Second: Receive and resolve complaints and defamation complaints of citizens
* Third: Relations with the National Assembly and the Senate, including the dissemination of laws passed by the National Assembly to the people throughout the country to hold public forums to gather opinions and suggestions from the people to facilitate the resolution of the people's requests.
* Fourth: Training on inspection skills at all levels through the National Institute of Inspection.
