Historical project! More than $ 10 million worth of $ 10 million submarine and submarine power lines have been inaugurated to supply electricity to residents and tourist areas on the island.
(Preah Sihanouk): The project to build a medium voltage line buried under the sea and air on the islands in Koh Kong and Preah Sihanouk provinces, a national achievement of the nation, was launched on June 21, 2023 to supply electricity to Residents and hotels, guesthouses, commercial tourist sites on the entire Koh Rong to get electricity from the national grid at an affordable price like other areas throughout Cambodia.
The inauguration ceremony took place in Koh Rong City on the morning of June 21, 2023, presided over by Mr. Keo Rattanak, Minister Delegate to the Director General of Electricity of Cambodia and Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of the Board of Governors. Sihanoukville and with the participation of representatives of the Royal Group of Duke Kith Meng and the people.
The project to build a medium-voltage network buried under the seabed and the air over the islands was made on the recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, for the development of the islands in the waters of Cambodia, especially Koh Rong. Accept large-scale investments such as the construction of resorts and hotels, as well as improve the livelihoods and quality of life of many fishing families there.
1- Medium voltage power network in Kirisakor district, Koh Kong province and Koh Rong city, Preah Sihanouk province, as well as the network buried under the sea from the mainland from Poy Peam Kay through Koh Mneas, Koh Ta Taem to Koh Rong.
Mr. Keo Rattanak thanked the Royal Government for its support on this priority project and thanked the local authorities and the people for their understanding and cooperation during the construction. Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) will make full use of the nation's new infrastructure to benefit the national economy and its people.
He continued, "Today is the inauguration of the historic achievement of the nation to supply electricity to the homes of about 700 families and hotels, guesthouses, tourist attractions on Koh Rong to use electricity from the network. "Affordable nation like other regions throughout Cambodia."
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun said that now the stability of electricity supply in Sihanoukville has improved with reasonable electricity prices.
He hopes that the implementation of this project will be successful to expand the power supply capacity, improve the quality of electricity and, in particular, reduce the interruption of electricity supply to the maximum, ensure better supply stability, which responds to the significant growth. Rapid economic activity, industry, tourism and continuous consumption of people in Koh Rong area, Koh Rong city, Sihanoukville province.
"The Sihanoukville Provincial Administration will continue to fully support all the infrastructure development projects of the power grid of EDC that are being implemented and the projects being implemented in the geography of Sihanoukville Province," he said.
In addition, Royal Group Koh Rong Development Company has built a 35 kV power line with a total length of 22 km, in addition to the power line of EDC, which is more than 20 km long, 0.4 kV power line length. A total of 20.8 km and 23 35 / 0.4kV transformers installed at a total cost of 2 million US dollars.
Royal Group plans to build more solar power plants as renewable energy and additional sources of assistance. In addition, the Royal Group has built infrastructure such as concrete roads across the entire island and is building an airport. Director General: As of now, the public administration operating in Cambodia is worth $ 1.04 billion
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sok Dara, Director General of the Public Administration Regulation, on June 21, 2023, stated that as of now, the amount of public administration operating in Cambodia is about 1.04 million. Billion US dollars.
This statement was made on the occasion of Mr. Sok Dara's participation in the signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between the Regulatory Authority of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport (MPWT) and CAMED Institute on "Cooperation on Awareness raising and exchange of technical assistance within the framework of the administrative sector in Cambodia.
Mr. Sok Dara stated, "For the civil service operating in Cambodia so far, 523 cases have been registered with the municipality of about 1.04 billion dollars, but next month this number will "Increasing."
In addition, the Director General of the Regulatory Authority said that we can expect that in the middle of next month or at the end of next month, this figure will be the official figure, the amount of collateral working in Cambodia will increase to 1.13 billion dollars. But this is a temporary perspective.
Mr. Sok Dara pointed out that for the purpose of the regulatory authority, the amount of capital operating in Cambodia will increase by 1.5 billion US dollars, about 5% of GDP.
Please be informed that the signing of this Memorandum of Understanding in order to enhance and regulate the understanding of the field of public administration and related regulations, as well as to provide support and exchange of mutual technical assistance to contribute to the development process. Of the administrative sector in Cambodia.
The Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) signing ceremony was attended by senior experts of the NPC. And professors from CAMED Institute, as well as the participation of senior representatives of regulators and subordinate units, the Non-Banking Financial Services Authority (NAOF) and other stakeholders.
