(Battambang): A drug criminal was cracked down by the Battambang Provincial Gendarmerie together with more than 30 kilograms of ice drugs on June 19, 2023 and was made public before being sent to school. First, the province on June 21, 2023.
Speaking to Fresh News, General Hem Vuthy, Commander of the Battambang Provincial Gendarmerie, confirmed that after a long period of professional investigation into drug trafficking, and in accordance with the direct orders of General Sao Sokha, Commander-in-Chief. The Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the Commander of the National Gendarmerie, with the coordination of Mr. Keo Socheat, Prosecutor of the Battambang Provincial Prosecutor's Office.
He claimed that during the operation, he ordered Lieutenant Colonel Rong Pok, Deputy Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie in charge of crime prevention investigation, to lead a joint professional force to arrest one suspect while trafficking in crime. On June 19, 2023, in Battambang City, 31 kilograms of ice drugs were confiscated on the streets.
After questioning, the suspect confessed that his mastermind's drugs were hidden in a rented room in Chamkar Russey village, Sangkat Prek Preah Sdach, Battambang city, Battambang province.
After receiving the confessions from the suspects, General Hem Vuthy, Commander of the Battambang Provincial Gendarmerie, and Mr. Tuth Vinith, Representative of Mr. Keo Socheat, Prosecutor of the Battambang Provincial Prosecutor's Office, Deputy Commanders of the relevant specialized forces conducted a forensic examination. The drugs in front of the suspects and the media observed that these white powders were indeed drugs.
Currently, according to the confessions of the suspects and all the exhibits, the Anti-Drug Bureau has prepared a case to be sent to court on the afternoon of June 21, 2023 to proceed with the procedure.
