Minister Pan Sosak, Representing the Royal Government, Leads a Delegation to a Meeting to Defend the Draft Law on Rules of Origin
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of June 21, 2023, at the Senate, Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, representing the Royal Government, led a delegation from the Ministry of Commerce and the Ministry of Economy and Finance to attend a meeting to discuss and defend the draft law. On the rules of origin of goods in the 10th plenary session of the 10th Senate, 4th legislature.
The plenary session was chaired by Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate, and was attended by the Supreme Members of the Senate.
To begin with, Mr. Kong Sarach, Chairman of the Ninth Committee of the Senate, reported to the 10th Plenary Session of the 4th Senate on the detailed study and review process of the 9th Commission on the Draft Law on the Rules of Origin. The resulting goods check that the draft law is prepared in accordance with the form and law and in accordance with the provisions of the Constitution, laws and relevant legal norms.
