(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and the Founder of Win-Win Politics, reaffirmed that the win-win policy, which is the policy of extinguishing the flames of war in Cambodia, was implemented on February 11, 1996 and ended. Completely on December 29, 1998. Such assertions are intended to dispel misconceptions and misrepresentations about the dates of important historical events of the Cambodian political and social process.
This result came after Mr. Keo Pong met with Samdech Hun Sen on February 7, 1996.
In addition to confirming the start date of the win-win policy, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also confirmed the closing date of the win-win policy. The closing day of the win-win policy is December 29, 1998, the day when the Khmer Rouge locomotive, including: Former Head of State Khieu Samphan, Former Speaker of the National Assembly Nuon Chea, Ieng Sary, Chan Youran, Chuon Choeun, and his family met with Samdech Techo Hun Sen at home in Takhmao city, Kandal province.
Regarding the operators leading to a successful win-win political implementation, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also reminded of the merits of Mr. Yi Chhean, Commander of the Khmer Rouge's 415th Brigade in Pailin and Mr. Sokpheap, Commander of the 450th Khmer Rouge Brigade in Malai. Samdech Techo considered the secession of the Royal Government by Mr. Yi Chhean and Mr. Sok Pheap as an important current to promote the integration of the Khmer Rouge forces.
In addition to the three policies and the five strategies, win-win politics depends on seven other success factors, including:
1. Leadership: The mission that brings peace to the nation and the people is not a simple thing and can not be achieved without the right leader. Cambodia is fortunate to have a talented leader, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the founder of peace.
2. The role of the central administration: The central administration is very important in leading the Cambodian navy, from the King, the legislature and the executive are united as one to work together for victory.
3. Operators: Good leaders are important. At the same time, operators such as the masses and the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, which are the core force in the implementation of win-win politics, are very important.
4: Building trust: Building trust from the people to the leadership is an indispensable mechanism, starting from small things to big events, to keep the people.
5: Political, economic and trade ideological factors: This is an important factor to push closer to victory in the context of changing the economic flow of Cambodia as a major context in history, turning to a free market economy that has reached all. Nation layer.
6: Foreign factors: Not only within the nation, the international and regional community also plays an important role. Especially in the circumstances where the international community has changed its position of supporting the government of Democratic Kampuchea to recognize the government led by Samdech Techo.
7: Divide the Khmer Rouge regime: The first pillar of the Divide strategy was Divide, which means that the divisions that separated the core forces of the Khmer Rouge into separate groups, such as Ta Mok standing at Anlong Veng and Nuon Chea standing at Samlot. Only then did the influence of the Khmer Rouge weaken and the Royal Government was able to achieve complete victory for the entire nation.
