Senior Minister Ly Thuch: Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh Historical Site in Koh Kong Province Completed Mine Clearance Supported by "Cambodia Mine Action Fund 2025"
As a result of the demining work, the entire Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh historical site in Chroy Pros commune, Koh Kong and Kirisakor districts has been cleared of 38 mines and 183 unexploded ordnance.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Ly Thuch expressed his gratitude to Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh and all Cambodian fighters who joined Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister in liberating the country and the Cambodian people from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot and Seek complete peace for the whole of Cambodia through Samdech Techo's win-win policy.
As of June 2023, 21,188,620 square meters of landmines and explosive remnants of war in Koh Kong province had been cleared, and 2,476 anti-personnel mines were found and destroyed, the senior minister said. There were 14 anti-tank mines, 14,163 explosive remnants of war, and a total of 998 mine casualties, including 790 mines.
The Senior Minister stated that these achievements in Koh Kong Province came from the high attention of the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Prime Minister in solving the problem of mines and national remnants of the war in Cambodia. Without Samdech Techo, the number of mine and landmine casualties in Koh Kong province as well as across the country will continue to rise and socio-economic rehabilitation will be challenging.
