Kampong Chhnang Province Recognized as End-of-Field Discharge (ODF) Province
(Kampong Chhnang): Kampong Chhnang province was officially recognized as the province that ended the defecation (ODF) this morning, June 20, 2023. The ceremony was presided over by Mr. Sou Kong, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Rural Development, and was attended by a large number of government officials, residents and students at the Deum Po Park Forum.
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Xu Kong said that by improving the provision of clean water and sanitation services, the people of Kampong Chhnang province have changed their habits from drinking unsafe water to drinking safe water and defecation. Use the toilet properly and have a civilized lifestyle.
He added that the Ministry of Rural Development has been actively involved in improving the economic, social and cultural status of rural people so that they can achieve a harmonious and civilized development by setting out key strategies. Such as the connection of physical infrastructure, which is a prerequisite for promoting socio-economic interaction between rural and urban areas.
Activating rural economic activities, including agriculture and other occupations in rural communities, in order to help solve the problems of daily life, increase the income of each family, improve the social and cultural status, which is the foundation of rural economic development; Contribute to improving living conditions, reducing the gap in the provision of basic services between cities, towns and rural areas, the gap between the affluent families.
Mr. Su Kong also praised the leadership of Kampong Chhnang province that has achieved in the past in all areas, especially the improvement of living conditions through the improvement of water and sanitation services.
In this ceremony, Mr. Sun Sovannarith, Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province, stated that currently people use a total of 19,719 pump wells, 10,644 drainage wells, 180 community ponds, 1 rainwater filter, 033 basins, 17 community water distribution systems, 12 water treatment stations.
During the ceremony, certificates of appreciation were presented to the provincial governors, deputy governors, provincial departments and district governors of all districts, and there was also a parade to celebrate Kampong Chhnang province, where there is no more defecation in the streets. In the four districts of Kampong Chhnang, which has a large crowd of people to celebrate.
