Ministry of Labor signs memorandum of understanding with Singapore's SCIA International School to implement vocational training policy for 1.5 million young people
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has signed a Memorandum of Understanding with the Cambodia-Singapore International School (SCIA) of Singapore to prepare for the implementation of the Royal Government's policy on vocational training for 1.5 million young people. Will be implemented in August 2023.
On that occasion, Minister Ith Sam Heng said that the Royal Government of Cambodia has provided guidelines to the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training to plan vocational training for young people in poor and vulnerable families, a total of 1.5 million people. The Royal Government is responsible for tuition fees and provides monthly stipends.
The Minister continued that, having received the policy from the head of the Royal Government, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training needs additional partners to be ready to cooperate in providing training to the 1.5 million young people. The signing of the MoU with SCIA International School is also an important contribution to the professional development of young people in Cambodia.
Tan Wipin, Director of SCIA, said that his school already has a training program from Singapore, without having to rewrite the training program, just to provide training to trainees, including trainers from Singapore.
The principal of SCIA stated that the goal of cooperation with the Ministry of Labor as well as the Royal Government of Cambodia is to help train the professional skills of staff, workers, youth to increase the capacity to meet the needs of the labor market in Cambodia.
